x/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.md","content":"# Site Plan Facts\n\n# Facts — Valley View Townhomes (SP-2025-0126C)\n**3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704**\n\n---\n\n## Discrepancies\n\n- **Easement (Greenbelt Access & Use, Instrument 2010070731):** A perpetual, no-build greenbelt easement covering 0.31 acres (13,524 sq ft) of the NE interior of Lot 1 is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer. County clerk research confirms it is real, recorded, and perpetual. Must be depicted before approval.\n- **Easement (City of Austin Drainage, Instrument 2011021137):** A perpetual City of Austin drainage easement covering 0.130 acres (5,670 sq ft) of the NE corner of Lot 1 is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer. County clerk research confirms it is real, recorded, and perpetual. Must be depicted before approval.\n- **Combined NE no-build zone (~0.44 ac):** Together, the two easements above encumber approximately 0.44 acres (~19%) of the NE portion of the 2.16-acre site. Neither is shown on submitted plans. Proposed building layout must be evaluated against both easement footprints.\n- **Acreage:** Site plan states 2.16 ac; 2019 deed/survey states 2.158 ac; TCAD states 2.1970 ac; COA GIS parcel measures 2.111 ac (91,944 sq ft). If the controlling acreage is 2.111 ac (GIS), the IC calculation based on 2.16 ac should be rechecked.\n- **10' Wastewater Easement (Vol 73/76, C8S-75-160):** COA GIS shows this plat-dedicated easement running across the parcel. Not confirmed on the submitted site plan. Site plan notes \"must verify no conflicts.\"\n- **25' Drainage Easement and 7.5' PUE (Vol 64/13, C8-71-079):** GIS shows these easements (from the Cortez Heights plat) running across the NE boundary of Lot 1. Not verified on site plan. Precise location relative to proposed improvements must be confirmed.\n- **FIRM Panel Number:** Site plan cites Panel #48453C0585H (effective September 26, 2008). FloodPro returns null for both FIRM_PANEL and EFFECTIVE_DATE. Must be independently verified on FEMA Flood Map Service Center.\n- **Demolition permit number:** Site plan cites \"2022-101266 BP\" as the demolition permit. Amanda shows 2022-101266 as a Plumbing Permit (Repair); the actual demolition building permit is 2022-096813 BP (Final). Actual demolition is confirmed complete.\n\n---\n\n## Property\n\n- **Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- **Parcel ID (GeoID):** 0406100252\n- **Legal Description:** Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas\n- **Subdivision:** Mecey Subdivision (File No. C8S-75-100)\n- **Plat Instrument:** Vol 73 / Pg 76 (Instrument 418356), filed 1975-12-11\n- **County:** Travis\n- **Site Area (site plan):** 2.16 acres\n- **Site Area (2019 deed/survey):** 2.158 acres\n- **Site Area (TCAD):** 2.1970 acres (95,701 sq ft)\n- **Site Area (COA GIS parcel):** 2.111 acres (91,944 sq ft)\n- **Limits of Construction:** 2.26 acres\n- **Survey of Record (likely):** 2018 CDS Survey, Project No. 18-03-0225:021\n- **Current Land Use:** Vacant land (formerly assisted living / nursing care facility; demolished June 2022)\n\n## Ownership\n\n- **Owner:** WM 41 Austin RE, LLC\n- **Owner Mailing Address:** 500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010, Austin, TX 78701\n- **Acquisition Deed:** Instrument 2019197883 — Special Warranty Deed from SHG Resources LP to WM 41 Austin RE LLC (2019-12-11). Property conveyed subject to all easements of record.\n- **Civil Engineering Firm:** Bleyl Engineering\n- **Architecture Firm:** Danze & Davis Architects, Inc.\n- **Landscape Architecture Firm:** Blu Fish Collaborative, Inc.\n\n## Zoning & Land Use\n\n- **Zoning:** MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n- **Controlling Ordinance:** 20120112-092 (Zoning Case C14-2011-0093)\n- **Secondary Ordinance:** 19990225-070b\n- **Neighborhood Plan:** South Lamar NPA — SUSPENDED. No active neighborhood plan applies.\n- **Regulating Plan:** None\n- **Historic District / Landmark:** None\n- **Compatibility Standards:** LDC Subchapter F triggered by adjacent SF-3 parcel (0406100210). Within 25 ft of the SF-3 lot line: maximum 2 stories / 30 ft height. Step-up schedule applies for structures beyond 25 ft. Screening/buffer requirements between MF and SF-3 uses apply.\n- **Nonconforming Signs Area:** Yes (§25-10-152) — all signage must comply with nonconforming signs area standards\n- **Parkland Deficient Area:** Yes (2 polygon features intersect parcel) — parkland dedication fee-in-lieu will apply per unit; confirm fee with Parks Department\n- **Residential Design Standards (Subchapter F):** Active overlay\n\n## Flood\n\n- **FEMA Flood Zone:** Zone X (outside 100-year and 500-year floodplain)\n- **COA Flood Zone:** Zone X\n- **FIRM Panel (site plan claim):** 48453C0585H, effective September 26, 2008 — ⚠️ unverifiable in FloodPro; verify on FEMA portal\n- **FIRM Community:** 480624\n- **Elevation Certificate:** None on file\n- **LOMAs on file:** 0\n- **LOMRs on file:** 0\n- **Floodplain intersection:** None (fema-floodplain layer: empty; fully-developed-floodplain layer: empty)\n\n## Watershed & Environmental\n\n- **Watershed:** West Bouldin Creek (WBO) — Watershed ID 109\n- **Receiving Waters:** Lady Bird Lake → Colorado River below Longhorn Dam\n- **Watershed Class:** Urban\n- **Development Zone:** Desired Development Zone\n- **Impervious Cover Cap:** 65% (LDC §25-8-341)\n- **Proposed Impervious Cover:** ~59.5–60% (under cap — calculated against 2.16 ac site area; see acreage discrepancy)\n- **Existing Impervious Cover:** ~65%\n- **RSMP Participation:** No\n- **Smart Growth Zone:** Yes\n- **Drinking Water Protection Zone:** No\n- **Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone:** No\n- **Edwards Aquifer Contributing Zone:** No\n- **Creek Buffers:** None intersecting parcel\n- **Salamander Habitat:** No\n- **Underground Storage Tanks:** None registered\n- **Wildland Urban Interface (2024):** No\n\n## Easements & Encumbrances\n\n### ⛔ Critical — Not Depicted on Site Plan, Not in COA GIS\n\n**Easement 1 — Greenbelt Access & Use Easement**\n- **Instrument:** 2010070731 (filed 2010-05-18; executed 2010-03-12)\n- **Grantor:** SHG Resources LP | **Grantee:** Dupont / Barnett / Roberts (assignable to HOA)\n- **Area:** 0.31 acres (13,524 sq ft), NE interior of Lot 1\n- **Duration:** PERPETUAL\n- **Restrictions:** No-build zone. Exclusive pedestrian/greenbelt open space for adjacent condo project. No structures or improvements permitted in easement area.\n- **Status on Site Plan:** Not depicted — must be added before approval\n- **Status in COA GIS:** Not present in easement-polygons layer\n\n**Easement 2 — City of Austin Drainage Easement**\n- **Instrument:** 2011021137 (filed 2011-02-11; executed 2010-03-15)\n- **Grantor:** SHG Resources LP | **Grantee:** City of Austin (Watershed Protection)\n- **Area:** 0.130 acres (5,670 sq ft), NE corner of Lot 1\n- **Duration:** PERPETUAL\n- **Restrictions:** City holds unlimited rights to construct, operate, maintain, replace, upgrade, and repair a drainage channel. No development may occur without City of Austin consent. Related project: Clawson MultiFamily, SP-2010-0014C.SH.\n- **Status on Site Plan:** Not depicted — must be added before approval; requires Watershed Protection coordination\n- **Status in COA GIS:** Not present in easement-polygons layer\n\n### ⚠️ GIS-Confirmed — Not Verified on Site Plan\n\n**Easement 3 — 10' Wastewater Easement**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 73/76, Case C8S-75-160 (Mecey Subdivision plat)\n- **Width:** 10 ft\n- **Status:** Plat-dedicated. In COA GIS. Not confirmed depicted on site plan. Site plan notes \"must verify no conflicts.\"\n\n**Easement 4 — 25' Drainage Easement (from Cortez Heights plat)**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 64/13, Case C8-71-079\n- **Width:** 25 ft\n- **Status:** DEDICATED. Runs across NE boundary of Lot 1. Not verified on site plan.\n\n**Easement 5 — 7.5' Public Utility Easement (from Cortez Heights plat)**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 64/13, Case C8-71-079\n- **Width:** 7.5 ft\n- **Status:** DEDICATED. Runs across NE boundary of Lot 1. Not verified on site plan.\n\n**Easement 6 — 10' Drainage Easement (from Trico Subd plat)**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 69/14, Case C8S-74-075\n- **Width:** 10 ft\n- **Status:** DEDICATED. Runs across NE boundary of Lot 1. Not verified on site plan.\n\n### Plat-Dedicated (Confirm on Survey)\n\n**Easement 7 & 8 — 5' Electric Easements (×2)**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 73/76, Case C8S-75-160\n- **Width:** 5 ft each\n- **Status:** DEDICATED\n\n**Easement 9 — 7.5' Public Utility Easement**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 73/76, Case C8S-75-160\n- **Width:** 7.5 ft\n- **Status:** DEDICATED\n\n### Recorded Document Provisions\n\n**Instrument 2010070731 — Greenbelt Access & Use Easement:**\n- Entire 0.31-acre NE interior area is a strict no-build zone; no structures, fences, pavement, or permanent improvements permitted\n- Easement is exclusive to the adjacent condo project beneficiaries and is freely assignable to the project's HOA\n- Runs with the land; binds all successors and assigns of the grantor\n- No time limit; perpetual duration\n- Current property owner (WM 41) took title subject to this easement per the 2019 acquisition deed\n\n**Instrument 2011021137 — City of Austin Drainage Easement:**\n- City of Austin (Watershed Protection Department) holds unlimited, irrevocable right of access to the 0.130-acre NE corner area\n- City may construct, reconstruct, operate, inspect, maintain, repair, replace, and upgrade a drainage channel within the easement\n- Owner may not obstruct City access; any improvements within or adjacent to the easement require City coordination\n- Perpetual; binds all successors and assigns\n\n**Deed Restrictions / Covenants:** None found. County clerk search of 10 strategies found no height limits, use restrictions, parking ratios, setback covenants, or design review obligations recorded against Lot 1.\n\n## Jurisdiction\n\n- **Jurisdiction:** City of Austin — Full Purpose (Code 210)\n- **County:** Travis\n- **Council District:** 5\n- **School District:** Austin ISD (AISD)\n\n## Roadway Classification\n\n**Valley View Road**\n- **ASMP Street Level:** 1 — Local Street\n- **AMTP Classification:** Not in AMTP (local street — not classified as highway, arterial, expressway, or freeway)\n- **Project Type:** Local Mobility\n- **Segment Limits:** Manchaca Rd to End\n- **Existing Lane Count:** Not on file\n- **Future Cross-Section:** 2U-OP (2 undivided lanes, open pavement)\n- **Required ROW:** 58 or 64 ft (determination required — this is commercial redevelopment; single-family exception does not apply)\n- **Required Improvement:** Complete missing sidewalks within existing ROW\n- **Bicycle Facility:** None (existing and recommended)\n- **ROW Dedication Note:** ASMP remarks state ROW dedication may be required from new development and commercial redevelopment through the land development process. Reviewer must determine applicable standard (58 or 64 ft).\n\n## Adjacent Properties\n\n- **SF-3 parcel (0406100210):** Immediate neighbor — triggers LDC Subchapter F compatibility standards. This is the critical adjacency: multi-family development within 25 ft of this SF-3 lot line is subject to 2-story / 30-ft height cap and step-up schedule.\n- **GO parcel (0406100168):** General Office — adjacent\n- **MF-3 parcel (0406100170):** Multi-Family Medium-High Density — adjacent\n- **MF-3-CO parcel (0404090425):** Multi-Family Medium-High Density with Conditional Overlay — adjacent\n- **MF-2-CO parcel (0406101601):** Multi-Family Medium Density with Conditional Overlay — adjacent\n\nThe surrounding context is predominantly multi-family and office, consistent with infill development. The single SF-3 parcel is the critical zoning transition requiring Subchapter F compliance.\n\n## Site Plan Details\n\n- **Site Plan Number:** SP-2025-0126C\n- **Submittal Date:** May 20, 2025\n- **Status:** Awaiting Update (first-round comment response pending)\n- **Fiscal Surety Records:** Filed 2025-09-21 (one for SP-2025-0126C, one for Erosion Controls) — both \"New\" status; suggests progression toward pre-construction conditions\n- **Active Tree Permit:** Commercial Tree Permit pending (filed 2025-08-14)\n\n## Development Specifications\n\n- **Project Name:** Valley View Townhomes\n- **Proposed Use:** 39 multi-family townhome units, 8 buildings\n- **Occupancy Classification:** R3\n- **Construction Type:** Type V-B\n- **Sprinkler System:** NFPA 13D\n- **Proposed Impervious Cover:** ~59.5–60% (reduction from existing ~65%)\n- **Impervious Cover Cap:** 65% (Urban watershed)\n\n## Stormwater\n\n- **Stormwater Feature:** Stacked biofiltration / detention pond (privately maintained)\n- **Watershed:** West Bouldin Creek — Urban, Desired Development Zone\n- **IC Cap:** 65% | Proposed IC: ~59.5–60%\n\n## Fire & Safety\n\n- **Private Hydrants:** 1\n- **Fire Flow Demand:** 3,000 GPM @ 20 psi (reduced to 1,500 GPM with NFPA 13D sprinkler system)\n- **Building Fire Area:** 13,344 sq ft\n- **Wildland Urban Interface:** No\n\n## Development History\n\n- **DA-2021-1307:** Development Assistance, Site Plan Determination/Exemption — Agreed (2021-08-31)\n- **2022-096813 BP:** Building Permit — Demolition — Final (2022-06-28). Existing assisted living building demolished June 2022. Lot currently vacant.\n- **SP-97-0145CS:** Prior site plan — Southwood Nursing Care Center Addition — Approved 1997, Closed 1999 (confirmed prior assisted living use)\n\n","numLines":230,"startLine":1,"totalLines":230}}}
