Block 5: notes — Indicates the job number associated with the survey document.\n\nJOB NUMBER: 20240953\n\n## Block 8: notes — Certification statement and signature of the Registered Professional Land Surveyor who performed the survey.\n\nTHIS SURVEY WAS PERFORMED WITHOUT THE BENEFIT OF A CURRENT\nTITLE COMMITMENT AND THERE MAY BE EASEMENTS, BUILDING LINES,\nCONDITIONS, OR RESTRICTIONS OF RECORD NOT SHOWN OR NOTED\nHEREON.\nDATE OF SURVEY: DECEMBER 27, 2024\nRYAN T. LENZ\nREGISTERED PROFESSIONAL LAND SURVEYOR NO. 7624\nSINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.\nTBPELS FIRM No. 10089000\n4150 FREIDRICH LANE, SUITE A-1\nAUSTIN, TEXAS 78744\n(512) 443-1174\n\n## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and abbreviations used in the site plan drawing. It defines various symbols for pins, monuments, lines, and utility features.\n\nLEGEND\n\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND UNLESS NOTED\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN SET W/CAP MARKED S.L.S. RPLS 518\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED CARTER BURGESS\n- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED LIND & ASSOC.\n- MAG NAIL SET\n- 3/4\" BRASS MONUMENT FOUND\n- NAIL FOUND\n- 60D NAIL FOUND\n- CHAIN LINK FENCE\n- IRON PIPE FOUND\n- MAG NAIL FOUND\n- \"X\" FOUND IN CONCRETE\n- WATER METER\n- WATER VALVE\n- SPRINKLE FOUND\n- WOOD FENCE\n- UTILITY POLE\n- WIRE FENCE\n- LIGHT POLE\n- CRETE FENCE\n- PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT\n- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n- WATER, WASTEWATER EASEMENT\n- P.U.E. D.U.E. DRAINAGE EASEMENT\n- W.W.L.E. WASTEWATER LINE\n- W.L. WATER LINE\n- O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\n- T.L. TOWN LOT\n- C.I. CURB INLET\n- (BRG-DIST) RECORD CALL ADJOINER\n- - DECIDUOUS TREE (VARIOUS TYPES)\n- - CLEAN-OUT\n- - FIRE HYDRANT\n- - AIR CONDITIONER\n- - SIGN POST\n- - TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n- O.P.R.T.C.TX. OFFICIAL PUBLIC RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- R.P.R.T.C.TX. REAL PROPERTY RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- P.R.T.C.TX. PLAT RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- D.R.T.C.TX. DEED RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n- T. TRAFFIC SIGN\n- G. GAS MARKER SIGN\n- T. APPARENT GAS TEST STATION\n\n## Block 12: table — A table listing trees found on the property, providing an ID number, size (caliper in inches), and type (species) for each tree.\n\nTREE TABLE\n| NO # | SIZ. | TYPE |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4000 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4001 | 15\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4002 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4003 | 12\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4004 | 22\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4006 | 13\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4007 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4008 | 13\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4009 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4010 | 18\" | CHINA BERRY |\n| 4011 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4012 | 12\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4013 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4014 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4015 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4016 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4017 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4019 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4022 | 24\" | PECAN |\n| 4023 | 24\" | M |\n| 4024 | 8\" | ELM |\n| 4025 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4026 | 28\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4027 | 15\" | M |\n| 4028 | 36\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4030 | 14\" | PECAN |\n| 4031 | 16\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4032 | 18\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4033 | 11\" | ELM |\n| 4034 | 20\" | CHINA BERRY |\n| 4035 | 16\" | ELM |\n| 4036 | 14\" | PECAN |\n| 4037 | 11\" | ASH |\n| 4038 | 20\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4040 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n| 4041 | 13\" | ELM |\n| 4042 | 34\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4043 | 15\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4044 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4045 | 20\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4046 | 17\" | LIVE OAK |\n| 4047 | 16\" | PINE |\n\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
