{"level":30,"time":1778246278065,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: 1) The location and routing of the overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan - trace their path across the site; 2) The location of all proposed trees (shown as circles and symbols per the key notes - SY for street yard trees, PL for parking lot trees, P for buffer trees, M for mitigation trees); 3) The proximity of trees to the overhead electric lines - which trees appear to be within potential clearance zones (roughly 15-50 feet of the overhead conductors, depending on tree type and electric facility voltage); 4) Any tree symbols or labels near the OHE lines, including the species indicated by the symbols in the key. Please describe the spatial relationship between the overhead electric infrastructure and the proposed plantings.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
