{"level":30,"time":1778246278929,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WRr9wnhxZQM9moH618maen","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93610fe3-4c7d-4104-b697-f9712668890f","uuid":"3d1559b8-aecc-4d72-9c27-e882f6ec3891","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246278931,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7oBfF3YTsqV4iJa64z6gt","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n     2→\n     3→This page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n    11→- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n    12→- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n    13→- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n    14→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n    15→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n    16→- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    19→- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n    20→- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n    21→- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n    22→- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n    23→- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n    28→\n    29→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93610fe3-4c7d-4104-b697-f9712668890f","uuid":"1f8f14e4-22a9-4c49-83c9-6d80459697a5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n\nThis page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n\n**Key values**:\n- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246278933,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RAiGoaBzwRPHpKvtaHydAp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n     2→\n     3→Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n    11→*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n    12→*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n    13→*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n    14→*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n    15→*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n    16→*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n    17→*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n    18→*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n    19→*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n    20→*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    25→    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    28→    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    31→    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    34→    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    37→    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    40→    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    43→    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    46→    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    49→    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    52→    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    55→    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n    56→\n    57→*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    58→    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93610fe3-4c7d-4104-b697-f9712668890f","uuid":"e11b301b-85d6-4316-9596-615f0fcdd846","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n\nDetailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n\n*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n\n*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n\n*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n\n*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n\n*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n\n*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n\n*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246279837,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Identify all overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this landscape plan. For each overhead electric line or facility, please describe:\n1. The location on the site (which portion of the property)\n2. The routing direction/orientation (north-south, east-west, diagonal)\n3. The proximity to any proposed buildings, parking areas, trees, or other site features\n4. Whether the lines appear to cross over buildings or site features\n5. Any visible clearance dimensions or annotations related to overhead electric lines\n6. The condition of overhead poles or structures (if visible)\n\nAlso describe the overall site layout showing where the 8 buildings are located and where the detention pond is located to help establish the spatial context for the overhead lines.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\"), here are the findings regarding overhead electric (OHE) lines and the overall site layout.\n\n### Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines Analysis\n\nI have scanned the entire document for linetypes or annotations indicating overhead electric lines. Only one such line is identified on this specific sheet.\n\n**Identified Line: \"- OHE -\"**\n\n1.  **Location on the site:** There is a single line designated by the text \"- OHE -\" embedded within the line itself. It runs along the extreme southern boundary of the property line.\n2.  **Routing direction/orientation:** The line runs horizontally across the page, in an East-West orientation, parallel to the southern limit of construction (marked \"- LOC -\").\n3.  **Proximity to site features:**\n    *   It runs outside the footprint of any proposed buildings or central parking areas.\n    *   It runs parallel to and just south of a proposed sidewalk/path running along the southern edge of the site.\n    *   It passes through or immediately adjacent to several large circular outlines representing tree canopies (both existing and proposed, such as the one labeled \"H7\" near the bottom right).\n    *   It intersects perpendicularly with an underground storm drain line (marked \"- SD -\") near the bottom left/center area.\n4.  **Crossings:** The \"- OHE -\" line does **not** appear to cross over any buildings, parking areas, or the internal drive aisles shown on this plan. It does appear to cross through the drawn canopies of several trees located along the southern property line.\n5.  **Visible clearance dimensions/annotations:** There are **no** visible clearance dimensions, height requirements, or specific textual annotations related to this OHE line other than the linetype \"- OHE -\" itself.\n6.  **Condition of overhead poles/structures:** There are **no** visible poles, towers, or supporting structures explicitly drawn or labeled in association with this \"- OHE -\" line on this specific plan sheet.\n\n---\n\n### Overall Site Context (Buildings and Detention Pond)\n\nTo establish spatial context, here is the layout of the primary site features based on the drawing:\n\n*   **Buildings (8 Units):** The primary structures are located centrally on the site, arranged in two distinct, parallel rows oriented East-West.\n    *   **Northern Building Block:** A continuous structure containing 4 attached rectangular units.\n    *   **Southern Building Block:** A continuous structure containing 4 attached rectangular units (with a slight angular jog in the middle).\n    *   These two blocks are separated by a central East-West drive aisle and parking area.\n*   **Detention Pond / Basins:** In the northeast quadrant of the site plan (east of the northern building block and north of the main drive aisle), there are two distinct hatched rectangular areas designated for stormwater management.\n    *   The western area is explicitly labeled: **\"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\"**\n    *   The eastern area is explicitly labeled: **\"FILTRATION BASIN\"**\n    *   The word \"detention pond\" is not explicitly written on this sheet, but these two adjacent basins fulfill that site feature role.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1465,"outputTokens":688,"totalTokens":4038,"reasoningTokens":1885},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Identify all overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this landscape plan. For each overhead electric line or facility, please describe:\n1. The location on the site (which portion of the property)\n2. The routing direction/orientation (north-south, east-west, diagonal)\n3. The proximity to any proposed buildings, parking areas, trees, or other site features\n4. Whether the lines appear to cross over buildings or site features\n5. Any visible clearance dimensions or annotations related to overhead electric lines\n6. The condition of overhead poles or structures (if visible)\n\nAlso describe the overall site layout showing where the 8 buildings are located and where the detention pond is located to help establish the spatial context for the overhead lines."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-hMn3gtaB2iZVm2rpYgab3I61","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 08 May 2026 13:17:59 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::bvk2x-1778246254076-e160df03aaae"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan 