lue line. A text box with a leader line explicitly labels this feature as **\"Underground Electric Line\"** (located on the left side of the drawing, pointing to the line routing near Building 2). This main line loops through the central drive aisles of the property, serving all buildings.\n*   **Electrical Pull Boxes:** Numerous pull boxes are located along the underground routing, indicated by small blue circles. They are explicitly labeled with text boxes reading **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. These are found at:\n    *   Near the northwest corner of Bldg. 1.\n    *   Southwest of Bldg. 2, near the site entrance.\n    *   South of Bldg. 8.\n    *   South of Bldg. 7 (near the property boundary).\n    *   Between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7.\n    *   Southeast of Bldg. 6.\n    *   Northeast of Bldg. 5.\n*   **Electrical Transformer Pads:** There are three large rectangular pads depicted and labeled with text boxes reading **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. Their locations are:\n    *   On the western side of the site, in an island between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 2.\n    *   On the eastern side of the site, adjacent to the driveway between Bldg. 5 and Bldg. 6.\n    *   In the central/southern part of the site, adjacent to the driveway near the north face of Bldg. 7.\n*   **Electrical Meters:** Meters are shown as being mounted to the exterior walls of the buildings. Text boxes reading **\"Electrical Meters\"** point directly to the building footprints. Every building (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) has a specific callout pointing to the location of its electrical meters.\n\n### (3) Clearance dimensions or notes regarding electric facilities\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** There are **no explicit clearance dimensions** (e.g., specific measured distances drawn with dimension lines like $10'$) shown on this plan indicating required separations between transformer pads and buildings, or between underground lines and other structures.\n*   **Notes:** There are \"Utility Notes\" located in the bottom right corner of the sheet. The relevant notes regarding utility locations state:\n    *   \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n    *   \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n    *   A warning block at the bottom right states: \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"\n    *   There is a prominent **\"Texas 811 Call Before You Dig!!\"** logo included in the bottom center area.\n\n### (4) Relationships between buildings, driveways, or other site features and electric infrastructure\n*   **Routing:** The proposed **\"Underground Electric Line\"** enters the site from the western boundary (near the main driveway entrance) and creates a complete loop around the central buildings (Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7). The routing generally follows the layout of the paved driveways, either running underneath the pavement or immediately adjacent to it within designated landscape areas or sidewalk easements.\n*   **Transformers and Site Features:** The three **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** locations are strategically placed adjacent to the internal driveways, likely for maintenance access. They appear to be located in landscape buffers or islands between the parking areas and the building footprints, rather than obstructing pedestrian paths or parking spaces.\n*   **Meters and Buildings:** The **\"Electrical Meters\"** are directly associated with the buildings. Short branch lines of the underground blue dashed line are shown extending from the main loop or transformers directly to the exterior walls of Buildings 1 through 8, where the meters are designated to be installed.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1407,"outputTokens":1093,"totalTokens":4584,"reasoningTokens":2084},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the electrical design plan and identify: (1) Any overhead electric lines, poles, or conductors shown on the site plan; (2) The locations of underground electric lines, transformers, meters, or pull boxes; (3) Any clearance dimensions or notes regarding electric facilities; (4) Any relationships between bui