 is it all underground or are there overhead components?**\nThe layout for the proposed infrastructure serving the buildings is entirely underground.\n*   On the left side of the site, there is a callout box pointing to the main blue line entering the property that explicitly states: \"**Underground Electric Line**\".\n*   The solid blue lines representing the electrical routing connect ground-mounted equipment (\"Transformer Pad\", \"Pull Box\", \"Meters\") throughout the site. There are no symbols or labels indicating overhead routing (like poles or \"OHE\" labels) for the blue lines inside the property line.\n*   The only overhead component shown is the existing line outside the property on the far left, as noted in question 1.\n\n**4. If there are overhead lines, describe their routing and voltage classification if labeled.**\nThe only overhead line shown is the dashed line labeled \"**OHE**\".\n*   **Routing:** It runs vertically (North-South) along the extreme left (western) edge of the drawing. It appears to be located in a right-of-way or easement outside the primary boundary of the townhome site.\n*   **Voltage Classification:** After scanning the \"OHE\" line and surrounding text, there is no voltage classification (e.g., kV, 120/240V) labeled for this line on this document.\n\n**5. Are there any trees or landscaping features shown near the electrical infrastructure?**\nYes, there are numerous existing trees shown on the plan, represented by large circles with scalloped or squiggly edges. The proposed underground electrical infrastructure (blue lines) is routed very close to, and often directly underneath, the canopies of these trees.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** The electrical line routing between Bldg. 3 and Bldg. 5 passes through the canopy area of several large trees.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** The electrical lines and pull boxes running south of Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7 are located near the canopies of several trees along the southern property line.\n*   *