{"level":30,"time":1778246303558,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: 1) The location and routing of the overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan - trace their path across the site; 2) The location of all proposed trees (shown as circles and symbols per the key notes - SY for street yard trees, PL for parking lot trees, P for buffer trees, M for mitigation trees); 3) The proximity of trees to the overhead electric lines - which trees appear to be within potential clearance zones (roughly 15-50 feet of the overhead conductors, depending on tree type and electric facility voltage); 4) Any tree symbols or labels near the OHE lines, including the species indicated by the symbols in the key. Please describe the spatial relationship between the overhead electric infrastructure and the proposed plantings.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the findings regarding the overhead electric lines and proposed trees:\n\n**1) Location and Routing of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines:**\nThe overhead electric line is identified by the line style labeled **-OHE-**.\n*   **Routing:** There is one visible OHE line on this plan. It runs horizontally along the extreme bottom (southern) property boundary. It enters the site view at the bottom left (west) corner, routes straight across the bottom edge of the site plan following the property line, and exits at the bottom right (east) corner.\n\n**2) Location of Proposed Trees (SY, PL, P, M):**\nAccording to the \"KEY NOTES\" on the right side of the page:\n*   **SY** = STREET YARD TREE\n*   **PL** = PARKING LOT TREE\n*   **P** = PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** = MITIGATION TREE\n\nBased on these labels, the trees are located as follows:\n*   **Western Edge (Street Frontage):** There are two trees explicitly labeled **SY/M** located within the \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\" (H-3 hatch) area on the far left side of the plan.\n*   **Northern Edge (Top Property Line):** There is a row of trees running along the top boundary. From left to right, labels visible include **M**, **SY/M**, **M**, **M**, **M**, and **M**. There is also one tree labeled **PL/M** located near the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN.\"\n*   **Southern Edge (Bottom Property Line):** Near the bottom right (southeast) corner, there is a cluster of three trees labeled **M**.\n*   *(Note: No trees explicitly labeled with just \"P\" were found on this specific sheet, though the designation exists in the key).*\n\n**3) Proximity of Trees to the Overhead Electric Lines (Clearance Zones):**\nThere is a direct spatial conflict shown on the plan between the proposed/existing tree canopy locations and the OHE line running along the southern boundary.\n*   Moving west to east along the **-OHE-** line at the bottom of the page, the large circles representing tree canopies significantly overlap the OHE line.\n*   Specifically, in the bottom right (southeast) corner, there are three proposed tree planting symbols (indicated by circles with crosshairs representing the trunk location). The center points of these three trees are plotted directly on top of, or immediately adjacent to, the **-OHE-** line. These trees are definitively within the potential clearance zone (well within the 15-50 foot range mentioned).\n\n**4) Tree Symbols/Labels Near OHE Lines and Species:**\nFocusing on the immediate vicinity of the **-OHE-** line at the bottom of the plan:\n*   In the bottom right corner, there are three specific tree symbols clustered together directly over the OHE line.\n*   Each of these three tree symbols has a leader line pointing to a label designating them as **M**.\n*   According to the Key Notes, **M** designates a **MITIGATION TREE**.\n*   **Species:** There is no plant schedule, species list, or botanical name provided on this specific document sheet. Therefore, the exact species of these mitigation trees cannot be identified from this image alone.\n\n**Summary of Spatial Relationship:**\nThe landscape plan indicates a significant spatial conflict along the southern property boundary. Three proposed Mitigation (\"M\") trees are sited directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the routing of the Overhead Electric (-OHE-) line, placing their future growth path directly into the infrastructure's clearance zone.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1474,"outputTokens":795,"totalTokens":4109,"reasoningTokens":1840},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: 1) The location and routing of the overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan - trace their path across the site; 2) The location of all proposed trees (shown as circles and symbols per the key notes - SY for street yard trees, PL for parking lot trees, P for buffer trees, M for mitigation trees); 3) The proximity of trees to the overhead electric lines - which trees appear to be within potential clearance zones (roughly 15-50 feet of the overhead conductors, depending on tree type and electric facility voltage); 4) Any tree symbols or labels near the OHE lines, including the species indicated by the symbols in the key. Please describe the spatial relationship between the overhead electric infrastructure and the proposed plantings."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-k7gdLs9IQNE0S1VuMmNSUs6T","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 08 May 2026 13:18:23 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"r