riveway (Southwest):** The line directly crosses the main entrance/exit driveway located in the southwest corner of the site (labeled \"**Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 1/335-2**\").\n    *   **Retaining Walls (South Central/Southeast):** The line runs directly over or parallel to several retaining wall segments labeled \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\", \"**Concrete Retaining Wall**\", and \"**End Concrete Retaining Wall Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall**\".\n    *   **Buildings:** Building 8 (\"**Bldg. 8**\"), Building 7 (\"**Bldg. 7**\"), and Building 6 (\"**Bldg. 6**\") are located to the north of this line, seemingly near the edge of the utility easement (which implies they are in close proximity, potentially near the 15-foot threshold, though exact scaled distance cannot be definitively stated without physical measurement).\n*   **East OHE Line (Eastern Boundary):**\n    *   **Retaining Walls (East):** The line runs directly over or immediately adjacent to a wall labeled \"**Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced**\".\n    *   **Fences/Walls (East):** The line crosses or runs parallel to features labeled \"**Concrete Wall**\" and \"**Wood Fence**\".\n    *   **Buildings:** Building 5 (\"**Bldg. 5**\") and Building 6 (\"**Bldg. 6**\") are situated just west of this eastern property line and OHE line.\n\n**4) Clearance Dimensions**\n*   There are **no explicit vertical or horizontal clearance dimensions** labeled on the plan detailing the required distance between the overhead electric lines and nearby site features (such as the driveway, retaining walls, or buildings).\n\n**5) Location of Meters or Other Electrical Equipment**\n*   **West Side (Central/Northwest):** There is a square equipment pad labeled exactly as \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\" located just to the west of Building 1 (\"**Bldg. 1**\").\n*   *(Note: A small meter label near the northwest driveway reads \"Existing Water Meter,\" which is not electrical).*\n\n**6) Notes Regarding Overhead Utilities**\n*   **Southeast Corner:** There is a specific easement note confirming the presence of these utilities along the boundary, explicitly transcribed as: \"**15' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.**\" \n*   No specific construction notes or site plan release notes in the provided text tables explicitly detail overhead utility clearance rules or handling instructions.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1457,"outputTokens":794,"totalTokens":4807,"reasoningTokens":2556},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan drawing 