{"level":30,"time":1778246311732,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan. Please identify:\n1. The location of any overhead electric utility lines or equipment shown on this plan\n2. Whether these lines are distribution or transmission based on voltage labeling or equipment shown\n3. Any notes about conductor locations or pole locations\n4. Cross-reference to understand if the overhead electric line runs along the southern property boundary adjacent to Valley View Road\n5. Any reference to the landscape plan or tree coordination","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here is the information requested:\n\n**1. Location of overhead electric utility lines or equipment**\nOverhead electric lines, denoted by lines with \"OHE\" text embedded within them, are located along two property boundaries shown on this plan:\n*   Running along the **Western boundary**, parallel to the right-of-way labeled \"Valley View Road\". Associated utility poles are visible along this line.\n*   Running along the **Northern boundary** of the site.\n\n**2. Type of lines (distribution vs. transmission)**\n*   **Voltage Labeling:** There are **no specific voltage labels** (e.g., 12kV, 138kV) visible on the overhead lines themselves in this document.\n*   **Equipment Shown:** The plan shows blue lines tapping off the system to route underground into the site, feeding equipment explicitly labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** located next to the residential buildings (e.g., adjacent to Bldg. 2, Bldg. 5, Bldg. 6).\n*   **Conclusion:** While not explicitly labeled with a voltage, the presence of these pad-mounted transformers stepping power down directly for residential townhome buildings indicates these are **distribution** lines, not high-voltage transmission lines.\n\n**3. Notes about conductor or pole locations**\n*   Near a pole on the western OHE line (along Valley View Road, towards the bottom left of the sheet), there is a specific callout note pointing to the pole that reads: **\"See Sht. 19 for Profile\"**. This likely contains vertical profile information for the conductors/poles.\n*   In the **\"Utility Notes\"** section in the bottom right corner, notes 1 and 2 state:\n    *   *\"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"*\n    *   *\"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"*\n*   Below the Utility Notes box, there is a general disclaimer block regarding existing utilities which states: *\"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"*\n\n**4. Cross-reference regarding the southern property boundary and Valley View Road**\nBased on the North arrow situated in the top right corner of the drawing (pointing upwards):\n*   **Valley View Road is located on the Western boundary** of the site, not the Southern boundary. As noted in point 1, there *is* an overhead electric line running along this Western boundary adjacent to Valley View Road.\n*   Looking at the **Southern boundary** (the bottom edge of the drawing), there are **no overhead electric lines (\"OHE\") visible**. The southern boundary shows adjoining property information (e.g., \"William Lewis...\").\n\n**5. Reference to landscape plan or tree coordination**\n*   In the bottom center of the sheet, there is a bordered box titled **\"Tree List\"**. The text inside this box states exactly:\n    **\"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"**\n*   Additionally, large, light-grey circular linework representing existing tree canopies is drawn throughout the site plan, demonstrating visual coordination between the electrical routing and existing trees, though the specific tree data is deferred to the landscape plan.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1402,"outputTokens":762,"totalTokens":4049,"reasoningTokens":1885},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine t