{"level":30,"time":1778246318065,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFbvQxdpeEKRKGakKDE8cb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n     2→\n     3→Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n    11→*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n    12→*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n    13→*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n    14→*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n    15→*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n    16→*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n    17→*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n    18→*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n    19→*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n    20→*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    25→    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    28→    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    31→    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    34→    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    37→    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    40→    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    43→    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    46→    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    49→    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    52→    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    55→    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n    56→\n    57→*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    58→    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0303f2e2-ff0c-4b14-bd62-f1e72863d84c","uuid":"6c86b0a3-cb70-4a29-b58c-e8f2982a39b6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n\nDetailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n\n*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n\n*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n\n*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n\n*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n\n*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n\n*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n\n*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246323239,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Identify all electric infrastructure shown on this preliminary electrical design plan, including:\n1. Whether there are overhead electric lines (conductors, poles, guy wires) shown on or adjacent to this site\n2. The routing and location of any existing overhead electric facilities\n3. The location of proposed electrical service connections, transformers, meters, and other electrical infrastructure\n4. Whether there are any clearance dimensions or annotations related to overhead electric lines\n5. The routing of underground electric lines (if shown)\n6. The relationship between proposed buildings and any overhead electric lines or poles\n7. Any easements designated for electric facilities\n\nAlso describe the overall site layout showing the 8 buildings and their locations relative to any overhead electric infrastructure.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" document, here is a description of the electrical infrastructure and site layout as requested:\n\n**1. Overhead electric lines (conductors, poles, guy wires) on or adjacent to the site:**\nYes, overhead electric lines are present adjacent to the site. They are indicated by line types with text annotations.\n*   A line labeled **\"- OHE -\"** (indicating Overhead Electric) runs north-south along the western boundary of the site, appearing to be located within or adjacent to the right-of-way for \"Valley View Road\". Several utility pole symbols (small circles, some with crosshairs) are visible along this line.\n*   Another line labeled **\"- OHE -\"** runs east-west along the southern boundary of the property.\n\n**2. Routing and location of existing overhead electric facilities:**\n*   **Western Route:** The overhead line (\"- OHE -\") begins near the northwest corner of the visible plan and runs straight south, parallel to the western property line and outside the main development boundary.\n*   **Southern Route:** An overhead line (\"- OHE -\") runs along the southern edge of the property, connecting near the southwest corner and running eastward parallel to the southern property line.\n\n**3. Location of proposed electrical service connections, transformers, meters, and other infrastructure:**\nThe proposed electrical design is heavily annotated using blue lines and rectangular callout boxes pointing to specific symbols throughout the interior of the site. I have transcribed the exact text from these blue callout boxes and their general locations:\n\n*   **Near Bldg. 1 (NW corner):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Meters\"**, **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**, and **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Near Bldg. 2 (Mid-West):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**, **\"Electrical Meters\"**, and **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**.\n*   **Near Bldg. 3 (North-Center):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Meters\"** and **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**.\n*   **Near Bldg. 4 (Center):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Meters\"**, **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**, and **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**.\n*   **Near Bldg. 5 (NE corner):** Callout for **\"Electrical Meters\"**.\n*   **Near Bldg. 6 (Mid-East):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** and **\"Electrical Meters\"** (located to the south of the building).\n*   **Near Bldg. 7 (South-Center):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**, **\"Electrical Meters\"** (pointing to two separate locations near this building).\n*   **Near Bldg. 8 (SW corner):** Callouts for **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**, **\"Electrical Meters\"**, and **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**.\n\n**4. Clearance dimensions or annotations related to overhead electric lines:**\nThere are **no** specific clearance dimensions (e.g., radius arcs, offset lines, or text stating minimum distances) shown between the proposed buildings and the adjacent overhead (\"- OHE -\") electric lines on this plan.\n\n**5. Routing of underground electric lines:**\nThe routing of the underground electric lines is clearly shown using dashed blue lines that form a network throughout the interior of the development. Two blue callout boxes specifically label these lines as **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n*   The primary feed appears to start near the northwest corner of the site.\n*   The blue line loops through the property, routing east-west between the northern row of buildings (Bldgs 1, 3) and the middle row (Bldgs 2, 4), and then continues through the site to connect all the transformer pads, pull boxes, and meter banks associated with the 8 buildings. It essentially forms an internal grid/loop serving the entire complex.\n\n**6. Relationship between proposed buildings and overhead electric lines/poles:**\nThe 8 proposed buildings are situated within the interior of the site, set back from the property boundaries.\n*   Because the overhead electric lines (\"- OHE -\") are routed along the extreme western and southern outer perimeters (right-of-way/property boundaries), none of the overhead lines cross directly over any of the proposed buildings.\n*   The buildings (specifically Bldgs 1, 2, and 8 on the west, and Bldgs 8, 7, and 6 on the south) are separated from the overhead lines by setbacks, landscaping areas, and internal driveways/parking.\n\n**7. Easements designated for electric facilities:**\nThere are several specific easements noted on the plan that mention electrical use:\n*   On the northern boundary (near the center): A circular dashed area is labeled **\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 69, Pg... P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** (Public Utility Easements typically include electric).\n*   On the eastern boundary (mid-way down): Text notes a **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   On the southern boundary (near the center): Text notes a **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   On the southern boundary (further east): Text notes a **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 385 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**Overall Site Layout Summary:**\nThe site consists of 8 rectangular buildings labeled \"Bldg. 1\" through \"Bldg. 8\". They are arranged generally in three columns from west to east:\n*   **Western column:** Bldg. 1 (North), Bldg. 2 (Middle), Bldg. 8 (South).\n*   **Center column:** Bldg. 3 (North), Bldg. 4 (Middle), Bldg. 7 (South).\n*   **Eastern column:** Bldg. 5 (North), Bldg. 6 (Middle).\nAs described in item 6, this central arrangement keeps all 8 buildings buffered away from the existing overhead electric infrastructure on the western and southern edges of the plan, relying instead on the proposed blue-lined underground electric network for service.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1457,"outputTokens":1391,"totalTokens":5282,"reasoningTokens":2434},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Identify all electric infrastructure shown on this preliminary electrical design plan, including:\n1. Whether there are overhead electric lines (conductors, poles, guy wires) shown on or adjacent to this site\n2. The routing and location of any existing overhead electric facilities\n3. The location of proposed electrical service connections, transformers, meters, and other electrical infrastructure\n4. Whether there are any clearance dimensions or annotations related to overhead electric lines\n5. The routing of underground electric lines (if shown)\n6. The relationship between proposed buildings and any overhead electric lines or poles\n7. Any easements designated for electric facilities\n\nAlso describe the overall site layout showing the 8 buildings and their locations relative to any overhead electric infrastructure."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-h8VyStDTVUldMDemOAMmhaZg","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, P