e.\n*   The blue line loops through the property, routing east-west between the northern row of buildings (Bldgs 1, 3) and the middle row (Bldgs 2, 4), and then continues through the site to connect all the transformer pads, pull boxes, and meter banks associated with the 8 buildings. It essentially forms an internal grid/loop serving the entire complex.\n\n**6. Relationship between proposed buildings and overhead electric lines/poles:**\nThe 8 proposed buildings are situated within the interior of the site, set back from the property boundaries.\n*   Because the overhead electric lines (\"- OHE -\") are routed along the extreme western and southern outer perimeters (right-of-way/property boundaries), none of the overhead lines cross directly over any of the proposed buildings.\n*   The buildings (specifically Bldgs 1, 2, and 8 on the west, and Bldgs 8, 7, and 6 on the south) are separated from the overhead lines by setbacks, landscaping areas, and internal driveways/parking.\n\n**7. Easements designated for electric facilities:**\nThere are several specific easements noted on the plan that mention electrical use:\n*   On the northern boundary (near the center): A circular dashed area is labeled **\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 69, Pg... P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** (Public Utility Easements typically include electric).\n*   On the eastern boundary (mid-way down): Text notes a **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   On the southern boundary (near the center): Text notes a **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   On the southern boundary (further east): Text notes a **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 385 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**Overall Site Layout Summary:**\nThe site consists of 8 rectangular buildings labeled \"Bldg. 1\" through \"Bldg. 8\". They are arranged generally in three columns from west to east:\n*   **Western column:** Bldg. 1 (North), Bldg. 2 (Middle), Bldg. 8 (South).\n*   **Center column:** Bldg. 3 (N