r a manhole that reads **\"FH (Out): 682.03, FH (In): 682.33\"**.\n\n**3. Is there a parking area shown on the site plan? If so, what is the location and proximity to any transformer pads?**\n*   Yes, surface parking areas are depicted. The \"Parking Data\" table indicates \"10 Surface\" spaces provided. These are located in three groups off the main internal driveway: four spaces east of Bldg. 1, four spaces east of Bldg. 2, and two spaces south of Bldg. 8.\n*   **Proximity to Transformer Pads:** A feature is explicitly labeled **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** on the west side of Bldg. 1. Similar unmarked rectangular shapes appear on the exterior sides of several other buildings. \n    *   Most of these pads (like those west of Bldgs. 1 and 2) are on the opposite side of the building from the surface parking spaces.\n    *   However, the rectangular pad located immediately south of **Bldg. 8** is situated directly to the west of the two surface parking spaces in that area. They appear to be separated only by a narrow depicted strip of landscaping/buffer.\n\n**4. Are there utility easements depicted on the drawing? If yes, describe which utilities have easements and their locations.**\n*   Yes, numerous utility easements are clearly depicted and labeled throughout the site. They include:\n    *   **Wastewater Easement:** Labeled \"Wastewater Easement Doc#\" located in the northwest corner near the site entrance.\n    *   **Public Utility Easement:** Labeled **\"5' P.U.E.\"** running along the northern property line.\n    *   **Drainage Easement:** A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** is located in the northeast corner within the perimeter of the detention pond. Another line labeled **\"Drainage Easement\"** is located in the southeast corner.\n    *   **Electric/Telecommunications Easement:** An **\"Electric Easement\"** is labeled along the eastern boundary line. Near the southern property boundary, there are labels for a **\"5' Elec. Easement\"** and a **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\"**.\n    *   **Water Easement:** An **\"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement Doc#\"** is located internally, situated between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 8.\n\n**5. Are property lines clearly marked? Can you identify any areas where transformer pads might be straddling property lines?**\n*   Yes, the property boundary is clearly marked by a heavy, thick solid line encompassing the entire development. \n*   Based on the drawing, all rectangular footprints representing the transformer pads (including the one specifically labeled west of Bldg. 1 and the typical unlabelled ones around the site perimeter) appear to be situated entirely *inside* this heavy property boundary line. None appear to be straddling or crossing the outer property line. \n\n**6. Are there any bollards or protective barriers shown on the plan near the transformer pads?**\n*   No. While bollards are shown on the plan (specifically labeled as **\"Bollard (Typ)\"** near the driveway east of Bldg. 5 and between Bldgs. 6 and 7 to protect building corners from vehicles), there are no bollards or protective barriers depicted immediately adjacent to or surrounding the rectangular outlines representing the transformer pads.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex