{"level":30,"time":1778246350610,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VVMDR2HNKYJ5T7GK98FF9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Grading Plan (Sheet 11) shows building elevations and spot elevations, but there's NO mention of overhead electric lines or clearance dimensions from any overhead lines to buildings, driveways, or parking areas.\n\nLet me now check if there's an Existing Conditions Survey detailed look at what overhead poles/lines are shown. But I already did that via the vision tool. Let me now think about applicability:\n\n**APPLICABILITY ASSESSMENT:**\n\nBased on my research:\n1. There ARE existing overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the site plan:\n   - One OHE line runs north-south along the western boundary (in/near Valley View Road ROW)\n   - One OHE line runs east-west along the southern boundary\n   - Multiple utility pole symbols are visible\n\n2. There ARE proposed site features:\n   - 8 multi-family residential buildings\n   - Parking areas\n   - Driveways\n   - Trees (landscape plan)\n   - Retaining walls\n\nTherefore, this grouping IS APPLICABLE - there are overhead electric facilities and proposed site features that must maintain clearances.\n\n**RESEARCH FINDINGS SUMMARY:**\n\nWhat I found:\n1. Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows:\n   - Existing OHE lines on western (north-south) and southern (east-west) boundaries\n   - Multiple utility pole symbols\n   - NO clearance dimensions shown from OHE lines to proposed buildings\n   - Proposed underground electric service infrastructure (transformers, meters, pull boxes)\n\n2. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows:\n   - One OHE line along the southern boundary\n   - NO clearance dimensions or annotations related to OHE\n\n3. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows:\n   - Building FFEs and spot elevations\n   - NO overhead line elevations or clearance dimensions\n   - NO profile sections showing vertical clearances\n\n4. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows:\n   - Note: \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date\"\n   - Utility lines depicted but without clearance dimensions\n\n5. Sheet 1 (Cover Sheet) shows:\n   - NO 48-hour Austin Energy notification requirement\n\nWhat I could NOT find/verify:\n1. NO building elevation sheets showing overhead conductor heights and clearances from building faces/projections\n2. NO profile sections showing vertical clearances from overhead lines to driveways/parking\n3. NO clearance dimensions from outer conductor to any site features\n4. NO specification of whether lines are primary, neutral, or secondary conductors\n5. NO notation of line voltages/types (distribution vs. transmission)\n6. NO mid-span clearance survey data\n7. NO 48-hour notification note on plans\n8. NO separate proximity survey as required by UCM § 1.10.3\n9. NO section/profile exhibits showing clearance verification\n10. NO utility-compatible tree verification for trees proposed near overhead lines\n\nMissing proximity survey documentation per code requirements, section/profile exhibits to verify clearances, and confirmation that any proposed trees near overhead lines meet utility compatibility standards. Now I need to evaluate each of the 47 checklist items based on this research.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7700aa25-0227-4e8e-93af-3aee77428b5b","uuid":"ec90c612-fbac-46ab-a4b1-8c4e38c81843"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246351180,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VVMDR2HNKYJ5T7GK98FF9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a comprehensive analysis of each checklist item. Based on my research, I've found:\n\n**Key Findings:**\n- There ARE existing overhead electric (OHE) lines on the site boundaries (west and south)\n- Multiple utility pole symbols are shown\n- Building elevations are NOT provided\n- NO clearance dimensions are shown from overhead lines to buildings/features\n- NO section profiles showing vertical clearances\n- NO 48-hour Austin Energy notification note found\n- Underground electrical service is proposed (transformers, meters, pull boxes)\n- Tree landscape plan exists but tree species compliance with utility-compatible list not verified\n- No vertical clearance dimensions for driveways under overhead lines\n\nLet me now evaluate each checklist item systematically:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7700aa25-0227-4e8e-93af-3aee77428b5b","uuid":"2c619f84-49ff-4687-b2b3-6d27e5c1f235"}
