{"level":30,"time":1778246351499,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: (1) Any trees shown on the plan, particularly their locations and proximity to overhead electric lines (marked as \"OHE\" or \"Overhead Electric\"); (2) The locations of tree symbols and their designations (SY, PL, P, M meanings are in the legend); (3) Any trees proposed within or near the transmission easement area (top-right corner area); (4) Tree species if labeled; (5) Any clearance notes or spacing dimensions related to overhead utilities. Provide specific details about tree locations relative to the overhead electric infrastructure.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246354899,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VVT9AMH6C8GR3SC2DY3QE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The blocks are limited. Let me look at what facts.md says about electric easements. From my earlier reading of facts.md, I saw:\n\nFrom the facts.md file (lines 135-143):\n\"**Easement 7 & 8 — 5' Electric Easements (×2)**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 73/76, Case C8S-75-160\n- **Width:** 5 ft each\n- **Status:** DEDICATED\n\n**Easement 9 — 7.5' Public Utility Easement**\n- **Document Ref:** Travis County Doc 73/76, Case C8S-75-160\n- **Width:** 7.5 ft\n- **Status:** DEDICATED\"\n\nSo there are electric easements on the plat. But are these transmission easements? The grouping mentions transmission easements specifically. From the facts.md file, I also noticed that no regulating plan applies (line 52: \"Regulating Plan: None\").\n\nNow I need to understand what's actually in the utilities shown. Let me check if there's information about whether there are transmission lines or just distribution lines. The fact that the OHE line is shown on the landscape plan suggests there are overhead lines on or adjacent to the property.\n\nLooking at the vision output, the three trees are estimated to be 2-5 feet from the OHE line, which would violate:\n- EL-2.6: Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole (if there are poles)\n- EL-2.8: Trees proposed within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment (if these are near underground equipment)\n\nBut more specifically, the overhead electric line itself requires minimum clearance based on whether it's distribution or transmission.\n\nI need to determine:\n1. Are these distribution or transmission lines?\n2. Are the proposed trees utility-compatible?\n3. What are the mature heights of the proposed trees?\n4. Are there any Austin Energy approvals for variance?\n\n\n5. I should check the Grading Plan to see where the easement boundaries actually fall on the site.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3284e2-1747-4d44-a558-2f00d9a24819","uuid":"dcadf46a-5c89-4ebb-bfa0-6a88f12ebb70"}
