ner of record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced, maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project includes 2 private hydrants.\"\n\n**Fire Zone Notes:**\nThis section reads exactly:\n> \"1. Restricted Zone signage to be placed on front of lockers and along boat slip retaining walls as necessary or required.\n> 2. Stencil the words \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" in white letters at least 4\" high at 30 foot intervals along the curb and the entire curb shall be painted red to serve as the background for the white letters.\n> 3. Signs stating \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" shall be posted at both ends of a fire zone and at each entry and exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of Austin Detail 801S-6.\n> 4. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n> 5. All private hydrants shall be painted red.\"\n*(Note: Item 1 appears to contain legacy text from a different project type, but is transcribed exactly as it appears).*\n\n**Notes:**\nThis section reads exactly:\n> \"1. Underground mains feeding NFPA 13 sprinkler systems must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA 13, and the Fire Code, by a licensed sprinkler contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n> 2. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n> 3. The Knox-box is to be located at exterior fire riser room door (non-hinged side).\"\n\n**Fire Riser Room Note:**\nThis text box reads exactly:\n> \"All buildings are to have a NFPA 13D fire suppression system.\"\n\n**Fire Flow Test:**\nThis text box reads exactly:\n> \"See Sheet 18, Austin Water General Notes, for the fire flow test results.\"\n\n### 4. Proximity of Fire Lanes to Transformer Pad Locations\nAfter a thorough review of this specific sheet, **there are no transformer pads visibly labeled or identifiable** on this Fire Protection Plan. While there is a \"5' Electric Easement\" noted on the eastern property boundary, specific transformer equipment locations are not shown, so their proximity to the fire lanes cannot be determined from this document alone.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1394,"outputTokens":1248,"totalTokens":6055,"reasoningTokens":3413},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":1778246317473,"endTime":1778246357840,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"reL9acqCJ_aZ5OMPide2mQM"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.058945","ma