{"level":30,"time":1778246375648,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the trees and utilities on this landscape plan. Please identify:\n1. The location of trees relative to overhead electric (OHE) lines - which trees are closest to the OHE line and approximately how far away (visually)?\n2. Identify trees shown near the western edge of the property (near Valley View Road and the transformer pad area mentioned on Sheet 9).\n3. List all tree symbols you can identify on the plan with their location descriptions (e.g., \"north side near Building 3\", \"south side along property line\").\n4. Note any labels or annotations on tree symbols that might indicate species or size.\n5. Are there any dimension lines or clearance measurements shown between trees and utilities?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the visual analysis regarding trees and utilities:\n\n**1. Location of trees relative to overhead electric (OHE) lines**\n*   The overhead electric line is clearly marked with a line type reading **\"-OHE-\"** running along the entire **southern property line** (bottom edge of the drawing).\n*   A continuous row of trees is proposed along this entire southern boundary, planted just north of the OHE line.\n*   **Proximity:** Visually, the outer circles (canopies) of almost all trees along this southern edge appear to directly overlap or touch the \"-OHE-\" line. The center points (trunks) of these trees are located a short distance north of the line. Without specific dimensions, they appear to be planted directly adjacent to the utility easement/line.\n\n**2. Trees shown near the western edge of the property (Valley View Road / transformer area)**\n*   The western edge of the property borders **\"Valley View Road\"**.\n*   There is a designated shaded landscape buffer area running along this western edge, adjacent to the parking area and street.\n*   Several trees are planted within this buffer zone:\n    *   A cluster in the northwest corner.\n    *   Trees located in the parking islands/peninsulas protruding into the parking lot.\n    *   Near the southwest corner, there is a rectangular pad structure outlined with a dashed line (which may correspond to the transformer pad mentioned in your prompt). There are at least two trees planted in close proximity to this structure: one large canopy tree immediately north/northeast of it, and another to the west.\n\n**3. List of tree symbols and their location descriptions**\nTree symbols are distributed primarily around the perimeter of the site:\n*   **North side:** A long row of trees is planted along the northern property boundary, adjacent to the line labeled \"-LOC-\".\n*   **East side:** Trees are sparsely placed along the eastern property line, with a small cluster near the northeast corner and another cluster near the southeast corner.\n*   **South side:** A dense, continuous row of trees runs along the entire southern boundary, parallel to the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **West side:** Trees are clustered in the landscape buffer along Valley View Road, including in the street yard (annotated with Key Notes H-2, H-3) and parking lot islands (Key Note H-4).\n*   **Interior:** Very few trees are shown in the interior courtyards. There is one tree symbol shown adjacent to the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\" on the eastern side of the property.\n\n**4. Labels or annotations on tree symbols indicating species or size**\nThere are no standard botanical species abbreviations (like *Qv* for Quercus virginiana) or sizes (like *3\" cal.*) directly labeling the individual tree symbols on the plan view. However, many tree symbols contain letter codes in their center circles that correspond to a legend on the right side of the sheet:\n*   **\"M\"**: Many trees, especially along the north, south, and east property lines, have an \"M\" in the center. The legend at the top right defines this as **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n*   **\"PL\"**: At least one tree on the northern boundary has \"PL\" next to it. The legend defines this as **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**.\n*   **\"SYM\"**: Two trees on the western boundary (within the shaded parking island area) appear to have the letters **\"SYM\"** inside their center circles.\n*   Many other trees simply have a standard crosshair (\"+\"), an \"x\", or an empty circle in the center without specific text labels.\n\n**5. Dimension lines or clearance measurements between trees and utilities**\n*   **No dimension lines or specific clearance measurements** (e.g., \"10' clearance\") are shown between the tree symbols and the utility lines (like the OHE line) on this specific sheet. The plan shows layout and relative positioning visually, but lacks explicit distance measurements for utility clearances.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1460,"outputTokens":896,"totalTokens":4469,"reasoningTokens":2113},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information th