n your prompt). There are at least two trees planted in close proximity to this structure: one large canopy tree immediately north/northeast of it, and another to the west.\n\n**3. List of tree symbols and their location descriptions**\nTree symbols are distributed primarily around the perimeter of the site:\n*   **North side:** A long row of trees is planted along the northern property boundary, adjacent to the line labeled \"-LOC-\".\n*   **East side:** Trees are sparsely placed along the eastern property line, with a small cluster near the northeast corner and another cluster near the southeast corner.\n*   **South side:** A dense, continuous row of trees runs along the entire southern boundary, parallel to the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **West side:** Trees are clustered in the landscape buffer along Valley View Road, including in the street yard (annotated with Key Notes H-2, H-3) and parking lot islands (Key Note H-4).\n*   **Interior:** Very few trees are shown in the interior courtyards. There is one tree symbol shown adjacent to the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\" on the eastern side of the property.\n\n**4. Labels or annotations on tree symbols indicating species or size**\nThere are no standard botanical species abbreviations (like *Qv* for Quercus virginiana) or sizes (like *3\" cal.*) directly labeling the individual tree symbols on the plan view. However, many tree symbols contain letter codes in their center circles that correspond to a legend on the right side of the sheet:\n*   **\"M\"**: Many trees, especially along the north, south, and east property lines, have an \"M\" in the center. The legend at the top right defines this as **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n*   **\"PL\"**: At least one tree on the northern boundary has \"PL\" next to it. The legend defines this as **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**.\n*   **\"SYM\"**: Two trees on the western boundary (within the shaded parking island area) appear to have the letters **\"SYM\"** inside their center circles.\n*   Many other trees simply have a standard crosshair (\"+\"), an \"x\", or an empty circle in the center without specific text labels.\n\n**5. Dimension lines or clearance measurements between trees and utilities**\n*   **No dimension lines or specific clearance measurements** (e.g., \"10' clearance\") are shown between the tree symbols and the utility lines (like the OHE line) on this specific sheet. The plan shows layout and relative positioning visually, but lacks explicit distance measurements for utility clearances."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778246376612,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) and determine:\n\n1. Transformer pad locations - Can you identify the four electrical transformer pads from Sheet 21 on this grading plan? Describe their locations using compass directions and building references.\n\n2. Grade elevations - What are the ground surface elevations at or near each of the transformer pad locations? Are there spot elevations or contour labels near the pads?\n\n3. Drainage direction - What is the slope direction and drainage flow pattern around each transformer pad? Is drainage flowing toward or away from building structures?\n\n4. For oil-filled transformer equipment specifically - if any pads contain oil-filled equipment, does the grading show drainage slopes directing liquid flow AWAY from buildings as required?\n\n5. Any grading notes or special drainage considerations for areas around the pads?\n\nPlease be specific about elevations, slope percentages, and directions.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a meticulous visual analysis of Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) for the Valley View Townhomes project, here are the findings regarding your requests. \n\n**CRITICAL OBSERVATION:** Physical electrical transformer concrete pads (typically depicted as solid or crosshatched rectangles and explicitly labeled \"Transformer\" or \"Pad\") are **not drafted or labeled** on this specific grading plan sheet. \n\nHowever, there are explicitly labeled **electrical easements** where this equipment is typically placed. To provide you with the most relevant information possible, the analysis below is based on the locations of these labeled electrical easements.\n\n### 1. Transformer Pad Locations (Based on Electrical Easements)\nWhile four distinct pads cannot be seen, I can identify three distinct electrical easement areas near the property boundaries:\n\n*   **Location A (East Property Line):** Located on the mid-east boundary of the site, directly east of **Bldg. 6**. It is designated by dashed lines and labeled exactly as **\"5' Electric Easement / Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Location B (South Property Line):** Located on the southern boundary of the site, directly south of the eastern half of **Bldg. 8**. It is designated by dashed lines and labeled exactly as **\"5' Elec. Easement / Vol. 66, Pg. 14 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Location C (Extreme Southeast Corner):** Located in the far southeast corner of the property line, southeast of the retaining wall. It is labeled exactly as **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement / Vol. 5468, Pg. 885 / D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n*Note: A fourth distinct electrical easement or pad location is not clearly identifiable on this specific sheet.*\n\n### 2. Grade Elevations\nBecause the pads themselves are not drafted, there are no spot elevations dedicated specifically to the corners of transformer pads. However, the surrounding grade elevations in the easement areas are as follows:\n\n*   **Near Location A (East of Bldg. 6):** \n    *   Proposed contour lines **681** and **682** run between Bldg. 6 and the easement.\n    *   An existing grade spot elevation is labeled exactly as **\"EG 689.84\"** within the text of the easement label.\n    *   The top of the proposed retaining wall adjacent to this easement is labeled **\"TW 680.26\"**.\n*   **Near Location B (South of Bldg. 8):**\n    *   Finished grade spot elevations along the property line/easement area are labeled exactly as **\"FG 680.70\"**, **\"FG 681.18\"**, and **\"FG 682.12\"**.\n    *   Adjacent top/bottom of curb spot elevations between the building and the easement include **\"681.69 / 681.19\"** and **\"682.06 / 681.56\"**.\n    *   The Finished Floor Elevation (FFE) for Bldg. 8 is **685.50**.\n*   **Near Location C (Southeast Corner):**\n    *   This is an area with a steep drop-off behind existing and proposed retaining walls. An existing grade spot elevation is labeled exactly as **\"EG 668.59\"**.\n    *   An adjacent top of wall elevation is labeled **\"TW 678.50\"**.\n\n### 3. Drainage Direction\nBased on the proposed contour lines and spot elevations, the macro-drainage patterns in these easement areas are as follows:\n\n*   **Location A (East of Bldg. 6):** The land slopes downwards from West to East. Drainage flows **away** from Bldg. 6 (FFE 685.0) down across contours 682 and 681, directing water toward the eastern property line and the retaining wall.\n*   **Location B (South of Bldg. 8):** The land slopes downwards from North to South. Drainage flows **away** from Bldg. 8 (FFE 685.50), dropping to curb elevations in the ~681.69 range, and further down to finished grades in the ~680.70 range at the southern property line/retaining wall.\n\n### 4. Oil-Filled Transformer Equipment Drainage Compliance\nBecause the specific micro-grading of concrete pads is not shown on this sheet, a definitive assessment of the pad itself cannot be made. \n\nHowever, looking at the macro-grading of the electrical easement areas where these pads would likely sit (East of Bldg. 6 and South of Bldg. 8), **the general grading plan does successfully direct surface flow AWAY from the adjacent building structures** and toward the perimeter retaining walls and property lines. If oil-filled equipment were placed in these easements matching the surrounding proposed grade, liquid would flow away from the buildings.\n\n### 5. Grading Notes or Special Considerations\nThere are **no specific grading notes, callouts, or details** on Sheet 11 that mention transformers, electrical pads, or special drainage considerations for oil-filled equipment. \n\nThe only general grading note present is located in the bottom left corner under \"Curb Note\", which reads exactly: *\"Grading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\"*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1487,"outputTokens":1202,"totalTokens":6015,"reasoningTokens":3326},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) and determine:\n\n1. Transformer pad locations - Can you identify the four electrical transformer pads from Sheet 21 on this grading plan? Describe their locations using compass directions and building references.\n\n2. Grade elevations - What are the ground surface elevations at or near each of the transformer pad locations? Are there spot elevations or contour labels near the pads?\n\n3. Drainage direction - What is the slope direction and drainage flow pattern around each transformer pad? Is drainage flowing toward or away from building structures?\n\n4. For oil-filled transformer equipment specifically - if any pads contain oil-filled equipment, does the grading show drainage slopes directing liquid flow AWAY from buildings as required?\n\n5. Any grading notes or special drainage considerations for areas around the pads?\n\nPlease be specific about elevations, slope percentages, and directions."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-9qwkQGwrRhXYErFIg1opqYV2","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 08 May 2026 13:19:36 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::jh2w6-1778246335604-167c7c5762d6"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a meticulous visual analysis of Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) for the 