.\n    *   The Finished Floor Elevation (FFE) for Bldg. 8 is **685.50**.\n*   **Near Location C (Southeast Corner):**\n    *   This is an area with a steep drop-off behind existing and proposed retaining walls. An existing grade spot elevation is labeled exactly as **\"EG 668.59\"**.\n    *   An adjacent top of wall elevation is labeled **\"TW 678.50\"**.\n\n### 3. Drainage Direction\nBased on the proposed contour lines and spot elevations, the macro-drainage patterns in these easement areas are as follows:\n\n*   **Location A (East of Bldg. 6):** The land slopes downwards from West to East. Drainage flows **away** from Bldg. 6 (FFE 685.0) down across contours 682 and 681, directing water toward the eastern property line and the retaining wall.\n*   **Location B (South of Bldg. 8):** The land slopes downwards from North to South. Drainage flows **away** from Bldg. 8 (FFE 685.50), dropping to curb elevations in the ~681.69 range, and further down to finished grades in the ~680.70 range at the southern property line/retaining wall.\n\n### 4. Oil-Filled Transformer Equipment Drainage Compliance\nBecause the specific micro-grading of concrete pads is not shown on this sheet, a definitive assessment of the pad itself cannot be made. \n\nHowever, looking at the macro-grading of the electrical easement areas where these pads would likely sit (East of Bldg. 6 and South of Bldg. 8), **the general grading plan does successfully direct surface flow AWAY from the adjacent building structures** and toward the perimeter retaining walls and property lines. If oil-filled equipment were placed in these easements matching the surrounding proposed grade, liquid would flow away from the buildings.\n\n### 5. Grading Notes or Special Considerations\nThere are **no specific grading notes, callouts, or details** on Sheet 11 that mention transformers, electrical pads, or special drainage considerations for oil-filled equipment. \n\nThe only general grading note present is located in the bottom left corner under \"Curb Note\", which reads exactly: *\"Grading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\"*"}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778246376621,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":19,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) and provide information about:\n\n1. Transformer pad locations - Are the four electrical transformer pads from Sheet 21 shown or referenced on this utility plan?\n\n2. Underground utility routing near transformers - For each transformer pad location, identify all underground utilities shown in close proximity:\n   - Water lines (W) - what is the distance from pad?\n   - Wastewater lines (WW) - what is the distance from pad?\n   - Storm drain lines (SD) - what is the distance from pad?\n   - Reclaimed water lines (RW) if present - what is the distance from pad?\n   - Any gas lines if shown?\n\n3. Utility crossings and separations - Are there any profile views, depth indicators, or separation dimensions shown for locations where utilities cross or run near transformer pads?\n\n4. Lift stations, cleanouts, or other utility access points - Are there any utility appurtenances located near the transformer pads that might restrict access or require clearances?\n\n5. Any notes about utility separations or conflicts?\n\nPlease use compass directions and building references in your descriptions.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (19)"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246381880,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Find and read all text blocks that contain notes about electric transmission lines, distribution lines, or electric utility clearances and requirements from Austin Energy. Specifically look for: 1) Electric Transmission Notes or Block 16, 2) Electric Notes or Blocks 14, 18, 19, 3) Any requirements about clearances from electric lines, 4) Any required 48-hour notification before work, 5) Any easement or access requirements, 6) Any tree work or trimming requirements near electric lines. Provide the complete text of these notes.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the site plan document provided, here are the exact transcriptions of the text blocks related to electric transmission lines, distribution lines, and electric utility clearances/requirements from Austin Energy:\n\n### **Electric Notes**\n(Located in the middle-left section of the page)\n\n1. \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n2. \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n3. \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n4. \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n5. \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### **Electric Transmission Notes**\n(Located in the upper-middle right section of the page)\n\n1. \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n2. \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7133 to schedule a meeting.\"\n3. \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7133 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n4. \"Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n5. \"Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n6. \"Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n7. \"For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n8. \"24 Hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\"\n9. \"Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n10. \"Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n11. \"Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/powerlines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be mountable curbing.\"\n12. \"Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n13. \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n14. \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\"\n15. \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\"\n16. \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n    any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n    any structures, including, but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\n### **Additional Unnumbered Austin Energy Paragraphs**\n*(Note: Positioned immediately below the numbered \"Electric Transmission Notes\" column. These five unnumbered paragraphs are duplicate text of the numbered \"Electric Notes\" 1-5 listed on the left side of the page, formatted here as standard paragraphs.)*\n\n* \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n* \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n* \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n* \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n* \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1428,"outputTokens":1584,"totalTokens":6397,"reasoningTokens":3385},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Find and read all text blocks that contain notes about electric transmission lines, distribution lines, or electric utility clearances and requirements from Austin Energy. Specifically look for: 1) Electric Transmission Notes or Block 16, 2) Electric Notes or Blocks 14, 18, 19, 3) Any requirements about clearances from electric lines, 4) Any required 48-hour notification before work, 5) Any easement or access requirements, 6) Any tree work or trimming requirements near electric lines. Provide the complete text of these notes."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-1XK9ZsgK0Lhp5cElRk5ugfaZ","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 08 May 2026 13:19:41 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload",