{"level":30,"time":1778246382775,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: (1) Any trees shown on the plan, particularly their locations and proximity to overhead electric lines (marked as \"OHE\" or \"Overhead Electric\"); (2) The locations of tree symbols and their designations (SY, PL, P, M meanings are in the legend); (3) Any trees proposed within or near the transmission easement area (top-right corner area); (4) Tree species if labeled; (5) Any clearance notes or spacing dimensions related to overhead utilities. Provide specific details about tree locations relative to the overhead electric infrastructure.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\"), here are the findings relative to your specific requests.\n\nFirst, to provide context for the tree labels found on the plan, here are the exact definitions from the legend located below the \"KEY NOTES\" on the right side of the page:\n*   \"**SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)**\"\n*   \"**PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)**\"\n*   \"**P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE**\"\n*   \"**M - MITIGATION TREE**\"\n\nHere is the analysis of the requested items:\n\n**(1) Trees shown on the plan, locations, and proximity to overhead electric lines (\"OHE\") & (5) Clearance notes or spacing dimensions related to overhead utilities:**\n*   **OHE Location:** A line designated with the text \"**-OHE-**\" runs horizontally along the extreme bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan, parallel to the property line.\n*   **Trees near OHE:** There is a cluster of three proposed trees located in the bottom-right (southeast) corner of the property, immediately adjacent to the southern boundary.\n    *   Two of these trees are labeled \"**M**\".\n    *   One of these trees is labeled \"**P**\".\n    *   The drawn circular outlines representing the canopies of these three specific trees graphically overlap the line labeled \"**-OHE-**\".\n*   **Clearance Notes/Dimensions:** There are **no** text notes, callouts, or spacing dimensions anywhere on this specific sheet that dictate clearance requirements, planting distances, or restrictions related to the overhead electric (\"OHE\") infrastructure.\n\n**(2) Locations of tree symbols and their designations:**\n*   **\"SY\" (Street Yard Trees):** Located exclusively along the left (western) edge of the property, parallel to what appears to be the street frontage. They are situated within a shaded area designated by key note \"H.2\" (\"STREET YARD\"). Note that several trees in this area bear a combined label of \"**SY/M**\".\n*   **\"M\" (Mitigation Trees):**\n    *   A distinct row of six trees labeled \"**M**\" is planted along the top (northern) property boundary, running from the top-left corner towards the top-right.\n    *   As noted above, three trees along the western street frontage are labeled \"**SY/M**\".\n    *   Two trees in the bottom-right (southeast) corner are labeled \"**M**\".\n*   **\"PL\" (Parking Lot Tree):** There is one tree symbol labeled \"**PL**\". It is located centrally within the upper paved courtyard area, situated between the building footprints and adjacent to parking spaces.\n*   **\"P\" (Parking Buffer Point Tree):** There is one tree symbol labeled \"**P**\". It is located in the bottom-right (southeast) corner of the property.\n\n**(3) Trees proposed within or near the transmission easement area (top-right corner area):**\n*   In the top-right quadrant of the plan, there are designated areas labeled \"**SEDIMENTATION BASIN**\" and \"**FILTRATION BASIN**\".\n*   The row of \"**M**\" (Mitigation) trees running along the northern boundary stops to the west of these basins.\n*   Looking strictly at the area to the east and immediately south of these basins (the far top-right corner inside the property line), there are **no** symbols indicating proposed trees (circles with a center crosshair and an SY/PL/P/M designation) located within this specific zone. There is a line indicating the Limit of Construction (\"**-LOC-**\") running vertically here, and the area east of it appears mostly blank except for fencing (\"H.6\") and part of an existing tree canopy extending from off-site.\n\n**(4) Tree species if labeled:**\n*   There are **no** tree species names (neither common nor botanical names) labeled anywhere on this specific sheet. The trees are identified solely by their functional designations (SY, M, PL, P).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1431,"outputTokens":921,"totalTokens":4700,"reasoningTokens":2348},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on anoth