{"level":30,"time":1778246385134,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VWPBQF7MH13AJ1SHA34D8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important. The vision analysis shows:\n\n1. Trees are proposed along the ENTIRE southern property boundary, directly adjacent to/overlapping with the OHE line\n2. The tree canopies appear to directly overlap or touch the OHE line\n3. NO dimension lines or clearance measurements are shown between trees and the OHE line\n4. Trees near the western edge (Valley View Road area) including near the transformer pad\n5. Various tree symbols labeled as \"M\" (mitigation), \"PL\" (parking lot), \"SYM\" (unclear)\n6. No species identification on the landscape plan symbols\n\nThis is a critical deficiency pattern. The grouping guidance states:\n\nFrom the grouping file:\n- **Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution conductors** = EL-2.1 violation\n- **Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 feet of transmission conductors** = EL-2.2 violation\n- **Large trees (40+ feet) within 25 feet of distribution** = EL-2.3 violation\n- **Large trees (40+ feet) within 50 feet of transmission** = EL-2.4 violation\n- **Trees within transmission easement boundaries** = EL-2.5 violation\n- **Trees within 10 feet of utility poles** = EL-2.6 violation\n- **Trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment** = EL-2.7 violation\n- **Trees within 5 feet of underground equipment** = EL-2.8 violation\n- **Trees within 20 feet of underground equipment lacking root barriers** = EL-2.9 violation\n- **Plant legend/schedule doesn't identify species** = EL-2.10 violation\n- **Large trees not differentiated on plans** = EL-2.11 violation\n- **Clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor** = EL-2.12 violation\n\n\n- **Clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk** = EL-2.13 violation\n- **Trees not shown on landscape plan relative to OHE facilities** = EL-2.14 violation\n- **Trees in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval** = EL-2.15 violation\n\nThe landscape plan has a significant disconnect: Sheet 35 lists specific species like Cedar Elm and Live Oak, but Sheet 31 doesn't link those species to the actual tree symbols shown—just generic circles marked M, PL, or SYM. This creates an EL-2.10 violation since the working landscape plan lacks species identification. I can't verify whether large trees are properly differentiated across the drawings either.\n\nThe OHE line isn't clearly cross-referenced to the plant schedule, making it impossible to confirm species compatibility with utility requirements. There are also no dimension lines showing clearances from conductors, which violates both EL-2.12 and EL-2.13.\n\nTo resolve this, I need to identify which species are planted where, cross-check their utility compatibility against ECM Appendix F, confirm their mature heights to determine if they qualify as \"large trees,\" and measure the actual clearances from the OHE line. I'll start by measuring distances from the southern property line OHE to the nearby trees.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4f0070e-2a45-4059-b037-c9cf1f4aff02","uuid":"5b3a43a2-27d6-4054-88b3-58676b9e1c05"}
