{"level":30,"time":1778246390662,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and identify: (1) The location and routing of overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on the plan; (2) The locations of all proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) and their proximity to overhead electric infrastructure; (3) Any clearance dimensions or notes related to overhead electric clearances; (4) Locations of proposed driveways, parking areas, or sidewalks and their proximity to overhead lines; (5) Any utility poles or electric infrastructure shown on the site plan. Provide specific details about the spatial relationships between proposed structures and overhead electric facilities.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (9)"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246392062,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VWKH4ED3EZW2R6F91BQDS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've gathered initial research on this site plan review for tree clearances from overhead electric lines (grouping EL-2). Let me organize what I've found so far:\n\n**KEY FINDINGS FROM RESEARCH:**\n\n1. **Site Overview:**\n   - Valley View Townhomes - 39 multi-family townhome units\n   - Located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin TX 78704\n   - MF-2 zoning\n   - Site area: 94,203 SF (2.16 acres)\n\n2. **Overhead Electric Facilities Identified:**\n   - ONE overhead electric (OHE) distribution line running along the WESTERN property boundary adjacent to Valley View Road\n   - ONE overhead electric line running along the NORTHERN boundary\n   - The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows the distribution line has transformers stepping down to residential buildings\n   - Distribution line (NOT transmission - confirmed by presence of pad-mounted transformers for residential service)\n   - No voltage specifications provided on plans\n   - Utility poles visible along both western and northern boundaries\n\n3. **Proposed Trees Identified:**\n   From the plant schedule (Sheet 35):\n   - **Shade Trees:** \n     * 2 Live Oaks (Quercus virginiana) - 100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' min height at planting\n     * 10 Cedar Elms (Ulmus crassifolia) - 100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' min height at planting\n   - **Ornamental Trees:**\n     * 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 45 gal., 2.5\" cal., 8' min height at planting\n     * 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 45 gal., 2.5\" cal., 10' min height at planting\n   - **Shrubs & Groundcovers** - various small species\n   \n4. **Critical Gap - Mature Height Data Missing:**\n   The plant schedule only lists minimum planting heights, not mature heights, which creates a compliance problem. UCM § 1.10.10.4 requirements hinge on mature heights, and I need to cross-reference these species against ECM Appendix F to determine if any qualify as \"Large trees\" (40+ ft mature height) that would trigger stricter clearance restrictions. The species designations for utility compatibility also aren't documented on the plans.\n\n5. **Tree Placement Concerns:**\n   Vision analysis indicates trees positioned 5-10 feet north of the northern boundary, which I need to evaluate against the overhead line locations.\n\n6. **Documentation Gaps:**\n   The plan lacks mature height specifications, ECM Appendix F verification for utility-compatible designations, documented clearance measurements from conductors to tree trunks, clarification on whether distances are measured from pole centerline or outside conductor, and any Austin Energy written approval for deviations. Sheet 21 references Sheet 19 for conductor profile details that would be needed to assess actual clearances.\n\nNow evaluating the checklist requirements: EL-2.1 cannot pass because I cannot confirm all trees meet utility-compatible standards without the plant schedule providing UC designations and mature heights to cross-reference against ECM Appendix F. EL-2.2 is not applicable since no transmission lines exist on site. For EL-2.3, I'm unable to determine if proposed trees will reach the 40+ foot mature height threshold that triggers the 25-foot clearance requirement, as the plant schedule only lists planting heights rather than mature specifications.\n\nThe remaining items follow similar patterns: EL-2.4 and EL-2.5 are not applicable due to absence of transmission facilities and easements. EL-2.6 cannot be verified because while trees appear near poles in the site visit, actual distances lack precise dimensioning. EL-2.7 is not verifiable due to unclear spatial relationships between trees and transformer pads shown on the plan. EL-2.8 addresses underground electrical routing but requires further assessment of tree proximity to buried equipment.\n\nFor EL-2.9, verification depends on locating underground equipment relative to trees. EL-2.10 passes since the plant schedule does provide both common and scientific names. EL-2.11 cannot be assessed without specified mature heights to identify which trees qualify as \"large.\" EL-2.12 is not verifiable because the landscape plan lacks dimension lines showing how clearances were measured or whether they reference pole centerlines versus conductors.\n\nEL-2.13 presents a similar issue—trees appear as symbols without dimension callouts indicating whether measurements reference the canopy or trunk. EL-2.14 passes because both trees and the overhead electric line are depicted on the landscape plan. For EL-2.15, no Austin Energy approval documentation is visible, and actual distances need measurement to confirm whether any trees encroach prohibited zones, though visual inspection suggests some may be close to clearance limits. I should review supplementary documents next to check for utility coordination records or approvals.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0303f2e2-ff0c-4b14-bd62-f1e72863d84c","uuid":"a9e96531-ac0d-440b-882c-bb6e968cf5ce"}
