{"level":30,"time":1778246398942,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the grading plan and identify: 1) All utility easements shown on the plan - look for labels or notation indicating electric easements, transmission easements, telephone/utility easements, drainage easements, and any other utility infrastructure; 2) The specific location and width of each electric easement (look for notation like \"5' Electric Easement\", \"7.5' PUE\", or similar); 3) The location of utility poles, if any are shown, and whether they are labeled as transmission or distribution poles; 4) Any indication of whether the overhead or underground electric facilities are transmission voltage (69kV, 138kV, 345kV, etc.) or distribution voltage (12.47kV, 34.5kV, etc.); 5) The location of the southern property boundary relative to the easements and any notation about street frontage easements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided grading plan, here is the information requested:\n\n**1) Utility Easements Shown on the Plan**\nThe following utility, drainage, and related easements are explicitly labeled on the plan:\n*   **North Boundary:**\n    *   \"5' P.U.E. Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   \"7.5' P.U.E. Vol. 69, Pg. 14 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n*   **East Boundary:**\n    *   \"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   \"Greenbelt Access & P.U.E. Easement Doc. 20110419131 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n*   **South Boundary:**\n    *   \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 3498, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.T.s\"\n*   **West Boundary (Street Frontage):**\n    *   \"Wastewater Easement Doc#\" (Document number is cut off/unclear)\n    *   \"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\" (Multiple labels along the western edge; document numbers are cut off/unclear)\n    *   \"Water Line Vault Easement Doc#\" (Document number is cut off/unclear)\n\n**2) Specific Location and Width of Each Electric Easement**\nElectric easements (including Public Utility Easements, which typically encompass electric) are located and sized as follows:\n*   **5-foot wide:** \"5' P.U.E.\" running along the north-central property boundary.\n*   **7.5-foot wide:** \"7.5' P.U.E.\" running along the northeast property boundary.\n*   **5-foot wide:** \"5' Electric Easement\" running along a portion of the eastern property boundary (near Building 6 and the adjacent existing apartment building).\n*   **5-foot wide:** \"5' Elec. Easement\" running along the south-central property boundary.\n*   **5-foot wide:** \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" located in the southeast corner of the property.\n\n**3) Location of Utility Poles (Transmission vs. Distribution)**\nThere are no symbols or labels explicitly identifying utility poles as either \"transmission\" or \"distribution\" on this grading plan. The plan primarily details grading contours, building footprints, retaining walls, and easement boundaries.\n\n**4) Indications of Overhead/Underground Electric Facilities and Voltage**\nThere is no notation on this grading plan indicating whether the electric facilities are overhead or underground, nor are there any voltage indicators (e.g., 69kV, 138kV, 12.47kV) present in the text or labels. The easements only reference volume and page deed record numbers (e.g., \"Vol. 69, Pg. 14\").\n\n**5) Southern Property Boundary Relative to Easements and Street Frontage**\n*   **Easements:** The southern property boundary is bordered by the \"5' Elec. Easement\" and the \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" as transcribed above. \n*   **Street Frontage:** There is no street frontage on the southern boundary. The southern boundary abuts an adjacent lot labeled for single-family residential use (\"Zoning: SF-3-CO / Use: Single Family\"). All street frontage for this site is located on the western boundary along \"Valley View Road\", which features the previously mentioned Sidewalk, Wastewater, and Water Line/Vault easements.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1493,"outputTokens":923,"totalTokens":5494,"reasoningTokens":3078},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the grading plan and identify: 1) All utility easements shown on the plan - look for labels or notation indicating electric easements, transmission easements, telephone/utility easements, drainage easements, and any other utility infrastructure; 2) The specific location and width of each electric easement (look for notation like \"5' Electric Easement\", \"7.5' PUE\", or similar); 3) The location of utility poles, if any are shown, and whether they are labeled as transmission or distribution poles; 4) Any indication of whether the overhead or underground electric facilities are transmission voltage (69kV, 138kV, 345kV, etc.) or distribution voltage (12.47kV, 34.5kV, etc.); 5) The location of the southern property boundary relative to the easements and any notation about street frontage easements."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-SezNsLPkBw6RFFk7rAmHQjFf","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 08 May 2026 13:19:58 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::zhr8z-1778246363412-eb6a077f5711"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided