dings are located in the southern portion of the site. They are the closest structures to the `- OHE -` line that runs along the southern boundary. While exact distances to the wires are not explicitly dimensioned, the southern facades of these buildings face the property line where the OHE routing is indicated.\n\n**3. Clearance dimensions or notes related to overhead electric clearances**\n*   There are **no explicit clearance dimensions** (such as radial clearance arcs or specific setback distances from the wires) shown on the plan for the overhead electric lines.\n*   A review of the \"Site Plan Release Notes,\" \"General Notes\" (if any), and other text blocks does not reveal any specific textual notes regarding OSHA, NESC, or local utility clearance requirements for the OHE.\n\n**4. Locations of proposed driveways, parking areas, or sidewalks and proximity to overhead lines**\n*   **Driveway:** The primary entrance driveway on the west side of the property, labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 433S-2\", is routed directly underneath the north-south `- OHE -` line.\n*   **Sidewalks/Retaining Walls:** A \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" and pedestrian pathways are proposed along the southern edge of the property, running parallel and in close proximity to the southern `- OHE -` line.\n*   **Parking Areas:** The surface parking areas are primarily internal to the site (between the buildings) and do not appear to be situated directly underneath the indicated `- OHE -` lines.\n\n**5. Utility poles or electric infrastructure shown**\n*   **Utility Poles:** Several utility poles are indicated along the `- OHE -` routes. On the western frontage, near the main driveway entrance, there are symbols labeled \"Pole\" both north and south of the driveway (with the southern one indicating a \"Guy\" wire anchor). Additional pole symbols are scattered along the southern `- OHE -` line.\n*   **Transformer Pad:** A \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" is explicitly labeled in the central-western portion of the site, situated south of Bldg. 1, west of Bldg. 2, and adjacent to a \"Tree Well\".\n*   **Easements:** On the far eastern boundary of the site, adjacent to the \"Existing Apartment Building\", there is a labeled \"5' Electric Easement\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1428,"outputTokens":791,"totalTokens":4125,"reasoningTokens":1906},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan and identify: (1) The location and routing of overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on the plan; (2) The locations of all proposed buildings (Buildings 1