ting electrical routing traverse the site. The primary feed originates from the western property line (street side), labeled explicitly as \"Underground Electric Line\". It branches north and south along the western buildings (Bldgs 1, 2, 8) and runs a main trunk line east-west through the center of the site to service the inner buildings.\n*   **Electrical Pull Boxes:** There are several labeled \"Electrical Pull Box\" located along the underground electric lines:\n    *   One is located northwest of Building 1, near the street connection.\n    *   One is located west of Building 2.\n    *   One is located just north of Building 4 (near Unit 401/402).\n    *   One is located immediately east of Building 4, just north of the transformer pad located there.\n    *   One is located south of Building 7, near the main east-west trunk line.\n    *   One is located west of Building 8.\n*   **Vaults:** \n    *   A \"Vault Easement\" is explicitly labeled and outlined with dashed lines surrounding the Electrical Transformer Pad west of Building 8.\n    *   In the far northwest corner of the property line, near a manhole, there is faint text indicating an existing \"AT&T Vault\".\n\n**3. Utility Poles Shown with Approximate Locations**\n*   An Overhead Electric line, labeled **\"OHE\"**, runs along the entire western boundary of the site (street side). \n*   While the explicit word \"pole\" is not written, there are standard circular symbols plotted along this \"OHE\" line (e.g., one near the northwest corner near the AT&T Vault, and others further south along the boundary) which represent the utility poles supporting this overhead line. \n\n**4. Notes About Clearances or Setbacks from Trees or Landscaping**\n*   There are **no explicit textual notes** found on this sheet detailing specific clearance distances or setbacks required between the electrical infrastructure and trees or landscaping. The electrical lines are drawn weaving around the plotted root zones/canopies of the existing trees, but no numeric clearance rule is noted in the general or utility notes.\n\n**5. Reference to Landscape Plan Coordination Regarding Tree Placement**\n*   In the lower-left center of the drawing, there is a box titled **\"Tree List\"**. The text inside this box states exactly: **\"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"** \n*   There are no explicit notes directing coordination between tree *placement* and electrical infrastructure, only the cross-reference to the landscape plan for tree details.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1413,"outputTokens":845,"totalTokens":4589,"reasoningTokens":2331},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you d