{"level":30,"time":1778246451529,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine each of the 5 transformer pads and measure their distances to adjacent features using the 1\"=20' scale shown on the sheet. For each pad:\n\n1. Transformer Pad 1 (NW, near Building 1):\n   - Horizontal distance from pad edge to Building 1 wall\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to nearest parking space edge\n   - Distance to electrical meters/pull boxes nearby\n   - Position relative to driveway/curb\n\n2. Transformer Pad 2 (W, near Building 2):\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to Building 2 wall\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to sidewalk or property boundary\n   - Proximity to any fence or easement boundary\n\n3. Transformer Pad 3 (SW, near Building 8):\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to Building 8 wall\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to property boundary/sidewalk\n   - Whether pad is inside or outside the Vault Easement boundary\n\n4. Transformer Pad 4 (E, near Buildings 4-5):\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to existing retaining wall\n   - Distance to drainage easement boundary\n   - Building proximity\n\n5. Transformer Pad 5 (SE, near Buildings 6-7):\n   - Horizontal distance from pad to existing retaining wall\n   - Proximity to property line/boundary\n   - Distance to adjacent buildings\n\nFor each measurement, provide estimated distance in feet based on scaling from the graphic scale.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" and using the graphic scale located in the top right corner (where the bar indicates 20 feet), here are the estimated measurements and observations for the five electrical transformer pads. \n\n*Note: All distances are visual estimates derived by comparing the gap on the plan to the provided 20-foot graphic scale bar.*\n\n**1. Transformer Pad 1 (NW, near Building 1):**\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad edge to Building 1 wall:** The pad is located just south of Building 1. The distance to the southern wall of Building 1 appears to be roughly **5 to 8 feet** (less than half the 20' scale bar).\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to nearest parking space edge:** There are no striped parking spaces immediately adjacent to the pad. The nearest parking spaces to the east (in front of Bldg 1) appear to be approximately **20 feet** away (about one full scale bar length).\n*   **Distance to electrical meters/pull boxes nearby:** There is an \"Electrical Pull Box\" immediately to the north of the pad, estimated to be within **5 feet**. There are \"Electrical Meters\" located on the west wall of Building 1, estimated to be roughly **10 to 12 feet** away.\n*   **Position relative to driveway/curb:** The pad is situated immediately adjacent to the inner edge of the curved curb/driveway at the western entrance. The distance to the curb line appears to be less than **5 feet**.\n\n**2. Transformer Pad 2 (W, near Building 2):**\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to Building 2 wall:** The pad is located west of Unit 201. The distance to the western wall of the building is estimated to be approximately **8 to 10 feet** (slightly less than half the scale bar).\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to sidewalk or property boundary:** The distance to the inner boundary line labeled \"Sidewalk Easement\" to the west is estimated at **10 to 12 feet**. The distance to the heavy dashed property line further west is estimated at roughly **20 to 25 feet**.\n*   **Proximity to any fence or easement boundary:** The pad sits east of the \"Sidewalk Easement\" boundary. It is situated in an open area between the building and the sidewalk easement, just north of a line labeled \"Underground Electric Line\".\n\n**3. Transformer Pad 3 (SW, near Building 8):**\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to Building 8 wall:** The pad is located west of Unit 801. The distance to the western wall of Building 8 is relatively close, estimated at **4 to 6 feet** (roughly a quarter of the scale bar).\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to property boundary/sidewalk:** Similar to Pad 2, the distance to the inner edge of the \"Sidewalk Easement\" to the west is estimated at **10 to 12 feet**. The distance to the heavy dashed main property line is estimated at roughly **20 feet**.\n*   **Whether pad is inside or outside the Vault Easement boundary:** The \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and an adjacent \"Electrical Pull Box\" are located strictly **inside** a dashed rectangular boundary explicitly labeled \"Vault Easement\".\n\n**4. Transformer Pad 4 (E, near Buildings 4-5):**\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to existing retaining wall:** The pad is located on the eastern side of the property. The distance to the jagged line labeled \"Existing Retaining Wall\" further east is substantial, estimated to be roughly **30 to 40 feet** (1.5 to 2 times the scale bar length).\n*   **Distance to drainage easement boundary:** There is a dashed line indicating a \"25' Drainage Easement\" located east of the pad. The distance from the pad to this easement line is estimated at **5 to 10 feet**.\n*   **Building proximity:** The pad is situated in the gap between Building 4 and Building 5. The horizontal distance to the eastern wall of Building 4 (Unit 404) is estimated at roughly **10 feet**. The distance to the eastern wall of Building 5 (Unit 504) is similarly estimated at roughly **10 feet**.\n\n**5. Transformer Pad 5 (SE, near Buildings 6-7):**\n*   **Horizontal distance from pad to existing retaining wall:** The pad is located on the eastern side of the property, south of Pad 4. The distance east to the \"Existing Retaining Wall\" is estimated to be roughly **20 to 30 feet** (1 to 1.5 times the scale bar).\n*   **Proximity to property line/boundary:** The heavy dashed property line is located just beyond the retaining wall to the east. The distance from the pad to this property line is estimated at **30 to 35 feet**.\n*   **Distance to adjacent buildings:** Similar to Pad 4, this pad sits in the gap between buildings. The distance to the eastern wall of Building 7 (Unit 704) is estimated at roughly **10 feet**. The distance to the eastern wall of Building 6 (Unit 604) is similarly estimated at roughly **10 feet**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1614,"outputTokens":1141,"totalTokens":5135,"reasoningTokens":2380},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine each of