{"level":30,"time":1778246464507,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019CD5KPNx8fKMV3DC2SGRaM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 37 — Landscape Details\n     2→\n     3→Contains landscape details for tree planting, tree protection, and shrubs.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides standard landscape detail drawings for the Valley View Townhomes project. It primarily contains City of Austin compliant specifications for tree planting, tree protection during construction, and general shrub planting guidelines.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   **Tree Protection Critical Root Zone (CRZ)**: Radius = 1ft per inch (12mm per mm) of trunk diameter.\n    11→*   **Tree Protection Mulch**: 150mm (6\") depth inside the protection zone.\n    12→*   **Tree Protection Clearance**: Minimum 1.5m (5') necessary work space; if less, add boards strapped to trunk.\n    13→*   **Tree Planting Pit Size**: 3x the width of the rootball.\n    14→*   **Tree Planting Stakes**: 8' length black painted steel T-post, driven min. 18\" below tree pit.\n    15→*   **Tree Planting Rootball**: Set level to grade or slightly above grade (1/2\").\n    16→*   **Tree Trunk Support**: Arborbrace webbing allowing a maximum 2\" movement in any direction.\n    17→*   **Planting Mulch (Trees & Shrubs)**: 3\" depth organic wood mulch; for trees, keep mulch 6\" away from the root crown.\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 1: diagram — City of Austin Tree Protection Detail**: Illustrates standard fencing and mulching requirements to protect existing trees during construction (Standard 610S-4). READ the block content for specific CRZ calculation formulas and standard watershed protection notes. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the fencing relative to the dripline and building footprint.\n    22→*   **Block 2: diagram — Shrub Planting Detail**: Shows the standard trenching and soil amendment layout for shrubbery. READ the block content for contractor coordination instructions regarding dirt removal and amended soil mix placement. Use VISION to observe the 15\" planting depth and continuous soil trenching layout.\n    23→*   **Block 3: diagram — City of Austin Tree Planting Detail**: Comprehensive cross-section and specification list for new tree installations. READ the block content for extensive text instructions covering rootball preparation, acceptable pruning, hardware specifics (Arborbrace webbing, Stakesafe protectors), and soil settling methods. Use VISION to examine the 4'-6\" stake height above ground, the 3x rootball width pit dimensions, and the rootball elevation relative to the finished grade.\n    24→*   **Block 4: seal — Professional Seal & Administrative**: Contains the Registered Landscape Architect seal (dated 02/13/2026), project title (Valley View Townhomes), and sheet indexing (34 of 35). READ for basic administrative verification.\n    25→\n    26→---\n    27→\n    28→- `block-3.md` — diagram: Detailed drawing showing the requirements for planting a tree in the City of Austin. Includes instru\n    29→\n    30→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    31→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bba534d5-0ed6-41d8-bc2c-fb63a7697ee2","uuid":"331bf12f-25d1-4c13-81c8-ebbf707265ff","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-37/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 37 — Landscape Details\n\nContains landscape details for tree planting, tree protection, and shrubs.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides standard landscape detail drawings for the Valley View Townhomes project. It primarily contains City of Austin compliant specifications for tree planting, tree protection during construction, and general shrub planting guidelines.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Tree Protection Critical Root Zone (CRZ)**: Radius = 1ft per inch (12mm per mm) of trunk diameter.\n*   **Tree Protection Mulch**: 150mm (6\") depth inside the protection zone.\n*   **Tree Protection Clearance**: Minimum 1.5m (5') necessary work space; if less, add boards strapped to trunk.\n*   **Tree Planting Pit Size**: 3x the width of the rootball.\n*   **Tree Planting Stakes**: 8' length black painted steel T-post, driven min. 18\" below tree pit.\n*   **Tree Planting Rootball**: Set level to grade or slightly above grade (1/2\").\n*   **Tree Trunk Support**: Arborbrace webbing allowing a maximum 2\" movement in any direction.\n*   **Planting Mulch (Trees & Shrubs)**: 3\" depth organic wood mulch; for trees, keep mulch 6\" away from the root crown.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — City of Austin Tree Protection Detail**: Illustrates standard fencing and mulching requirements to protect existing trees during construction (Standard 610S-4). READ the block content for specific CRZ calculation formulas and standard watershed protection notes. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the fencing relative to the dripline and building footprint.\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Shrub Planting Detail**: Shows the standard trenching and soil amendment layout for shrubbery. READ the block content for contractor coordination instructions regarding dirt removal and amended soil mix placement. Use VISION to observe the 15\" planting depth and continuous soil trenching layout.\n*   **Block 3: diagram — City of Austin Tree Planting Detail**: Comprehensive cross-section and specification list for new tree installations. READ the block content for extensive text instructions covering rootball preparation, acceptable pruning, hardware specifics (Arborbrace webbing, Stakesafe protectors), and soil settling methods. Use VISION to examine the 4'-6\" stake height above ground, the 3x rootball width pit dimensions, and the rootball elevation relative to the finished grade.\n*   **Block 4: seal — Professional Seal & Administrative**: Contains the Registered Landscape Architect seal (dated 02/13/2026), project title (Valley View Townhomes), and sheet indexing (34 of 35). READ for basic administrative verification.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — diagram: Detailed drawing showing the requirements for planting a tree in the City of Austin. Includes instru\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246466380,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the grading plan and identify: (1) The location and routing of overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on the plan; (2) The locations of finished grades (contour lines or spot elevations) in areas beneath the overhead electric lines, particularly near driveways, parking areas, or retaining walls; (3) Any vertical clearance dimensions or notes relating to overhead electric facilities; (4) The locations and elevations of retaining walls, particularly along the southern boundary; (5) Any profile cross-sections shown or referenced. Provide specific details about elevations relative to electric infrastructure.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Grading Plan (Sheet 11 of 39 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**(1) Location and routing of overhead electric lines (OHE)**\nAn overhead electric line, indicated by utility pole symbols connected by a line labeled \"-OHE-\", runs north-south along the western boundary of the site, parallel to Valley View Road. This line spans the entire western frontage and crosses directly over the two proposed vehicular driveway entrances on the western edge of the property. \n\n**(2) Locations of finished grades beneath overhead electric lines**\nThe OHE line primarily runs along the western right-of-way line. Proposed finished grades (spot elevations) in the immediate vicinity beneath and adjacent to this line at the driveway crossings include:\n*   **Northern Driveway Entrance:** Spot elevations shown at or near the property line/sidewalk easement crossing include 688.40, 688.35, 688.21, 688.14, and 688.00.\n*   **Southern Driveway Entrance:** Spot elevations shown at or near the property line/sidewalk easement crossing include 679.75, 679.25, 679.88, 679.46, 679.32, and 678.82.\n\n**(3) Vertical clearance dimensions or notes relating to OHE**\nThere are no vertical clearance dimensions, minimum height requirements, or specific notes relating to overhead electric facilities or line clearances provided on this sheet. \n\n**(4) Locations and elevations of retaining walls (Southern Boundary)**\nRetaining walls run along the majority of the southern boundary. Specific callouts and Top of Wall (TW) elevations from west to east include:\n*   Near the southwest corner, a label points to the wall stating: **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"**. Adjacent Top of Wall elevations are noted as **\"TW 682.23\"** and **\"TW 684.40\"**.\n*   Moving eastward along the wall, consecutive Top of Wall elevations are provided: **\"TW 684.39\"**, **\"TW 683.84\"**, **\"TW 683.63\"**, and **\"TW 683.50\"**.\n*   In the south-central section of the boundary, a leader line points to the wall with the exact text: **\"Tie into existing Retaining Wall Match existing Wall Elevations\"**.\n*   Continuing east, there are multiple labels reading **\"Existing Retaining Wall\"**, with an additional elevation noted as **\"TW 683.23\"**. \n*   Further east towards the southeast corner, an elevation of **\"TW 678.50\"** is shown on the wall line, ending near an existing grade label of \"EG 668.59\".\n\n*(Note: Retaining walls are also present along the eastern boundary, marked \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" with corresponding TW elevations, but the focus requested was the southern boundary).*\n\n**(5) Profile cross-sections**\nThere are no profile cross-section cut lines (e.g., Section A-A), profile details, or references to other profile sheets shown anywhere on this grading plan. Consequently, there are no profile details regarding elevations relative to electric infrastructure on this document.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1428