{"level":30,"time":1778246485028,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VZXJSSG3QEWBD072600EW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I've provided the structured output with all 15 checklist items evaluated. The findings include:\n\n**FAIL items (2):**\n- EL-2.10: Plant legend/landscape plan does not identify species\n- EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on plans\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE items (13):**\n- EL-2.1 through EL-2.9 and EL-2.12 through EL-2.15: Various issues including lack of species identification, no voltage specification for OHE, no clearance dimensions, no underground equipment overlay, no root barrier specifications, no Austin Energy approval documentation\n\nThe evaluation reflects conservative pass/fail logic where:\n- FAIL is used when the required plan element is simply missing or documentation shows non-compliance\n- NOT-VERIFIABLE is used when evidence is insufficient to determine compliance or non-compliance\n- The burden is on the applicant to demonstrate compliance\n\nThis is a comprehensive evaluation of all 15 checklist items with detailed findings, agent traces showing my reasoning and tools used, appropriate code citations, and actionable remediation guidance for the applicant.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4f0070e-2a45-4059-b037-c9cf1f4aff02","uuid":"af477f1b-d46a-414d-8529-4dcb28f7b975"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246485512,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan (Sheet 31) carefully. Please identify:\n1. What electrical infrastructure is shown on this landscape plan (overhead lines, poles, transformer pads, pull boxes, underground lines)\n2. How clearly are the transformer pads, utility poles, and underground electrical infrastructure depicted?\n3. Are the underground electrical lines clearly marked or noted?\n4. What is the spatial relationship between all proposed trees and the shown electrical infrastructure? Which trees are closest to which electrical facilities?\n5. Are any clearance dimensions dimensioned or called out on this landscape plan?\n6. Is the landscape plan adequate to allow verification of clearances between trees and electrical infrastructure?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (noted as Sheet 28 of 35, despite the prompt's reference to Sheet 31), here are the findings regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**1. What electrical infrastructure is shown on this landscape plan?**\nThe only electrical infrastructure explicitly labeled on this landscape plan is an overhead electric line. This is indicated by a line type containing the text \"**OHE**\" running horizontally along the southern (bottom) edge of the property boundary shown on the plan. Transformer pads, pull boxes, and underground electrical lines are not labeled or explicitly depicted. \n\n**2. How clearly are the transformer pads, utility poles, and underground electrical infrastructure depicted?**\nThey are not clearly depicted. \n*   **Transformer pads:** There are no features explicitly labeled as transformer pads, \"TX\", or similar abbreviations.\n*   **Utility poles:** While the \"OHE\" line indicates the presence of an overhead line, specific utility poles are not clearly identified with labels or distinct recognizable symbols along that line.\n*   **Underground electrical infrastructure:** This is entirely omitted or not distinctly labeled. \n\n**3. Are the underground electrical lines clearly marked or noted?**\nNo. While other underground utilities are clearly marked (e.g., \"**W**\" for water and \"**SD**\" for storm drain), there are no lines marked for underground electric (typically labeled as \"UGE\", \"UG\", or \"E\").\n\n**4. What is the spatial relationship between all proposed trees and the shown electrical infrastructure? Which trees are closest to which electrical facilities?**\nBecause only the \"**OHE**\" line is shown, spatial relationships can only be evaluated against it. Several proposed trees (indicated by circles with crosshairs or central dots) are placed along the southern property boundary directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the \"**OHE**\" line. Specifically, near the bottom right portion of the plan, there are trees (some containing letters like \"M\" or \"+\") that appear to overlap or sit directly next to the overhead electric line in this plan view. Since underground lines and transformers are not shown, spatial relationships to those elements cannot be determined.\n\n**5. Are any clearance dimensions dimensioned or called out on this landscape plan?**\nNo. There are no dimensions, distance callouts, or notes specifying required clearances between the proposed trees and any electrical infrastructure.\n\n**6. Is the landscape plan adequate to allow verification of clearances between trees and electrical infrastructure?**\nNo, this specific sheet is highly inadequate for verifying clearances. It lacks necessary information including:\n*   The locations of underground electrical lines.\n*   The locations of ground-level infrastructure like transformer pads or pull boxes.\n*   Explicit locations of utility poles.\n*   Dimensioned distances between the proposed plantings and the one visible utility line (OHE). \nA reviewer would not be able to confirm if required clearance radii or setback distances are being met using this sheet alone.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1449,"outputTokens":621,"totalTokens":3966,"reasoningTokens":1896},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan (Sheet 31) carefully. Please identify:\n1. What electrical infrastructure is shown on this landscape plan (overhead lines, poles, transformer pads, pull boxes, underground lines)\n2. How clearly are the transformer pads, utili