{"level":30,"time":1778246489538,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":1,"prompt":"Examine the cover sheet and identify: (1) Any notes regarding the 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752); (2) General notes about electric transmission clearances or safety requirements; (3) Any warnings or special notes about overhead electric facilities; (4) The project general notes or disclaimer sections where such safety requirements would typically be listed. Report what safety notes related to electric utilities are (or are not) present.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a thorough visual analysis of the provided Site Plan cover sheet for \"Valley View Townhomes,\" here are the findings regarding your specific queries:\n\n**(1) 48-Hour Notification Requirement to Austin Energy**\nThere are **no notes** present on this cover sheet regarding a 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752).\n\n**(2) General Notes about Electric Transmission Clearances or Safety Requirements**\nThere are **no general notes** on this cover sheet concerning electric transmission clearances or related electrical safety requirements.\n\n**(3) Warnings or Special Notes about Overhead Electric Facilities**\nThere are **no warnings or special notes** anywhere on this cover sheet regarding overhead electric facilities.\n\n**(4) Project General Notes or Disclaimer Sections (Where such notes would typically be listed)**\nThe cover sheet contains two main sections where general project notes, warnings, and disclaimers are located. A detailed review of these sections confirms the absence of electrical safety notes:\n\n*   **Left Column (Below \"Site Development Data\" and \"Legal Description\"):** This section contains numerous environmental, utility, and compliance notes. Topics covered include:\n    *   West Bouldin Creek Watershed boundaries and flood plains.\n    *   Temporary spoils and equipment storage areas.\n    *   Detention basins and water quality ponds maintenance.\n    *   Contractor responsibilities for EPA forms.\n    *   \"Edwards Aquifer Note\" (stating the project is not within the recharge zone).\n    *   Subchapter E of the Land Development Code compliance.\n    *   Potable water system \"lead free\" requirements.\n    *   City of Austin approval limitations.\n    *   \"City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division\" note regarding private fire hydrants.\n    *   Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance compliance.\n    *   Integrated Pest Management Plan.\n    *   \"DCM Waiver Note\".\n*   **Right Column (Below the \"Sheet List Table\" and \"Reviewed By:\" section):** This section contains liability disclaimers and specific construction warnings. Topics covered include:\n    *   Engineer responsibility for plan adequacy.\n    *   Liability disclaimers for Bleyl Engineering.\n    *   Application release not constituting verification of data.\n    *   Requirements for a Texas registered civil engineer to certify the plan.\n    *   Fee in-lieu of parkland dedication requirements.\n    *   Underground storage tank (UST) discovery protocols during construction.\n    *   \"Traffic Control Plan Note\" regarding the right of way management division.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThere are **no safety notes related to electric utilities, overhead lines, or Austin Energy notifications present on this specific cover sheet.** Note that because this is only Sheet 1 of 39 (as indicated in the bottom right corner), these specific electrical safety notes may be located on subsequent pages, such as the dedicated \"General Notes\" sheet (Sheet 3) listed in the Sheet List Table.","provider