{"level":30,"time":1778246506182,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VWWEWMH840N3QKQFVRF4C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F5ARfkZoFfFya3hD9Mkor4","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows Buildings 6, 7, and 8 located directly north of the southern OHE line, clearly within proximity to overhead electric facilities. No clearance dimensions are shown between the building edges and the OHE line on any plan sheet.","reasoning":"The grouping specifies that 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance must be maintained from overhead conductors. Buildings are shown in the site plan without any dimensions from the conductor to the building perimeter. The absence of clearance dimensions combined with the visible proximity of buildings to the OHE line constitutes a deficiency per the reviewer convention that the applicant must affirmatively demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["south and east property boundaries where Buildings 6, 7, 8 are located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings 6, 7, and 8 are shown in proximity to the southern OHE line without any documented clearance dimensions from the outside conductor. No clearance verification provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"A transformer pad is shown on Sheet 21 electrical plan in the area of Building 1. The site plan shows OHE lines on the south and east boundaries, but no radial clearance dimensions are shown from the transformer pad to the conductors.","reasoning":"The checklist requires verification that customer facilities (including transformers) maintain 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary and neutral conductors. Without clearance dimensions on the plans and without confirmation of whether the OHE lines are distribution (voltage <60kV) or transmission (voltage ≥60kV) facilities, compliance cannot be verified from available evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad location west of Building 1"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad shown on site but no clearance dimensions from OHE lines provided. Conductor voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission) not confirmed on plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows 8 proposed buildings with various elevations and roof configurations. No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan set. Sheet 21 guide indicates there are no elevation details showing overhangs, balconies, or canopies relative to overhead lines.","reasoning":"Verification of clearances for building projections requires building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and dimension lines from the conductor to all projections. These sheets are not provided in the submitted site plan. Without this documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all 8 buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed conductor elevations and clearances from building projections (overhangs, balconies, canopies) to overhead conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of the site plan (Sheet 9) and all referenced sheets shows no gas pump canopies or fuel dispensing facilities proposed on this project.","reasoning":"This checklist item applies only when gas pump canopies are proposed. No such facilities are shown on the site plans for this 39-unit residential townhome project.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies proposed on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows the layout of stairs, elevated walkways, and pedestrian paths (including decomposed granite walkways) throughout the site. The plan indicates these features are present but does not provide clearance dimensions from these features to the OHE lines.","reasoning":"Clearance verification for elevated features requires either dimension annotations on the plan or section views showing the 15-foot radial clearance. No such dimensions or sections are provided. Without documented clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["elevated walkways and pedestrian platforms near OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Elevated walkways and pedestrian platforms are shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions from OHE lines are provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows that the OHE lines run along the south and east property boundaries, adjacent to right-of-way. Buildings are set back from the property line but exact distances are not dimensioned relative to the OHE line conductor location.","reasoning":"Verification that buildings maintain both 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances from OHE in ROW adjacent to site requires clearance dimensions from the conductor to building faces. No such dimensions are shown on the site plan or any elevation/section sheets.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["buildings adjacent to south and east property boundaries where OHE runs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings located near OHE lines on south and east boundaries but no clearance dimensions from conductor shown on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of the site plan set sheets 1-39 reveals no building elevation sheets are included. The sheet index in the README shows building elevations are not part of the submitted site plan package. Sheet 21 shows electrical equipment layout but not building elevations.","reasoning":"The code explicitly requires that surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors be included on building elevation sheets to demonstrate that required clearances are met. The complete absence of building elevation sheets constitutes a failure to submit required documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all 8 buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations are not included in the submitted site plan set."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all 39 site plan sheets shows no section or profile views with dimension lines extending from the outer conductor to the edges of buildings or building projections. No such exhibits are provided in the submitted documentation.","reasoning":"Clearance verification requires section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from the outer conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and all projections. These exhibits are absent from the site plan package, making compliance verification impossible.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all building locations in proximity to OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section or plan view exhibits provided showing dimension lines from outer conductor to building edges."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) vision analysis identified a wooden privacy fence (marked H.6) running parallel and very close to the OHE line along the southern property boundary. Sheet 9 site plan also shows fence alignments near the OHE line. No clearance dimensions are shown between the fence and the conductor.","reasoning":"Without clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the fence face, the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified from available plan evidence. The fence location relative to the OHE is noted, but specific clearance documentation is absent.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["wooden privacy fence along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wooden privacy fence is shown near OHE line on landscape plan but no clearance dimensions provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fences are shown on the site plan near the property lines where OHE lines are located. However, individual utility pole locations are not explicitly marked with symbols or callouts on the plans, and fence post locations are not dimensioned relative to any pole locations.","reasoning":"Verification requires either explicit pole location markings on the plan with dimension lines to fence posts, or a survey document showing pole locations. Neither is provided. Without this documentation, the 10-foot clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["fence post locations along property boundaries with OHE"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence posts shown in proximity to OHE but utility pole locations not explicitly marked and no 10-foot clearance dimensions provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md and site plan sheets shows no electrical substation facilities on the property or connected to the project infrastructure. The project uses underground electrical service with proposed transformer pads.","reasoning":"This checklist item applies only when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation is present on or immediately adjacent to the property.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation facilities present on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes reference transmission facilities with specific clearance and documentation requirements (25-foot clearance zones, no digging/grading restrictions, pre-construction meeting requirements). However, the plans do not explicitly identify conductor voltages or transmission vs. distribution line designations.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are identified by Sheet 3 transmission notes and the presence of transmission easement notes on the site plan. However, without explicit voltage labeling and material specifications for any proposed fencing beneath transmission lines, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["transmission easement areas if fencing proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission line easement referenced on site plan but no proposed fencing beneath transmission lines shown. Fence material specifications and grounding details not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows fencing but does not indicate any vehicle barrier fencing specifically positioned beneath or immediately adjacent to overhead electric lines where vehicle contact risk exists.","reasoning":"This item applies only when vehicle barrier posts or fencing are proposed beneath or adjacent to overhead lines for safety purposes. No such specialized barrier fencing is identified on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing beneath overhead lines proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan vision analysis explicitly states that retaining walls are located 'directly over or parallel to several retaining wall segments' along the southern boundary where the OHE line runs. Multiple retaining wall callouts are shown directly along or crossing the OHE line route. No clearance dimensions from the conductor to the wall face are shown on any sheet.","reasoning":"Retaining walls shown directly over the OHE line location on the site plan without any clearance dimensions constitutes a deficiency. The grouping guidelines state that the burden is on the applicant to affirmatively demonstrate compliance. The absence of dimension lines from the outside conductor to the wall face, combined with the visible overlap in the plan view, indicates the requirement is not met.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls along south and east property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown directly over or parallel to the southern OHE line. No clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the wall face provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No Austin Energy substation structures or substation property boundaries are shown on the site plan or identified in the project documentation.","reasoning":"This item applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. No substation exists adjacent to this site.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation adjacent to site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows stairs, walkways, and drainage features but no features are explicitly labeled as 'emergency access structures' such as bridges or elevated platforms. The location and purpose of various elevated structures cannot be clearly determined from the available plan sheets.","reasoning":"Without explicit identification of emergency access structures and without section views showing elevations of these features relative to surveyed overhead conductor heights, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["elevated structures if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Emergency access structures not clearly identified on plans. No elevation sections provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows multiple retaining wall segments throughout the property. No section view sheets are provided showing vertical profiles of the retaining walls with dimension lines originating from the conductor location to the wall face.","reasoning":"Clearance verification for retaining walls requires section exhibits with explicit dimensions from the outer conductor to the outermost edge of the wall. The absence of these section exhibits constitutes a deficiency in submitting required documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls throughout site, particularly south and east boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section views provided showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to retaining wall faces."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows the main driveway crossing the southern OHE line in the southwest corner. The vision analysis explicitly states 'the line directly crosses the main entrance/exit driveway located in the southwest corner' and 'There are **no explicit vertical or horizontal clearance dimensions** labeled on the plan detailing the required distance between the overhead electric lines and nearby site features (such as the driveway...).'","reasoning":"The driveway visibly crosses the OHE line location on the plan. Vertical clearance verification requires either clearance dimensions on the site plan or section profiles showing the finished driveway grade with the lowest point of the overhead facilities dimensioned above it. No such documentation is provided. The grouping notes that driveways crossing overhead lines are a common violation pattern.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["main driveway at southwest corner where it crosses southern OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway shown crossing southern OHE line with no vertical clearance dimensions or surveyed mid-span conductor elevation data provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows parking areas (78 garage spaces and 10 surface parking spaces) distributed around the site. No specific vertical clearance dimensions are provided between parking areas and the OHE lines. The spatial relationship between parking locations and OHE line routes is unclear from plan view alone.","reasoning":"Determining whether vehicle parking occurs beneath overhead lines requires either explicit dimension callouts or section views showing parking pad elevations relative to conductor heights. Without this documentation and without clarity on which parking areas (if any) fall directly under OHE routes, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["parking areas in proximity to OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Parking locations shown but no vertical clearance from OHE lines documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes confirm the presence of transmission facilities on or adjacent to the property. The site plan shows driveways and grading in proximity to the OHE/transmission lines. However, no section profiles showing final driveway grades with a 30-foot vertical clearance dimension from the transmission line are provided.","reasoning":"Verification that roads and driveways maintain 30-foot minimum vertical clearance from transmission lines requires documented grading sections with dimension callouts. These sections are not provided in the site plan package.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["driveways and roads in transmission easement or beneath transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading plan does not show 30-foot vertical clearance dimensions from transmission lines to final grade."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows only local street and driveway access. No state highway or freeway facilities are present. The project does not involve highway or freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures.","reasoning":"This item applies only to highway and freeway projects with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission tower structures. This residential townhome project does not involve such infrastructure.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures present."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows the main driveway crossing the southern OHE line route. Existing utility pole locations are not explicitly marked or labeled with pole symbols on the site plan. No notation indicates whether poles will be relocated, abandoned, or remain in place.","reasoning":"Determining compliance with the 30-foot pole relocation requirement requires explicit pole location markings on the plan with associated relocation notes. Poles are not clearly marked on the submitted site plan. Additionally, the grouping notes that 'utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans,' which may mean poles exist but are not shown.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["driveway alignment where it crosses OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway crosses OHE line but utility pole locations not explicitly shown on site plan. Pole relocation notes not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all site plan sheets (9, 21, 31) and supporting documentation shows no clearance dimensions of any type (horizontal or vertical) are shown between OHE lines and any site features (buildings, fences, walls, driveways). The plans show OHE line locations but not dimension annotations from the conductor.","reasoning":"The grouping specifies that clearance dimensions must originate at the outside conductor location, not from the pole centerline or pole structure. The complete absence of any clearance dimensions on the plans prevents verification of this measurement methodology requirement. This constitutes a deficiency in submitting required clearance documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all areas with OHE lines and proposed site features"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions shown on any plan sheets. Measurement methodology (from outside conductor vs. pole center) cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 notes reference 'Lighting Note' and 'Figure 34' showing required fully-shielded light fixtures. However, the specific locations of streetlight poles relative to the OHE lines are not explicitly shown with dimension callouts on the site plan.","reasoning":"Determining whether streetlight poles are located beneath overhead lines requires either explicit callouts showing pole locations relative to conductor routes or a section view showing vertical clearance. This information is not provided in sufficient detail to verify compliance.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["streetlight pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Streetlight poles not explicitly detailed relative to OHE line locations. No dimension callouts provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows sidewalk improvements throughout the site and along Valley View Road frontage. Existing power poles (if any) are not explicitly marked at the property ends along ROW. The survey legend on Sheet 4 includes 'UTILITY POLE' symbol but poles are not clearly marked on the site plan.","reasoning":"Without explicit pole location markers at property line intersections with sidewalk alignment, it cannot be verified whether poles exist at these locations and whether they are cleared from new sidewalk paths.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["sidewalk alignments at property boundaries along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk improvements shown but existing power pole locations not clearly marked at property line ends."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows trash collection areas for residential waste management integrated into the building designs. No explicit detail drawings show trash enclosure locations or demonstrate clearance from overhead lines. The grouping notes identify enclosed trash areas as a common violation pattern.","reasoning":"Determining whether trash bins raised during service would create contact risk with overhead conductors requires specific clearance dimension callouts or section views showing the maximum height of raised bin arms relative to conductor position. This information is not provided.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["trash enclosure locations within buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash enclosure locations integrated in buildings but clearance from OHE lines not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan vision analysis states the driveway 'directly crosses the main entrance/exit driveway located in the southwest corner.' Additionally, retaining walls are shown 'directly over or parallel to several retaining wall segments' along the southern boundary where the OHE line runs. Both features are shown in spatial overlap with the OHE line route with no clearance documentation.","reasoning":"The grouping explicitly prohibits customer facilities from being installed under or over overhead distribution facilities, 'separate from maintaining clearance distances' and states this is an 'absolute prohibition regardless of clearance distances.' The driveway crossing the OHE line and retaining walls over the OHE line violate this absolute prohibition. Additionally, no clearance dimensions are provided for facilities within the electric easement.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["driveway crossing at southwest corner; retaining walls along south boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway and retaining walls shown directly over/crossing OHE line, violating absolute prohibition on customer facilities under/over distribution lines. No clearance documentation provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water service lines to the buildings. A water meter symbol is referenced in the survey legend on Sheet 4 but specific water meter locations are not dimensioned relative to overhead electric service drop locations on the electrical plan (Sheet 21).","reasoning":"Clearance verification for water meters requires either a utility plan with explicit dimension callouts from service drops to meter locations or confirmation that no service drops pass over meter locations. This documentation is not provided with sufficient clarity.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations shown on utility plan but clearance from overhead electric service drops not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 shows water line routing throughout the site. OHE lines are shown on Sheet 9 along property boundaries. However, no explicit clearance dimensions are provided on the utility plan showing separation between water lines and the overhead electric poles/conductors.","reasoning":"Determining clearance between underground water lines and overhead electric distribution poles requires either explicit dimension callouts or a detailed utility plan with clearance annotations. While both utilities are shown on plans, their vertical and horizontal relationship is not documented.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["water line routing near OHE pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines shown near OHE poles but clearance dimensions not provided on utility plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows building locations throughout the site. The properties are not immediately identified as being within 5 feet of the property line, but without a detailed dimension scale measurement, the exact setback cannot be determined from the plan view.","reasoning":"Verifying whether foundations are within 5 feet of the property line requires either explicit dimension callouts or a scale determination from the site plan. While the scale is provided (1\" = 20'), visual estimation without measurement tools cannot confirm compliance.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["building foundation locations near property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building setbacks from property line not explicitly dimensioned on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows driveways and buildings in proximity to OHE lines but contains no registered surveyor data sheet or mid-span clearance survey documentation. No surveyed conductor elevation data or mid-span clearance measurements are provided in the site plan package.","reasoning":"The checklist item specifically requires that 'a registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances' be provided when overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements. The grouping guidelines emphasize that profile plans must show 'surveyed mid-span clearance data.' This required documentation is absent.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["areas with potential marginal vertical clearance (driveway, buildings near OHE)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey provided showing pole locations and conductor elevations for clearance verification."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows the driveway crossing the southern OHE line. However, no specific angle dimension or crossing detail is provided indicating the angle at which the driveway centerline intersects the OHE line.","reasoning":"Determining whether OHE crossings of roadways are oriented at 90-degree angles requires either explicit angle callouts on the plan or a utility plan detail showing the crossing geometry. This information is not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["driveway crossing of southern OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"OHE line crossing angle at driveway not specified on plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows underground electric infrastructure. Sheet 9 site plan shows OHE lines on boundaries. No section views or crossing details showing the vertical relationship between secondary and primary OHE lines are provided.","reasoning":"Verifying the routing relationship between secondary and primary overhead lines (ensuring secondary is not above primary) requires section views at line crossing locations. These are not provided.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["OHE line crossing locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section views or crossing details showing relationship between secondary and primary overhead lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows signage compliance notes but no marquee signs (large rooftop signs extending above building lines) are proposed for this residential townhome project.","reasoning":"This item applies only when marquee signs are proposed. No such signs are shown on the site plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows proposed transformer pads and underground electrical service but no new utility poles for underground service conversion are shown.","reasoning":"This item applies only when new utility poles are proposed for underground service conversion. The project uses underground service with ground-mounted transformer pads, not new poles.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 includes Lighting Note requiring full cut-off and fully-shielded fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5. Photometric details or landscape plan shows some lighting but specific decorative lighting fixture locations relative to OHE lines are not detailed with clearance callouts.","reasoning":"Without explicit location callouts for decorative lighting fixtures and their clearance from OHE lines, compliance cannot be verified from the available documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["decorative lighting locations if under overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Decorative lighting required to be full cut-off and shielded per lighting notes, but specific fixture locations and OHE clearances not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 Landscape Plan vision analysis states: 'Several tree canopies (both proposed and potentially existing... are drawn directly over or immediately adjacent to the \"OHE\" line along the southern property edge.' The vision analysis further notes 'There are no specific clearance dimensions, distance callouts, or notes regarding required spacing between the overhead electric lines (\"OHE\") and site features.' Additionally, the landscape plan does not show tree species identification mapped to ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list.","reasoning":"The grouping requires: (1) trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution must be utility-compatible (ECM Appendix F 'UC' designation), and (2) within 50 lateral feet of transmission. The site plan shows trees directly over OHE without any species verification against the utility-compatible list. This constitutes two deficiencies: absent species verification and trees placed directly over OHE.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape planting areas along southern property boundary where OHE runs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees shown on landscape plan directly over OHE line. Tree species not verified against ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list. No lateral distance callouts provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations on the electrical plan. No detailed meter location plan or enlarged drawings showing the immediate area around meters with obstruction analysis are provided in the site plan package.","reasoning":"Determining meter access obstruction requires either a detailed meter area enlargement with clearance annotations or explicit notes confirming adequate clear space (30-inch width, 36-inch depth, 6.5-foot height minimum). This level of detail is not provided.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["meter pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Meter locations shown on electrical plan but detailed obstruction analysis and access clearance verification not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows new buildings proposed at distances from the property line sufficient to avoid streetlight pole conflicts. Existing streetlights, if any, are not explicitly shown on the plans.","reasoning":"This item applies when new buildings are proposed adjacent to existing streetlight poles. If existing streetlights are present, they are not identified on the submitted site plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing streetlight locations not identified on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows accessible routes and driveways throughout the site. The survey legend (Sheet 4) includes down guy symbols, but down guy anchor locations are not explicitly marked on the site plan. Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes reference 'down guy anchors' but do not show their specific locations relative to proposed site features.","reasoning":"The grouping explicitly notes: 'electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans.' Down guy wires and anchors may exist but are not shown on the submitted site plan. Without explicit down guy location markings, conflicts cannot be determined. This constitutes a documentation deficiency.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["accessible paths and driveway alignments"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wire locations from existing electric poles not shown or documented on site plan. Potential conflicts with accessible routes not identified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes reference transmission structures but no angled guy anchors from transmission towers are shown on the site plan. Transmission structures appear to exist in easements on property boundaries but angled guy anchors are not identified.","reasoning":"This item applies when angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist on site and require easements. If transmission structures are present with guy anchors, they are not explicitly shown with easement designations on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No angled guy anchors from transmission structures identified on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes reference 'down guy anchors' but these are not explicitly marked on the site plan with accompanying easement designations. The easement exhibit shows electric easements but specific down guy easement boundaries are not delineated.","reasoning":"If down guy anchors from distribution poles exist on the property, they require dedicated easements per the checklist item. Without explicit down guy anchor location markings and associated easement boundaries on the plans, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["down guy anchor locations if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor locations and associated easement boundaries not shown on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows transformer pad locations but does not include vertical section views showing the elevation of the top of transformer equipment relative to the height of overhead electric lines running over the pad area.","reasoning":"Clearance verification for transformers requires section views with vertical dimensions from overhead conductor(s) to the top of transformer equipment. Without these sections, the 7.5-foot vertical clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad shown on electrical plan but no section view showing vertical clearance from overhead lines to top of equipment provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads as ground-mounted installations, not in niche service configurations with covered or recessed installations. No niche structures are described in the electrical plan.","reasoning":"This item applies only to transformers in niche service configurations (covered installations with overhead structures). The transformer pads on this site are open pad-mounted installations.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers are pad-mounted, not in niche configurations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows the site layout with adjacent properties. The grouping requires verification of construction staging areas and equipment operation zones. No separate construction logistics plan or staging area detail is provided showing 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines.","reasoning":"Determining compliance with the 10-foot radial construction clearance requirement (distinct from permanent clearances) requires a site logistics or construction phasing plan. This documentation is not provided in the submitted site plan package.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["construction staging areas adjacent to OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones not detailed on site plan. OSHA 10-foot radial clearance requirement not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes explicitly state: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.' This note is part of the general notes section required to be reviewed prior to site approval.","reasoning":"The checklist requires that 'plans include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.' The submitted site plan includes this requirement in the Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3, satisfying the documentation requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["general site construction requirements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"48-hour notification requirement included in Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set includes no building elevation sheets showing service-mast through-roof installations or roof clearance details. Without building elevations, the specific location and clearance of any service masts cannot be verified.","reasoning":"Verification of service-mast clearances requires building elevation sheets with surveyed roof heights and service mast locations clearly marked. These are not provided in the submitted site plan package.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["building service mast locations"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing service-mast installations and roof clearance dimensions."}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"537eedd0-5217-4f75-802b-fac17558245e","uuid":"d64cfb01-4d5d-434c-8a61-00b0c742ac82"}
