{"level":30,"time":1778246509867,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 2 (Plat) and provide information about:\n\n1. Property boundaries and lot lines - What is the exact boundary of Lot 1? Are property lines clearly delineated?\n\n2. Easements shown - What easements are depicted on the plat? Include:\n   - Electrical easements (type, width, location)\n   - Drainage easements\n   - Water easements\n   - Wastewater easements\n   - Public utility easements\n   - Any other easements\n   \n   For each, note the width, direction, and location relative to the property lines.\n\n3. Right-of-way - Is there a public right-of-way shown for Valley View Road?\n\n4. Scale and orientation - Confirm the scale noted on the plat and the orientation (north arrow if present).\n\n5. Notes and declarations - Are there any legal notes, dedications, or restrictions noted on the plat that affect the property?\n\nThis is the historical plat from the Mecey Subdivision (1975), so these easements may be foundational to the current site.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided plat map (Sheet 2, MECEY SUBDIVISION), here is the information requested:\n\n### 1. Property boundaries and lot lines\n**Boundary of Lot 1:**\nProperty lines are clearly delineated using solid lines for outer boundaries and a dashed line separating Lot 1 from Lot 2. However, distinct linear distance measurements exclusively for the top and bottom boundaries of *just* Lot 1 are not explicitly provided; the measurements shown span the entirety of the subdivision (Lot 1 + Lot 2).\n\n*   **Northern Boundary:** Bounded by a solid line with an overall bearing of \"**S 61° 14' E**\" and an overall distance of \"**419.67'**\" (which spans both lots). A dimension of \"**374.00'**\" is also noted above this line, near the western end.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Bounded by a solid line with an overall bearing of \"**N 61° 42' W**\" and an overall distance of \"**414.35'**\" (spanning both lots).\n*   **Western Boundary:** Bounded by \"**VALLEY VIEW ROAD**\" along a curve. A callout points to a \"**CURVE DATA**\" table which reads exactly:\n    *   \"$\\Delta = 31^\\circ 25'$\"\n    *   \"$T = 20.84'$\"\n    *   \"$R = 74.10'$\"\n    *   \"$LC = 40.12'$\"\n    *   \"$ARC = 40.63'$\"\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Separated from Lot 2 by a vertical dashed line. The length of this specific boundary is not directly labeled on the Lot 1 side, but a dimension of \"**80.65'**\" is noted on the shared boundary line on the Lot 2 side.\n\n### 2. Easements shown\nVarious easements are depicted across the subdivision using dashed lines.\n*   **Public Utility Easements (P.U.E.):**\n    *   **\"15' P.U.E. (Exist.)\"**: Runs east-west parallel to the entire northern property line across both lots.\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E.\"**: Runs north-south parallel to the eastern boundary line of Lot 2 (along Clawson Drive).\n*   **Electrical Easements:**\n    *   **\"Exist. 5' Elec. Ease.\"**: Runs east-west parallel to the entire southern property line across both lots.\n    *   **\"5' Elec. Ease.\"**: Runs north-south entirely within Lot 2, near the eastern boundary.\n*   **Drainage Easements:**\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement (Existing)\"**: Runs generally east-west across the northern portion of Lot 2.\n*   **Water/Wastewater Easements:**\n    *   **\"10' Water/Waste Water Ease.\"**: Runs north-south. It is located just inside the western boundary of Lot 2, immediately adjacent to the dashed dividing line between Lot 1 and Lot 2.\n*   **Other Easements:** No other specific types (e.g., access, landscape) are explicitly labeled with text.\n\n### 3. Right-of-way\nYes, a public right-of-way is shown for Valley View Road.\n*   **\"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\"** is labeled vertically along the western boundary of Lot 1.\n*   Dashed lines indicate the road area, with dimensions \"**15.18'**\" and \"**20'**\" noted between the lot boundary curve and the outer street lines.\n*   The owner's dedication explicitly states: \"...*and I do hereby dedicate to the public all streets and easements as shown hereon.*\"\n\n### 4. Scale and orientation\n*   **Scale:** The scale is explicitly noted under the LEGEND block at the bottom center: \"**Scale 1\\\" = 100 Feet**\".\n*   **Orientation:** A North arrow is present in the upper-middle section of the drawing (to the left of the \"THE STATE OF TEXAS\" text block). It is oriented pointing slightly to the top-left of the page.\n\n### 5. Notes and declarations\nThere are several legal declarations and notes on the plat affecting the property:\n\n*   **Owner's Dedication:**\n    Located in the top right, it reads: *\"THE STATE OF TEXAS COUNTY OF TRAVIS KNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS: That I, Louis Mecey, being the owner of Lot A, Trico Subdivision... do hereby adopt this map or plat as my subdivision of said tract to be known and designated as MECEY SUBDIVISION and I do hereby dedicate to the public all streets and easements as shown hereon.\"*\n*   **City Code Compliance:**\n    Located in the bottom right, it reads: *\"C8c - 75 - 160 This is to certify that Austin City Code Chapter 23.27 of 1954 has been complied with. Surveyed Aug. 20, 1975\"* signed by Forrest B. Scott, Reg. Public Surveyor #399.\n*   **Filing Record:**\n    The plat is filed in the Travis County records. The text on the left side confirms it was filed on the *\"11 day of Dec. A.D. 1975\"* and recorded *\"in the Plat Records of said County in Book 73, Page 76\"*.\n*   **Adjoining Properties Identified:**\n    *   North: \"CORTEZ HEIGHTS - PLAT BK. 64 PG. 13\", \"F.D. BADGER\"\n    *   South: \"O.R. ROGERS\"\n    *   East: \"CLAWSON DRIVE\"\n    *   West: \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\", \"Doris Shropshire\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","us