{"level":30,"time":1778246519077,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012AJhghU9qQeQC5Cp2yJXyi","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3284e2-1747-4d44-a558-2f00d9a24819","uuid":"50676f3c-c7f2-42cb-bf8b-2b90562ae491","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246522538,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":38,"prompt":"Examine the wall plan and identify: (1) The plan view and any overhead electric lines (OHE) or utility poles shown relative to the retaining walls; (2) Any clearance dimensions from the retaining walls to overhead electric lines or poles; (3) The locations of retaining walls, particularly along the southern boundary; (4) Section views showing vertical clearances from wall to overhead lines; (5) Any notes or details about clearances or electric facility relationships. Provide specific details about the spatial relationships between walls and electric infrastructure.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided engineering document (labeled \"WALL PLAN\" for MLAW ENGINEERS), here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**(1) The plan view and any overhead electric lines (OHE) or utility poles shown relative to the retaining walls:**\nThe section labeled **\"PLAN VIEW\"** on the left side of the document shows the layout of \"EXISTING WALL\", \"POND WALL\", and a \"NEW RETAINING WALL\" (indicated by a thick dashed line). **There are no overhead electric lines (OHE) or utility poles shown or labeled in the \"PLAN VIEW\" or anywhere else on this document.**\n\n**(2) Any clearance dimensions from the retaining walls to overhead electric lines or poles:**\nBecause no overhead electric lines or poles are depicted on this document, **there are no clearance dimensions provided** between the retaining walls and such infrastructure.\n\n**(3) The locations of retaining walls, particularly along the southern boundary:**\nThe \"PLAN VIEW\" shows the geometric layout of the new and existing walls, but it does not include a North arrow or property boundary lines to explicitly define a \"southern boundary.\" However, there is a specific note located to the right of the wall section detail that references a southern location. It states exactly:\n> \"ONE 20' SECTION OF NEW FOOTING TO BE INSTALLED AT A TIME. START AT THE SOUTH SIDE OF EXISTING WALL.\"\n\n**(4) Section views showing vertical clearances from wall to overhead lines:**\nThe document includes a primary cross-section view labeled **\"14'-0\\\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\"**. This section details structural dimensions, rebar placement, backfill, and grade levels. **It does not show any overhead lines or provide vertical clearances to them.**\n\n**(5) Any notes or details about clearances or electric facility relationships:**\nThere are no notes that specifically mention clearances or spatial relationships to *electric* facilities or overhead lines.\nUnder the **\"NOTES:\"** section on the right side of the page, item number 2 provides a general directive regarding utilities prior to digging:\n> \"2. OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION.\"\n\nIn summary, this document focuses entirely on the structural engineering and construction details of the retaining walls. It contains no visual or textual information regarding overhead electrical infrastructure or specific spatial relationships/clearances to such facilities.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1417,"outputTokens":495,"totalTokens":3533,"reasoningTokens":1621},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1208488]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. I