{"level":30,"time":1778246531211,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W15T0NB4XPGYS4KTSHG5B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan, I now have sufficient evidence to evaluate all checklist items. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Existing Infrastructure Confirmed:**\n- Overhead electric distribution lines running along western boundary (Valley View Road) and southern boundary of property\n- Multiple utility poles with down guy wires along overhead line routes\n- 5-foot electric easements recorded along property boundaries\n- Underground proposed electrical infrastructure (transformers, meters, pull boxes)\n\n**Proposed Site Features Near Overhead Lines:**\n- Driveway entrance crossing OHE line on western boundary\n- Retaining walls along southern boundary parallel to OHE line\n- Trees with graphical canopy overlaps to OHE line at southern boundary\n- Buildings 7 & 8 in proximity to southern OHE line\n\n**Critical Missing Documentation:**\n- No vertical clearance dimensions for driveways beneath OHE\n- No clearance dimensions from retaining walls to OHE\n- No profile/cross-section exhibits with conductor elevations\n- No clearance dimensions from outer conductor to site features\n- No 48-hour Austin Energy notification note on plans\n- No tree species identification or utility-compatibility verification\n- No detailed down guy locations relative to driveway access\n- Wall Plan (Sheet 38) omits all overhead utilities\n\nNow I'll evaluate each of the 47 checklist items:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e942253-7258-4c80-b1f5-d3905a77aa10","uuid":"ebbe6d4a-3b01-4335-9f72-2e3b428c2e2a"}
