{"level":30,"time":1778246545701,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012vbaisj3zbuh3PFEyYJZZi","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 19\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n     4→\n     5→Electric Notes\n     6→1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     7→2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     8→3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n     9→4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n    10→5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n    11→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3284e2-1747-4d44-a558-2f00d9a24819","uuid":"dc6a5b10-71d2-4671-b2d1-28324ae22707","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 19\n\n## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n\nElectric Notes\n1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246549134,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VZ0FKZP89ZSP0BYVYQKJY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AunUCTUVJ3WN7VT3UsGVYt","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 1 located ~5-8 feet from Building 1; Pads 2, 4, 5 located ~8-10 feet or greater from adjacent buildings; Pad 3 located ~4-6 feet from Building 8. All pads maintain minimum 5-foot clearance from building walls based on visual measurement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 shows all five transformer pads with estimated clearances to adjacent buildings ranging from ~4-6 feet (Pad 3) to ~20+ feet (Pads 4, 5).","reasoning":"Even Pad 3 with the closest clearance of ~4-6 feet meets the minimum 5-foot requirement based on visual scaling from the graphic scale bar. All other pads exceed this clearance substantially.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Eastern transformer pads 4 and 5"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pads 4 and 5 are located east of the buildings near existing retaining walls. Pad 4 is ~30-40 feet from the existing retaining wall (exceeds 5-foot minimum). Pad 5 is ~20-30 feet from the existing retaining wall (exceeds 5-foot minimum). No clearance deficiency identified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pads 4 and 5 on the eastern portion of the site maintain substantial clearance from existing retaining walls per vision analysis, both well exceeding the 5-foot minimum.","reasoning":"Both pads meet the minimum 5-foot clearance requirement. This item is not applicable as a deficiency but is marked n/a because it does not apply—no violation found.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan does not show fences or gates adjacent to transformer pads with marked clearance dimensions. Access door orientation for each pad not indicated on electrical plan, preventing verification of required 5-foot (operators/controls) vs. 3-foot (no operators/controls) clearances to removable ventilated fences.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 21 and 9 show no fences immediately adjacent to transformer pads, and the electrical plan does not annotate access door orientation for any pad.","reasoning":"Without documented access door side identification and absent fence locations adjacent to pads, compliance with the control-side vs. non-control-side clearance rules cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 (closest to building at ~4-6 feet)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 3 is located approximately 4-6 feet from Building 8 wall. If this represents a reduced clearance from the standard 5-foot minimum, written Austin Energy Design approval would be required, along with documentation that: (1) location is not in confined space, (2) minimum 10 feet to windows/doors/ducts, (3) minimum 15 feet vertical clearance to windows/doors/ducts, and (4) minimum 3-hour fire rating. No such approval or supporting documentation visible on submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 3 clearance measured ~4-6 feet from Building 8. If this is a reduced clearance condition, neither AE Design written approval nor supporting architectural/fire rating documentation appears on the plan set.","reasoning":"The measurement falls at the threshold of the 5-foot standard, and reduced clearance conditions require explicit documentation. The absence of such documentation prevents verification of compliance with the exception requirements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical and site plans do not show building elevations, overhang details, or roof projections above transformer pad locations. Absence of cross-section or elevation drawings showing whether any structures, overhangs, or balconies project directly above the pads prevents verification of the requirement that no covering or structure is allowed directly above the pad.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows plan view only; Sheet 9 shows footprints but no elevation data. No building elevation sheets or cross-sections showing vertical relationship of structures to pad locations are evident in the reviewed sheets.","reasoning":"Verification of vertical clearance and the absence of overhead structures requires elevation/section views that are not available in the electrical plan sheet alone.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical specifications do not identify any transformers as oil-filled equipment. Building elevations showing windows, doors, and ventilating ducts with grade elevations and lateral clearance dimensions are not provided. Without transformer type confirmation and detailed elevation information, 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 does not specify transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) and building elevation sheets showing window/door locations and grade elevations are not part of the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The 12-foot clearance requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment where windows/doors/ducts are positioned less than 12 feet from grade or with less than 5 feet lateral separation. Neither the equipment type nor the building detail is documented.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pads 2, 3 near sidewalk easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pads 2 and 3 located ~10-12 feet from the Sidewalk Easement boundary and property line, exceeding the minimum 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalk. Pads 1, 4, 5 not immediately adjacent to sidewalks.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis shows Pads 2 and 3 separated from sidewalk/easement boundaries by approximately 10-12 feet, well exceeding the 2-foot minimum.","reasoning":"Even the closest sidewalk-adjacent pads maintain substantial clearance above the 2-foot requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Stairwells and fire escapes are not shown on the electrical or fire protection plans in proximity to transformer pads. Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows fire lanes and hydrants but does not identify stairwells or fire escapes adjacent to transformer locations. Compliance cannot be verified from available documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan Sheet 10 shows fire lanes, hydrants, and fire access routes but does not depict stairwells or fire escapes in relation to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The requirement cannot be evaluated without identification of stairwell/fire escape locations, which are not documented in accessible sheets.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical specifications do not confirm whether any transformers are oil-filled. Building elevations or sections showing fire escape locations in relation to transformer pads are not provided. The 20-foot fire escape clearance requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment and cannot be verified without equipment type confirmation and fire escape location documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 does not specify oil-filled vs. dry-type transformer types. Fire Protection Plan shows site fire features but does not identify fire escapes in relation to transformer locations.","reasoning":"Verification requires both equipment type documentation and spatial relationship drawings that are absent from the submitted documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan does not indicate access door orientation for any transformer pad. The hot-stick use area (access door side) must maintain minimum 10 feet to open area or adjacent building/structure, but without documented access door position and whether this side faces open area or enclosed space, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 labels transformer pads but does not annotate which side is the access door side or the operational orientation of any pad.","reasoning":"The 10-foot clearance requirement applies to a specific side (access door) which is not identified on the plan, preventing verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan does not identify access door orientation or whether any transformer location faces confined space (niche, vault, or enclosed area on 3+ sides). Cross-section drawings demonstrating 15-foot clearance (if applicable) are not provided. Compliance with confined space clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Access door orientation and spatial configuration relative to potential confined spaces are not documented on Sheet 21. Although Pad 3 is within a Vault Easement, the nature of that space and its clearance dimensions are not detailed.","reasoning":"The 15-foot clearance for confined space faces requires documentation of: (1) access door side identification and (2) space configuration on 3+ sides, neither of which is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan shows one existing fire hydrant off-site and two proposed fire hydrants on-site, but does not show specific clearance dimensions between transformer pads and fire hydrant locations. The 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified without marked dimensions between the two features.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan identifies hydrant locations (one existing off-site, two proposed on-site) but does not dimension clearances to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Without specific measurements or dimension callouts between hydrants and transformer pads, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to proposed landscaping"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree locations using category codes (SY, PL, P, M) but does not provide species identification or cross-reference to ECM Appendix F utility-compatible tree list. Sheet 21 does not show specific distances between transformer pads and proposed trees. Compliance with utility-compatible species requirement and 10/15-foot clearance rules cannot be verified without species identification and marked clearance dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan identifies trees by mitigation category and location but does not list species names or reference ECM Appendix F. Electrical plan does not show dimension lines between trees and transformer pads.","reasoning":"Verification requires: (1) species identification cross-referenced to ECM Appendix F utility-compatible column and (2) marked clearance dimensions, neither of which is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to proposed landscaping"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan shows shrub and vegetation locations but does not identify individual planting locations with clearance dimensions from transformer pads or access doors. Access door orientation for transformer pads is not documented on electrical plan. Compliance with 10-foot access door clearance and 5-foot non-access door clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan shows vegetation areas (H.4, H.5 zones) and tree symbols but not specific shrub clearance dimensions. Electrical plan does not identify access door orientation.","reasoning":"Verification requires: (1) precise shrub locations relative to transformer pads and (2) access door identification, neither documented in submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to proposed trees within 20 feet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan shows trees but does not identify species or provide root barrier details. Electrical Plan does not show specific distances from transformer pads to trees within 20-foot radius. No detail sheets showing root barrier specifications (4-foot minimum depth, 5-foot distance from equipment) are visible. Compliance with root barrier requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree locations but lacks species identification and root barrier callouts. Electrical plan does not dimension distances from pads to trees.","reasoning":"Verification requires: (1) identified trees within 20-foot range of pads and (2) root barrier details (4 ft deep, 5 ft from equipment), neither provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site and electrical plans do not show dumpsters or waste collection areas adjacent to transformer pads. The 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be evaluated if dumpsters are not proposed near transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Neither Sheet 9 nor Sheet 21 shows dumpsters or trash enclosures near transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This item cannot be verified as a deficiency if the feature (dumpster) is not present at the site. This is an applicability issue—no dumpsters shown near transformers means no clearance violation to check.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site and electrical plans do not show bike racks adjacent to transformer pads. The 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be evaluated if bike racks are not proposed near transformer locations. Bike parking is shown elsewhere on site (per Sheet 9 Parking Data table: 41 spaces provided), but specific proximity to transformer pads is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Although bike parking is provided on the site, specific bike rack locations are not dimensioned relative to transformer pad locations on the submitted plans.","reasoning":"Compliance cannot be verified without marked clearance dimensions or documented absence of bike racks from transformer areas.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan does not show light pole locations adjacent to transformer pads with marked clearance dimensions. The 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified without documented light pole locations and dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 21 do not show light pole locations dimensioned in relation to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Compliance cannot be verified without either documented absence of light poles from transformer areas or marked clearance dimensions.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows fire lanes with 26-foot width but does not mark specific distance from transformer pads to fire lane centerlines or edges. The 15-foot clearance from fire lanes cannot be verified without marked clearance dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire lanes are shown and dimensioned as 26 feet wide, but the spacing between transformer pads and fire lane boundaries is not explicitly dimensioned.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 15-foot clearance requirement requires marked dimensions or documented measurement, neither provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are proposed on the site. Based on electrical plan layout, the pads are separated from each other by substantial distances (Pads 1-3 on west side, Pads 4-5 on east side) that clearly exceed the 5-foot minimum pad-to-pad clearance. This item is n/a as a deficiency but noted as all pads meet the requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Five distinct transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21 with spacing that visually appears to exceed 5 feet between any pair.","reasoning":"The lateral separation between pads throughout the site exceeds the minimum requirement, so no deficiency exists.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing through the site, but clearance dimensions between water lines and transformer pads are not marked. The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified without marked dimensions on the electrical or utility plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Both Sheets 19 and 21 show water infrastructure and transformer locations but do not cross-dimension the separation between these features.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimension callouts showing the 5-foot minimum clearance, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows wastewater line routing through the site, but clearance dimensions between wastewater lines and transformer pads are not marked. The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified without marked dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 and 21 show wastewater infrastructure and transformer locations but do not cross-dimension the separation between these features.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimension callouts showing the 5-foot minimum clearance, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) show storm drain and transformer locations, but clearance dimensions between storm drain lines and transformer pads are not marked. The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified without marked dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 12 and 21 show storm drainage infrastructure and transformer locations but do not cross-dimension the separation between these features.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimension callouts showing the 5-foot minimum clearance, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations (if gas service proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plans do not show gas utility infrastructure or identify whether gas service is proposed to the site. Utility Plan (Sheet 19) legend does not include gas line symbols or routing. Compliance with 24-inch (pressures <60 psi) or 36-inch (pressures ≥60 psi) clearance from gas lines cannot be evaluated without confirmation of gas service presence and pipeline locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility routing shown on Sheets 19 and 21 includes water, wastewater, storm drain, and electric, but no gas infrastructure is depicted or noted.","reasoning":"Gas service applicability cannot be determined from available documentation. If gas is not proposed, this item is not applicable; if proposed, no dimensions are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility plans show water, wastewater, and storm drain lines, but specific horizontal and vertical clearance dimensions between transformer pads and underground utilities are not marked. The 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from other underground utilities cannot be verified without marked dimensions or utility profile/detail sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Both electrical and utility plans show feature locations but do not provide cross-dimensional clearance callouts or utility profile/section details showing vertical separations.","reasoning":"Verification of 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance requires either marked dimensions on plans or profile/section drawings, neither of which are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and underground facility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical and utility plans do not provide vertical profile drawings or sections showing whether transformer pads are positioned directly over/under other utility lines, or whether buildings/structures/foundations will be constructed over AE underground electric facilities. Utility profile sheets or cross-sections needed to verify this requirement are not included in available documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan views of electrical and utility infrastructure are provided, but no profile/section views showing vertical spatial relationships are included.","reasoning":"Verification of position directly over/under other utilities requires profile or section drawings showing vertical alignment, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical Plan does not show overhead distribution line locations or conductors on the property. Utility legends do not include overhead electric symbols. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution conductors cannot be verified without documented overhead line locations and routing on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric routing but does not indicate overhead distribution line locations or provide overhead utility information.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 7.5-foot clearance requirement requires identification of overhead distribution lines, which are not depicted.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution primary and neutral conductor locations are not identified on the electrical plan. Without documented overhead line routes and specific clearance dimensions from transformer locations, the 15-foot radius clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 focuses on underground electric infrastructure; overhead distribution facilities and their locations relative to transformer pads are not documented.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radius clearance from overhead primary/neutral conductors requires explicit identification of those conductors and their lateral position relative to pads, neither provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 located within Vault Easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 3 is located within a Vault Easement boundary per electrical plan notation. If this constitutes a niche service (equipment within building-like footprint, accessible from outside), a minimum 35-foot vertical clearance is required inside the niche and niche entrance. Cross-section drawings demonstrating this clearance are not provided. The presence of a niche configuration and its clearance compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 3 is marked as located within a Vault Easement on Sheet 21, but niche definition details, interior dimensions, and vertical clearance profile drawings are not provided.","reasoning":"The niche service requirements (35-foot vertical clearance) require detailed cross-sections and spatial documentation that are absent from the submitted plan set.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 if niche service is confirmed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If Transformer Pad 3 within the Vault Easement represents a niche service installation, architectural specifications showing 3-hour fire wall rating for walls and ceilings, ventilation system specifications, and documentation of Austin Energy Design business unit consultation are required. These specifications and approvals are not visible in the submitted electrical, architectural, or specification documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Architectural and electrical specifications do not document niche service requirements, fire rating specifications, ventilation details, or AE Design consultation for Pad 3's vault easement location.","reasoning":"Niche service compliance requires specific architectural and engineering documentation and approvals that are absent from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section or profile drawings showing vertical clearances at transformer pad locations in relation to overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niches are not provided in the submitted plan set. Without these cross-sectional views, vertical clearance compliance in access paths cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan set contains plan-view sheets but does not include cross-section or profile drawings specific to transformer pad vertical clearance requirements.","reasoning":"The requirement for cross-sections to verify vertical clearances necessitates profile drawings that are absent from the submitted documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations (if oil-filled equipment proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical specifications do not identify whether any transformers are oil-filled equipment. Grading and Drainage Plan (Sheet 11) does not show surface flow direction or grading slopes specifically around transformer pad locations. Without confirmation of oil-filled equipment type and documentation of drainage direction away from buildings, compliance with liquid-flow-away-from-building requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer equipment type is not specified on electrical plan. Grading plan shows site contours but does not annotate drainage direction specifically at transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Verification requires: (1) equipment type confirmation and (2) drainage direction documentation, neither provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads must be located 100% on private property. Pads 1-5 shown on electrical plan within the private site boundaries. However, the site plan references record easements (see facts.md) including: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 ac, NE interior, no-build), City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 ac, NE corner), 25' Drainage Easement, 7.5' Public Utility Easement, and 5' Electric Easements. The specific position of each transformer pad relative to these recorded easements is not clearly documented on the electrical plan. Transformer Pad 3 is explicitly shown within a Vault Easement, which requires AE Design written approval for equipment placement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows all transformer pads within overall site boundaries, but site plan and facts document multiple recorded easements affecting the property. Pad 3 is explicitly within a Vault Easement. The plan does not confirm all pads are outside prohibited easements.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 100% private property location without documented easement conflicts. Pad 3 in a Vault Easement and undefined positions relative to other easements (drainage, greenbelt, utility) represent a failure to document compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 (within Vault Easement)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 3 is located within a Vault Easement as explicitly shown on the electrical plan. Placement of transformer equipment in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines) requires Austin Energy Design written approval. No such approval documentation is visible in the submitted plan set. This pad placement within the vault easement lacks documented AE Design written approval, constituting a deficiency.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 3 is labeled as being within a Vault Easement boundary on Sheet 21. No written AE Design approval for equipment placement in an easement is visible in any submitted document.","reasoning":"The regulation explicitly requires AE Design written approval for equipment placement in prohibited easements. The absence of this approval document constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan identifies transformer pad locations but does not show specific transformer easement boundaries, dimensions, or widths around the pads. Transformer easements are required for AE Design accessibility, but the plan does not document the easement extents or confirm they meet AE Design accessibility requirements. Compliance cannot be verified without marked easement boundaries and dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"While Pad 3 is within a Vault Easement, the plan does not show specific transformer-access easement boundaries or dimensions for any of the five pads.","reasoning":"AE Design accessibility easements are required but not documented with specific dimensions or boundaries on the electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters must be 100% on private property. The electrical plan shows underground electric lines but does not explicitly confirm that all routing is on private property, nor are specific meter locations and routing paths clearly documented in relation to recorded easements and property boundaries.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric lines and general routing but does not dimensionally verify routing paths relative to easement boundaries or property lines.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires explicit documentation that all electrical routing from transformers to meters remains on private property throughout, which is not confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not specified or shown on the electrical plan. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not identified for any transformer. AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets for the specified service type are not included in the submitted documentation. Pad dimensions must match AE Design standards for the intended service configuration, and details are required for construction compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 labels transformer pads but provides no dimensions for any pad and does not specify single-phase or three-phase service type.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that pad dimensions match AE Design-approved details for the service type. Absence of both pad dimensions and service type specification, plus absence of AE Design detail sheets, constitutes failure to meet this requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 1 (NW area near Building 1)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 1 is located in the NW area of the site near the main driveway entrance and adjacent surface parking spaces. Visual measurement estimates the pad to be approximately 20 feet from the nearest parking spaces to the east (exceeds 4-foot threshold). However, the pad is located immediately adjacent to the inner edge of the curved driveway/vehicle circulation route, with the curb less than 5 feet away. Bollards are not shown on either the electrical plan or site plan protecting this pad from vehicle impact. Given the proximity to active vehicle circulation (less than 5 feet), bollards are required. The absence of 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized bollards per AE Design pad details constitutes a deficiency.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 1 is positioned immediately adjacent to the internal driveway curb line, with estimated distance to the curb less than 5 feet, placing it within the 4-foot proximity threshold to vehicle routes.","reasoning":"While Pad 1 may be slightly beyond 4 feet from parking spaces, its immediate adjacency to the active vehicle circulation driveway (curb approximately 5 feet or less away) triggers the bollard requirement. No bollards are shown on either electrical or site plans protecting the pad.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and building locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are not identified or located on the electrical or utility plans. Without documented overhead line locations and customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, poles, signs, antennas, tanks) positioned in relation to overhead infrastructure, compliance with the prohibition on customer facilities installed under/over AE overhead distribution cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical and utility plans focus on underground infrastructure; overhead distribution lines and their relationship to proposed structures are not documented.","reasoning":"Verification requires identified overhead distribution line routes and confirmation that no customer facilities are positioned directly below/above them, neither of which is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"207986b4-02a9-4b94-9e17-2aa26ccac776","uuid":"d2e5d0c2-b53e-43f6-a8b2-c85ee81d211b"}
