{"level":30,"time":1778246553122,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and provide information about:\n\n1. Parking layout - Where are the parking areas located? Are they surface parking or garage parking? What are the parking drive aisles?\n\n2. Transformer pads from Sheet 21 - Can you identify the four electrical transformer pads on this plan? If shown, describe their location relative to:\n   - Parking areas\n   - Buildings\n   - Driveways\n   - Property boundaries\n   - Fire lanes\n\n3. Distances from transformers to parking - Are there any transformer pads located within 4 feet of parking areas? This would require bollard protection per the electrical code.\n\n4. Retaining walls - Where are retaining walls located? Are any transformer pads near retaining walls?\n\n5. Fences - Are there fences or gates shown? Are they near transformer locations?\n\n6. Bollards - Are bollards shown anywhere on the site plan? \n\nPlease be specific about compass directions and distances.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan), here is the information requested:\n\n**1. Parking Layout**\n*   **Location & Type:** According to the \"Parking Data\" table on the right side of the plan, the site provides \"10 Surface/ 78 Garage\" spaces for \"Land Use: Residential\". Visually, the parking is primarily integrated into the residential buildings. The plan shows individual driveways leading to what correspond to garage spaces for each unit (e.g., Units 101-104, 201-206, etc.).\n*   **Drive Aisles:** The main drive aisle enters from the west street via a \"Construct Type II Driveway\" and branches out internally, meandering between the three rows of buildings (Buildings 1, 3, 5 to the north; Buildings 2, 4 in the center; Buildings 8, 7, 6 to the south) to provide access to the individual unit driveways/garages.\n\n**2. Transformer Pads**\n*   **Identification:** I can only definitively identify **one** electrical transformer pad explicitly labeled on this plan. The prompt mentions four, but only one bears a clear label. It is tagged as **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"**.\n*   **Location:**\n    *   It is located on the far **west** side of the property.\n    *   **Relative to Parking/Driveways:** It is situated south of the main entrance \"Construct Type II Driveway\" and west of the driveway for Building 8.\n    *   **Relative to Buildings:** It is west of Building 8 and southwest of Building 1.\n    *   **Relative to Property Boundaries:** It is near the western property line.\n    *   **Relative to Fire Lanes:** No dedicated fire lanes are explicitly shaded or labeled near it, but it sits adjacent to the main entry drive aisle.\n    *   It is situated within an area labeled \"Tree Well / need to look up approx. detail\".\n\n**3. Distances from Transformers to Parking**\n*   Based on the single identifiable \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" on the west side, it appears to be located in a landscaped area (\"Tree Well\") and set back from the adjacent main entry drive aisle and unit driveways. Utilizing the provided \"Scale 1\" = 20'\", the distance from the pad to the closest paved driveway edge appears visually to be greater than 4 feet, as it is separated by a walkway (\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\") and landscaping space. \n\n**4. Retaining Walls**\n*   **Locations:** Retaining walls are located prominently along the perimeter of the site:\n    *   **North/Northeast:** Around the detention pond (\"Concrete Retaining Wall\", \"End Concrete Retaining Wall\").\n    *   **East:** Along the eastern property line behind Buildings 5 and 6 (\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\", \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\").\n    *   **South:** Running along the southern property line (\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\", \"Concrete Retaining Wall\", \"End Concrete Retaining Wall Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\").\n*   **Proximity to Transformer:** The single identified transformer pad on the west side is **not** located near any of these retaining walls.\n\n**5. Fences**\n*   **Locations:** Fencing is indicated in several areas:\n    *   A **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** surrounds the \"Detention Pond\" in the northeast corner.\n    *   Line types indicating a fence (marked with \"x-x-x\") run along the northern, eastern, and southern property boundaries, with a specific label pointing to a **\"Wood Fence\"** on the eastern boundary.\n    *   A **\"2' Pond Access Gates\"** is labeled just north of Building 3.\n*   **Proximity to Transformer:** The identified transformer pad on the west side is not adjacent to the marked perimeter wood fences or pond fences.\n\n**6. Bollards**\n*   Yes, bollards are shown on the site plan. There are two specific labels for them:\n    *   **\"Bollard (Typ.)\"**: Located on the eastern side of the property, between Building 4 and Building 5, positioned at the end of the drive aisle near Units 404/405/504.\n    *   **\"Bollard (Typ.)\"**: Located slightly south of the first one, east of Building 7, positioned at the end of the drive aisle near Unit 705.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1511,"outputTokens":972,"totalTokens":6305,"reasoningTokens":3822},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and provide information about:\n\n1. Parking layout - Where are the parking areas located? Are they surface parking or garage parking? What are the parking drive aisles?\n\n2. Transformer pads from Sheet 21 - Can you identify the four electrical transformer pads on this plan? If shown, describe their location relative to:\n   - Parking areas\n   - Buildings\n   - Driveways\n   - Property boundaries\n   - Fire lanes\n\n3. Distances from transformers to parking - Are there any transformer pads located within 4 feet of parking areas? This would require bollard protection per the electrical code.\n\n4. Retaining walls - Where are retaining walls located? Are any transformer pads near retaining walls?\n\n5. Fences - Are there fences or gates shown? Are they near transformer locations?\n\n6. Bollards - Are bollards shown anywhere on the site plan? \n\nPlease be specific about compass directions and distances."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"ai