ormer pads are proposed on the site. Based on electrical plan layout, the pads are separated from each other by substantial distances (Pads 1-3 on west side, Pads 4-5 on east side) that clearly exceed the 5-foot minimum pad-to-pad clearance. This item is n/a as a deficiency but noted as all pads meet the requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Five distinct transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21 with spacing that visually appears to exceed 5 feet between any pair.","reasoning":"The lateral separation between pads throughout the site exceeds the minimum requirement, so no deficiency exists.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing through the site, but clearance dimensions between water lines and transformer pads are not marked. The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified without marked dimensions on the electrical or utility plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Both Sheets 19 and 21 show water infrastructure and transformer locations but do not cross-dimension the separation between these features.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimension callouts showing the 5-foot minimum clearance, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows wastewater line routing through the site, but clearance dimensions between wastewater lines and transformer pads are not marked. The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified without marked dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 and 21 show wastewater infrastructure and transformer locations but do not cross-dimension the separation between these features.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimension callouts showing the 5-foot minimum clearance, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) show storm drain and transformer locations, but clearance dimensions between storm drain lines and transformer pads are not marked. The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified without marked dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 12 and 21 show storm drainage infrastructure and transformer locations but do not cross-dimension the separation between these features.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimension callouts showing the 5-foot minimum clearance, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations (if gas service proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plans do not show gas utility infrastructure or identify whether gas service is proposed to the site. Utility Plan (Sheet 19) legend does not include gas line symbols or routing. Compliance with 24-inch (pressures <60 psi) or 36-inch (pressures ≥60 psi) clearance from gas lines cannot be evaluated without confirmation of gas service presence and pipeline locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility routing shown on Sheets 19 and 21 includes water, wastewater, storm drain, and electric, but no gas infrastructure is depicted or noted.","reasoning":"Gas service applicability cannot be determined from available documentation. If gas is not proposed, this item is not applicable; if proposed, no dimensions are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility plans show water, wastewater, and storm drain lines, but specific horizontal and vertical clearance dimensions between transformer pads and underground utilities are not marked. The 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from other underground utilities cannot be verified without marked dimensions or utility profile/detail sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Both electrical and utility plans show feature locations but do not provide cross-dimensional clearance callouts or utility profile/section details showing vertical separations.","reasoning":"Verification of 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance requires either marked dimensions on plans or profile/section drawings, neither of which are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and underground facility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical and utility plans do not provide vertical profile drawings or sections showing whether transformer pads are positioned directly over/under other utility lines, or whether buildings/structures/foundations will be constructed over AE underground electric facilities. Utility profile sheets or cross-sections needed to verify this requirement are not included in available documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan views of electrical and utility infrastructure are provided, but no profile/section views showing vertical spatial relationships are included.","reasoning":"Verification of position directly over/under other utilities requires profile or section drawings showing vertical alignment, which are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical Plan does not show overhead distribution line locations or conductors on the property. Utility legends do not include overhead electric symbols. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution conductors cannot be verified without documented overhead line locations and routing on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric routing but does not indicate overhead distribution line locations or provide overhead utility information.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 7.5-foot clearance requirement requires identification of overhead distribution lines, which are not depicted.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution primary and neutral conductor locations are not identified on the electrical plan. Without documented overhead line routes and specific clearance dimensions from transformer locations, the 15-foot radius clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 focuses on underground electric infrastructure; overhead distribution facilities and their locations relative to transformer pads are not documented.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radius clearance from overhead primary/neutral conductors requires explicit identification of those conductors and their lateral position relative to pads, neither provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 located within Vault Easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 3 is located within a Vault Easement boundary per electrical plan notation. If this constitutes a niche service (equipment within building-like footprint, accessible from outside), a minimum 35-foot vertical clearance is required inside the niche and niche entrance. Cross-section drawings demonstrating this clearance are not provided. The presence of a niche configuration and its clearance compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 3 is marked as located within a Vault Easement on Sheet 21, but niche definition details, interior dimensions, and vertical clearance profile drawings are not provided.","reasoning":"The niche service requirements (35-foot vertical clearance) require detailed cross-sections and spatial documentation that are absent from the submitted plan set.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 if niche service is confirmed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If Transformer Pad 3 within the Vault Easement represents a niche service installation, architectural specifications showing 3-hour fire wall rating for walls and ceilings, ventilation system specifications, and documentation of Austin Energy Design business unit consultation are required. These specifications and approvals are not visible in the submitted electrical, architectural, or specification documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Architectural and electrical specifications do not document niche service requirements, fire rating specifications, ventilation details, or AE Design consultation for Pad 3's vault easement location.","reasoning":"Niche service compliance requires specific architectural and engineering documentation and approvals that are absent from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section or profile drawings showing vertical clearances at transformer pad locations in relation to overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niches are not provided in the submitted plan set. Without these cross-sectional views, vertical clearance compliance in access paths cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan set contains plan-view sheets but does not include cross-section or profile drawings specific to transformer pad vertical clearance requirements.","reasoning":"The requirement for cross-sections to verify vertical clearances necessitates profile drawings that are absent from the submitted documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations (if oil-filled equipment proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical specifications do not identify whether any transformers are oil-filled equipment. Grading and Drainage Plan (Sheet 11) does not show surface flow direction or grading slopes specifically around transformer pad locations. Without confirmation of oil-filled equipment type and documentation of drainage direction away from buildings, compliance with liquid-flow-away-from-building requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformer equipment type is not specified on electrical plan. Grading plan shows site contours but does not annotate drainage direction specifically at transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Verification requires: (1) equipment type confirmation and (2) drainage direction documentation, neither provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads must be located 100% on private property. Pads 1-5 shown on electrical plan within the private site boundaries. However, the site plan references record easements (see facts.md) including: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 ac, NE interior, no-build), City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 ac, NE corner), 25' Drainage Easement, 7.5' Public Utility Easement, and 5' Electric Easements. The specific position of each transformer pad relative to these recorded easements is not clearly documented on the electrical plan. Transformer Pad 3 is explicitly shown within a Vault Easement, which requires AE Design written approval for equipment placement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows all transformer pads within overall site boundaries, but site plan and facts document multiple recorded easements affecting the property. Pad 3 is explicitly within a Vault Easement. The plan does not confirm all pads are outside prohibited easements.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 100% private property location without documented easement conflicts. Pad 3 in a Vault Easement and undefined positions relative to other easements (drainage, greenbelt, utility) represent a failure to document compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 (within Vault Easement)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 3 is located within a Vault Easement as explicitly shown on the electrical plan. Placement of transformer equipment in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines) requires Austin Energy Design written approval. No such approval documentation is visible in the submitted plan set. This pad placement within the vault easement lacks documented AE Design written approval, constituting a deficiency.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 3 is labeled as being within a Vault Easement boundary on Sheet 21. No written AE Design approval for equipment placement in an easement is visible in any submitted document.","reasoning":"The regulation explicitly requires AE Design written approval for equipment placement in prohibited easements. The absence of this approval document constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan identifies transformer pad locations but does not show specific transformer easement boundaries, dimensions, or widths around the pads. Transformer easements are required for AE Design accessibility, but the plan does not document the easement extents or confirm they meet AE Design accessibility requirements. Compliance cannot be verified without marked easement boundaries and dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"While Pad 3 is within a Vault Easement, the plan does not show specific transformer-access easement boundaries or dimensions for any of the five pads.","reasoning":"AE Design accessibility easements are required but not documented with specific dimensions or boundaries on the electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters must be 100% on private property. The electrical plan shows underground electric lines but does not explicitly confirm that all routing is on private property, nor are specific meter locations and routing paths clearly documented in relation to recorded easements and property boundaries.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric lines and general routing but does not dimensionally verify routing paths relative to easement boundaries or property lines.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires explicit documentation that all electrical routing from transformers to meters remains on private property throughout, which is not confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not specified or shown on the electrical plan. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not identified for any transformer. AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets for the specified service type are not included in the submitted documentation. Pad dimensions must match AE Design standards for the intended service configuration, and details are required for construction compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 labels transformer pads but provides no dimensions for any pad and does not specify single-phase or three-phase service type.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that pad dimensions match AE Design-approved details for the service type. Absence of both pad dimensions and service type specification, plus absence of AE Design detail sheets, constitutes failure to meet this requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 1 (NW area near Building 1)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 1 is located in the NW area of the site near the main driveway entrance and adjacent surface parking spaces. Visual measurement estimates the pad to be approximately 20 feet from the nearest parking spaces to the east (exceeds 4-foot threshold). However, the pad is located immediately adjacent to the inner edge of the curved driveway/vehicle circulation route, with the curb less than 5 feet away. Bollards are not shown on either the electrical plan or site plan protecting this pad from vehicle impact. Given the proximity to active vehicle circulation (less than 5 feet), bollards are required. The absence of 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized bollards per AE Design pad details constitutes a deficiency.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pad 1 is positioned immediately adjacent to the internal driveway curb line, with estimated distance to the curb less than 5 feet, placing it within the 4-foot proximity threshold to vehicle routes.","reasoning":"While Pad 1 may be slightly beyond 4 feet from parking spaces, its immediate adjacency to the active vehicle circulation driveway (curb approximately 5 feet or less away) triggers the bollard requirement. No bollards are shown on either electrical or site plans protecting the pad.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and building locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are not identified or located on the electrical or utility plans. Without documented overhead line locations and customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, poles, signs, antennas, tanks) positioned in relation to overhead infrastructure, compliance with the prohibition on customer facilities installed under/over AE overhead distribution cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical and utility plans focus on underground infrastructure; overhead distribution lines and their relationship to proposed structures are not documented.","reasoning":"Verification requires identified overhead distribution line routes and confirmation that no customer facilities are positioned directly below/above them, neither of which is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"405145e0-a585-4854-b0b1-f246176e0bfd"}
