{"level":30,"time":1778246609021,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Re-examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) in detail and focus specifically on:\n\n1. EXACT locations of all four transformer pads - list each one with:\n   - Compass direction on site (NW, W, N, E, S, etc.)\n   - Which buildings are nearby\n   - Specific unit numbers if labeled (e.g., near Unit 101)\n\n2. For each transformer pad, measure or estimate the clearance distance (in feet, using the 1\"=20' scale) from the pad to:\n   - The nearest building edge\n   - The nearest parking area or driveway\n   - The nearest property line\n   - The nearest fire lane\n\n3. Electrical specifications:\n   - Is there any text, label, or note that indicates:\n     - Single-phase or three-phase service?\n     - Oil-filled or dry-type transformer?\n     - Service capacity/size?\n     - Any reference to Austin Energy (AE) Design standard details?\n\n4. Underground utilities shown near transformers:\n   - Are there water lines (W), wastewater lines (WW), storm drain lines (SD), or other utilities shown crossing or running near the pads?\n   - Can you estimate clearance distances between pads and these utilities?\n\n5. Easements or access:\n   - Are there any property boundaries, easements, or access paths marked near the transformers?\n   - Is a transformer easement shown (typically a rectangular dashed area around the pad)?\n\nPlease be very specific and identify EACH of the four transformer pads individually.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 21, \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here is the specific information requested regarding the transformer pads. \n\nPlease note that distance measurements are visual estimates based on the provided graphic scale of **1\" = 20'**.\n\n### 1. & 2. Exact Locations and Estimated Clearances of Transformer Pads\n\nI have identified four distinct square symbols indicated by a leader line and the exact text label **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n\n**Transformer Pad 1 (Northwest)**\n*   **Location:** Located on the west side of the site, situated within a curved landscape island just inside the main entrance driveway.\n*   **Nearby Buildings/Units:** West of Building 1 (specifically near Unit 101/102).\n*   **Estimated Clearances:**\n    *   **Nearest building edge:** ~20-25 feet (to the southwest corner of Building 1).\n    *   **Nearest parking/driveway:** ~2-5 feet (it is located immediately adjacent to the concrete curb of the curved entrance drive).\n    *   **Nearest property line:** ~25-30 feet (to the western property boundary line).\n    *   **Nearest fire lane:** Assuming the main entrance drive serves as a fire lane, ~2-5 feet.\n\n**Transformer Pad 2 (West-Central)**\n*   **Location:** Located on the western edge of the property, south of Pad 1, positioned beside a pedestrian sidewalk.\n*   **Nearby Buildings/Units:** West of the junction between Building 2 (Unit 201) and Building 8.\n*   **Estimated Clearances:**\n    *   **Nearest building edge:** ~15-20 feet (to the western edge of Building 2/8).\n    *   **Nearest parking/driveway:** ~10-15 feet (there is a parking stall located to the north of the pad).\n    *   **Nearest property line:** ~15-20 feet (to the western property boundary line).\n    *   **Nearest fire lane:** The nearest main drive aisle is approximately ~30 feet to the east, past the buildings.\n\n**Transformer Pad 3 (East-Central)**\n*   **Location:** Located in the central-eastern part of the site, situated in the narrow courtyard space between two buildings.\n*   **Nearby Buildings/Units:** Between Building 4 (specifically Unit 404 to the west) and Building 5 (specifically Unit 503/504 to the east).\n*   **Estimated Clearances:**\n    *   **Nearest building edge:** ~10 feet to the eastern wall of Building 4; ~10 feet to the western wall of Building 5.\n    *   **Nearest parking/driveway:** ~40-50 feet (the main east-west drive aisle is located to the south).\n    *   **Nearest property line:** This pad is interior to the site; the nearest property line (East) is approximately >60 feet away.\n    *   **Nearest fire lane:** ~40-50 feet (drive aisle to the south).\n\n**Transformer Pad 4 (South-Central)**\n*   **Location:** *(Note: The text label for this pad is located on the right side over Unit 602, but the leader line snakes across the drawing to point to a specific square symbol).* The pad is located in the central courtyard area.\n*   **Nearby Buildings/Units:** Located just north of Building 7 (specifically Unit 703) and south of the pedestrian walkway connecting the buildings.\n*   **Estimated Clearances:**\n    *   **Nearest building edge:** ~10 feet to the northern wall of Building 7 (Unit 703).\n    *   **Nearest parking/driveway:** ~40-50 feet (the main drive aisle is located to the south of Building 7).\n    *   **Nearest property line:** ~60+ feet (to the southern property boundary).\n    *   **Nearest fire lane:** ~40-50 feet (drive aisle to the south).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Electrical Specifications\n\nBased on a thorough review of all text, labels, and notes (including the \"Utility Notes\" block) on this specific sheet:\n\n*   **Single-phase or three-phase service?** There is **no text or label** indicating the phase of the service.\n*   **Oil-filled or dry-type transformer?** There is **no text or label** indicating the transformer type.\n*   **Service capacity/size?** There is **no text or label** indicating the kVA rating or size of the transformers.\n*   **Reference to Austin Energy (AE) Design standard details?** There is **no mention** of Austin Energy, \"AE\", or specific AE design standards on this sheet. \n\nThe pads are solely identified by the generic label: **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Underground Utilities Near Transformers\n\n*   **Pad 1 (Northwest):** A dashed underground water line (labeled **\"W\"**) runs roughly parallel to the building edge, approximately **~10-15 feet east** of the transformer pad.\n*   **Pad 2 (West-Central):** A dashed water line (**\"W\"**) and a solid storm drain line (labeled **\"- SD -\"**) run north-south between the pad and the building. The water line is approx **~10 feet east**, and the storm drain is approx **~15 feet east** of the pad.\n*   **Pad 3 (East-Central):** A solid storm drain line (**\"- SD -\"**) runs directly north-south through the corridor between Building 4 and 5, passing extremely close to, or potentially directly underneath, the transformer pad symbol (clearance is visually **< 5 feet**). A water line (**\"W\"**) also runs parallel through this corridor, approx **~5-10 feet** from the pad.\n*   **Pad 4 (South-Central):** A storm drain line (**\"- SD -\"**) runs east-west to the north of the pad (approx **~10-15 feet** away), and a water line (**\"W\"**) runs nearby to the east.\n\n*(Note: Solid blue lines labeled \"- E -\" (Electrical) route directly to all four transformer pads as expected).*\n\n---\n\n### 5. Easements or Access\n\n*   **Transformer Easements:** There are **no specific, dedicated transformer easements** drawn or labeled around any of the four individual pads on this sheet. (Typically, this would appear as a dashed rectangular box immediately surrounding the pad with a label like \"10x10 Elec Esmt\").\n*   **General Easements:** There are larger general easements noted on the property boundaries (e.g., a \"Wastewater Easement\" near the western property line), but none explicitly carved out for the transformer pads themselves.\n*   **Access:** Access to the pads appears to be via the adjacent driveways (Pad 1), parking area sidewalks (Pad 2), or internal pedestrian walkways (Pads 3 & 4). No distinct maintenance access paths are drawn.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1640,"outputTokens":1552,"totalTokens":6992,"reasoningTokens":3800},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Re-examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) in detail and focus specifically on:\n\n1. EXACT locations of all four transformer pads - list each one with:\n   - Compass direction on site (NW, W, N, E, S, etc.)\n   - Which buildings are nearby\n   - Specific unit numbers if labeled (e.g., near Unit 101)\n\n2. For each transformer pad, measure or estimate the clearance distance (in feet, using the 1\"=20' scale) from the pad to:\n   - The nearest building edge\n   - The nearest parking area or driveway\n   - The nearest property line\n   - The nearest fire lane\n\n3. Electrical specifications:\n   - Is there any text, label, or note that indicates:\n     - Single-phase or three-phase service?\n     - Oil-filled or dry-type transformer?\n     - Service capacity/size?\n     - Any reference to Austin Energy (AE) Design standard details?\n\n4. Underground utilities shown near transformers:\n   - Are there water lines (W), wastewater lines (WW), storm drain lines (SD), or other utilities shown crossing or running near the pads?\n   - Can you estimate clearance distances between pads and these utilities?\n\n5. Easements or access:\n   - Are there any property boundaries, easements, or access paths marked near the transformers?\n   - Is a transformer easement shown (typically a rectangular dashed area around the pad)?\n\nPlease be very specific and identify EACH of the four transformer pads individually."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"c7797eb0-13f7-4dae-8876-b00bcec9ca61","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_2","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-RuWFFAPKEBUFlr6JIrsM644i","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 08 May 2026 13:23:29 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","