e also absent from the documentation (EL-2.12, EL-2.13).","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3284e2-1747-4d44-a558-2f00d9a24819","uuid":"12aef012-7e50-43e2-b06e-d813e889616d"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246618493,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W3T1YW46E790J12T3NMPK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Critical Deficiency Identified:**\nThe landscape plan shows three mitigation trees positioned at approximately 2-5 feet from an overhead electric (OHE) line on the southern property boundary. This placement appears to violate minimum clearance requirements for trees near electric infrastructure:\n- Within 15 feet of distribution lines (non-utility-compatible trees prohibited)\n- Within 25 feet of distribution lines (large trees prohibited)\n- Within 25 feet of transmission structures (all trees prohibited per Sheet 3, Block 13 Electric Transmission Notes)\n\n**Documented Deficiencies:**\n1. **EL-2.14 (FAIL)**: Trees not shown on landscape plan with sufficient clarity to allow independent verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities. The OHE line and three trees are depicted, but electrical infrastructure details are not adequately coordinated.\n\n2. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)**: Three mitigation trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones without documented written approval from Austin Energy. Despite evidence of Austin Energy review (referenced in Master Comment Report), no explicit approval letter authorizing this tree planting is provided.\n\n**Notable Pass:**\n- **EL-2.10 (PASS)**: Plant schedule (Sheet 35) provides complete species identification with both common and scientific names for all proposed trees.\n\n**Items Requiring Clarification:**\nMultiple items are flagged as **not-verifiable** due to insufficient plan coordination and missing documentation (10 items: EL-2.1, EL-2.2, EL-2.3, EL-2.4, EL-2.5, EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.11), including:\n- Species identification of the three specific trees near the OHE line\n- Confirmation of OHE line voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission)\n- Utility pole and pad-mount equipment location coordination\n- Root barrier specifications for trees near underground electric equipment\n\nThe review is now complete with all 15 checklist items evaluated."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3284e2-1747-4d44-a558-2f00d9a24819","uuid":"c47435b8-5f27-4618-b3d6-908f604126c3"}
