L-2.11), including:\n- Species identification of the three specific trees near the OHE line\n- Confirmation of OHE line voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission)\n- Utility pole and pad-mount equipment location coordination\n- Root barrier specifications for trees near underground electric equipment\n\nThe review is now complete with all 15 checklist items evaluated.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4b3284e2-1747-4d44-a558-2f00d9a24819","total_cost_usd":0.4692438000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":374,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131114,"cache_read_input_tokens":1915073,"output_tokens":22694,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":131114},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":374,"outputTokens":22694,"cacheReadInputTokens":1915073,"cacheCreationInputTokens":131114,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4692438000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of site, approximately 2-5 feet from OHE line on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three mitigation trees positioned near OHE line in southeast corner of landscape plan are shown at approximately 2-5 feet from conductor. Species identification not provided on landscape plan; cannot verify whether proposed trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F without documented species verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan Sheet 31 shows three trees marked 'M' (mitigation) in the southeast corner with trunk centers approximately 2-5 feet from the OHE line. The trees are represented by perfect circle symbols consistent with large shade trees. However, the landscape plan does not label these specific trees with species names or reference the plant schedule.","reasoning":"While the proximity (2-5 feet) appears to potentially violate the 15-foot minimum clearance for non-utility-compatible trees under distribution lines, the species of these three specific trees cannot be confirmed from the available plans. The plant schedule lists Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud as the proposed species, but which of these species are the three trees in the southeast corner cannot be determined without explicit labeling on the landscape plan. Without verified species identification, the utility-compatible status cannot be determined from ECM Appendix F.","tools_used":["vision","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Site-wide overhead electric transmission facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission structures confirmed to be present on or adjacent to site per Electric Transmission Notes (Sheet 3, Block 13). However, whether the OHE line shown on landscape plan is transmission or distribution voltage cannot be determined from plans provided. Without voltage classification, and without species verification for trees near OHE line, compliance with 50-foot transmission clearance for non-utility-compatible trees cannot be assessed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes) explicitly addresses transmission structures on the site and imposes a categorical prohibition on tree planting within 25 feet of transmission structures. The landscape plan shows an OHE line along the southern boundary. However, the plans do not specify the voltage level of this OHE line (transmission vs. distribution).","reasoning":"EL-2.2 requires assessment of non-utility-compatible trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors. While transmission structures are acknowledged in the general notes, the specific OHE line shown on the landscape plan is not labeled as transmission voltage. Without confirmation that the southern boundary OHE line is transmission (not distribution) voltage, and without species verification for trees near it, this item cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of site, approximately 2-5 feet from OHE line on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three trees in southeast corner are positioned at 2-5 feet from OHE line, well within the 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees from distribution conductors. However, species identification of these three specific trees is not provided on landscape plan. Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm and Live Oak (both potentially large trees), but cannot verify which species are the three trees in southeast corner without explicit labeling. Mature heights in plant schedule (16' minimum) appear lower than typical ECM Appendix F values for these species (40+ feet), creating ambiguity about whether these are truly large trees per ECM Appendix F definition (mature height ≥ 40 feet).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows three mitigation trees at 2-5 feet from OHE line. Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm with 16' HT minimum and Live Oak with 16' HT minimum specifications, which conflicts with typical ECM Appendix F mature height listings for these species (typically 40-50 feet). The three trees near the OHE line are not individually identified by species.","reasoning":"EL-2.3 requires large trees (mature height ≥ 40 feet per ECM Appendix F) to maintain 25-foot clearance from distribution conductors. The three trees in question cannot be identified by species from the landscape plan alone. The plant schedule minimum heights (16') are substantially lower than typical mature heights for Cedar Elm and Live Oak, making it unclear whether ECM Appendix F would classify these as large trees. Without verified species identification and reference to ECM Appendix F mature heights, the deficiency cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Site-wide overhead electric transmission facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission structures confirmed to be addressed in general notes (Sheet 3, Block 13). However, whether the OHE line on landscape plan represents transmission or distribution voltage is not specified. Without voltage classification and without species identification of specific trees, compliance with 50-foot transmission clearance for large trees cannot be assessed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 indicates transmission structures are present on or adjacent to the site. The landscape plan shows an OHE line but does not label it as transmission voltage.","reasoning":"EL-2.4 requires large trees to maintain 50-foot clearance from transmission conductors. Without confirmation that the OHE line is transmission voltage (not distribution), this item cannot be evaluated. The plans do not explicitly state the voltage classification of the OHE line shown on the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":["Transmission easement boundaries on site, if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading plan indicates a transmission easement is addressed in the design (evidenced by Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3). However, the exact boundaries of the transmission easement are not clearly delineated on the landscape plan in relation to proposed tree locations. Without explicit transmission easement boundary marking on the landscape plan, the specific locations of any trees within the easement cannot be confirmed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 contains detailed Electric Transmission Notes that address transmission easements. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) mentions various easements including electric easements, but the transmission easement boundary is not clearly distinguished from other easements or clearly overlaid on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"EL-2.5 requires verification that no trees are shown within transmission easement boundaries. While transmission easements are referenced in the project documents, the landscape plan does not clearly show the transmission easement boundary overlaid with the tree planting locations, making it impossible to definitively verify tree placement relative to the easement perimeter.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Utility poles if present on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan and electrical plan (Sheet 21) do not show utility pole locations explicitly marked or dimensioned. While overhead electric lines are depicted on the landscape plan, specific pole locations are not identified on either sheet, preventing verification of 10-foot clearance requirement from poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows an OHE line but no specific pole locations are marked. Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) describes underground electrical distribution but does not show overhead pole locations.","reasoning":"EL-2.6 requires verification that trees are not planted within 10 feet of utility poles. Without explicit pole location markings on the landscape or electrical plans, the proximity of trees to poles cannot be verified. The plans show the OHE line routing but not the specific pole base locations.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted equipment locations if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows transformer pads and electrical infrastructure with underground distribution, but the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not clearly identify pad-mounted equipment locations or access door orientations in relation to proposed trees. Without explicit pad-mount locations on the landscape plan, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 indicates transformer pads are part of the electrical design. Sheet 31 (landscape plan) shows building footprints and trees but does not clearly mark or dimension pad-mounted equipment locations relative to proposed plantings.","reasoning":"EL-2.7 requires trees to maintain 10-foot clearance from pad-mounted equipment and between equipment access doors and drivable surfaces. The landscape plan does not overlay pad-mount locations with sufficient clarity to verify tree distances from these facilities.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electric equipment locations if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows underground electric lines and pull boxes, but the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not overlay underground equipment locations with sufficient clarity to verify 5-foot clearance from tree planting locations. Coordination between electrical and landscape plans is insufficient for verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electrical infrastructure with pull boxes and duct banks. Sheet 31 does not clearly indicate how the underground equipment coordinates with the proposed tree planting locations.","reasoning":"EL-2.8 requires trees to maintain 5-foot clearance from underground electric equipment. The landscape and electrical plans are not sufficiently coordinated on a single clear drawing to verify tree trunk locations against underground equipment positions.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape details (Sheet 37) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) do not show explicit root barrier specifications at trees planted near underground electric facilities. The landscape plan does not clearly identify which trees are within 20-foot clearance zone of underground equipment, and landscape details do not specify root barrier requirements (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 37 (Landscape Details) and Sheet 31 do not provide explicit documentation of root barriers at trees near underground electric equipment. The coordination between electrical equipment locations and tree planting locations is not sufficiently detailed on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"EL-2.9 requires root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) for trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. Without clear identification of affected trees and documented root barrier specifications on the landscape details, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan tree planting legend"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule on Sheet 35 provides complete species identification with both common and scientific names for all proposed trees: Live Oak (Quercus virginiana), Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia), Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora), and Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana). Plant legend defines tree symbols (SY, PL, P, M designations).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 contains a complete plant list with scientific names provided for all four tree species proposed. Sheet 31 landscape plan includes a key notes section defining tree type abbreviations.","reasoning":"EL-2.10 requires that species be identified on landscape plans. Sheet 35 provides comprehensive species identification with both common and scientific botanical names for all proposed trees, satisfying the requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Large trees (40+ feet mature height) near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm and Live Oak with 16' HT minimum specifications, substantially lower than typical ECM Appendix F mature heights for these species. Landscape plan does not differentiate large trees from other trees or cross-reference to mature height designations. Without clear identification of which trees meet the 40+ feet mature height threshold per ECM Appendix F, large tree differentiation cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule specifies 16' HT minimum for both Cedar Elm and Live Oak, but these values appear to be installation heights, not mature heights. Typical mature heights for Cedar Elm and Live Oak range from 40-50 feet per standard horticultural references. Sheet 31 does not mark trees by mature height categories.","reasoning":"EL-2.11 requires large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) to be differentiated on plans to verify clearances. Without either: (1) confirmation of ECM Appendix F mature heights for the proposed species, or (2) explicit marking of large trees on the landscape plan, this requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees with dimensioned clearances from overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not include dimension lines or measurements showing clearances from specific trees to the OHE line. The tree locations and OHE line are shown graphically, but clearance distances are not dimensioned. Without explicit clearance dimensions, measurement reference points (pole centerline vs. outer conductor) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows the OHE line routing and tree locations graphically but does not include dimension strings showing distances between tree trunks and the overhead conductor line.","reasoning":"EL-2.12 requires that if clearances ARE dimensioned, they must be measured from the outer conductor, not pole centerline. Since the landscape plan does not dimension any clearances, there is no measurement reference to evaluate against this standard. This is not a violation, but rather indicates the requirement is not applicable as currently presented.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees with dimensioned clearances shown on plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not include dimensioned clearances showing measurements from trees to overhead electric facilities. Without dimension lines and callouts specifying clearance measurements, the reference point (trunk vs. canopy edge) cannot be evaluated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows trees and OHE line graphically but without dimension annotations specifying clearances or indicating whether measurements would be taken from trunk centerline or canopy edge.","reasoning":"EL-2.13 addresses how clearances should be measured IF they are dimensioned on plans (trunk center, not canopy edge). Since no clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan, this standard cannot be evaluated. The requirement is not applicable as currently presented.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast portion of landscape plan near OHE line on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three mitigation trees positioned at 2-5 feet from OHE line on southern property boundary cannot be verified for clearance compliance without cross-reference to electrical plan showing conductor locations and clearance zones. Landscape plan shows OHE line routing but does not overlay electrical infrastructure details, transmission easement boundaries, or utility pole locations with sufficient clarity to independently verify tree clearances from the landscape plan alone.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows an OHE line along the southern boundary and three trees positioned very close to it (2-5 feet trunk center distance). However, the OHE line is drawn as a simple line with no reference to the associated electrical plan (Sheet 21), conductor positions, clearance zones, pole locations, or transmission easement boundaries.","reasoning":"EL-2.14 requires that trees be shown on the landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities with sufficient clarity to verify clearances. While the OHE line is depicted, the electrical infrastructure is not sufficiently coordinated with the landscape plan to allow independent verification of clearances. The three trees in close proximity to the OHE line create ambiguity about compliance that requires cross-reference to missing electrical detail.","tools_used":["vision","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Three mitigation trees in southeast corner positioned at 2-5 feet from OHE line on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three trees marked as mitigation trees in the southeast corner of the landscape plan are positioned at approximately 2-5 feet from the OHE line along the southern property boundary, placing them within restricted clearance zones (15 feet for distribution non-utility-compatible trees, 25 feet for distribution large trees, 50 feet for transmission). No documentation of Austin Energy written approval for planting trees in these locations is provided in the submitted plans, application documents, or supplementary documents reviewed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan Sheet 31 visually depicts three trees marked 'M' (mitigation) with trunk centers positioned 2-5 feet from the OHE line per vision analysis. The Master Comment Report references an Austin Energy review (with a Bluebeam link to detailed comments) but no explicit Austin Energy approval letter authorizing tree planting in close proximity to the OHE line is included in the submitted documents. The Electric Transmission Notes (Sheet 3, Block 13) state 'No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure,' but no variance or exception approval is documented.","reasoning":"EL-2.15 requires documented written approval from Austin Energy for trees planted within prohibited clearance zones. While the 2-5 foot positioning of the three trees in the southeast corner clearly appears to violate standard clearance distances (15 feet for distribution, 25 feet for transmission), no approval letter or exception documentation is visible in the project documents. The presence of Austin Energy comments via Bluebeam suggests review occurred, but the explicit approval for this planting variance is not provided in the submitted materials.","tools_used":["vision","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d4011938-1669-4171-a635-0468502c9eed"}
