{"level":30,"time":1778246632198,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W49M4DC01BM2KVAM6BF1Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me now compile my research findings and begin systematic evaluation of each checklist item. Based on all the information I've gathered, here are my findings:\n\n## Research Phase Summary - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:\n\n**Critical Missing Elements:**\n\n1. **No Austin Energy (AE) Design Approval Documentation** - No ESPA (Electric Service Planning Application), transformer pad detail sheets, service type approval, or written approvals for any clearance reductions or variances are present in the project files.\n\n2. **No Transformer Specifications** - The site plan (Sheet 21) labels 4 transformer pads but provides NO information about:\n   - Service type (single-phase vs. three-phase)\n   - Equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n   - Service capacity/size\n   - Pad dimensions or AE Design standard detail reference numbers\n\n3. **No Transformer Easements** - No dedicated transformer easements are drawn or labeled around any of the four pads.\n\n4. **No Clearance Dimensions** - No horizontal clearances from pads to buildings, parking, fire lanes, property lines, or other features are dimensioned or labeled on any plan sheet.\n\n5. **No Access Door Orientation** - Cannot determine which direction access doors face, preventing verification of hot-stick use area clearances (10-foot vs. 15-foot).\n\n6. **No Utility Separation Dimensions** - While utilities are shown near transformers (water, wastewater, storm drain lines), NO separation dimensions, profile views, or depth indicators are provided.\n\n7. **No Fire Escape Locations** - Fire escapes are not shown on the building plans.\n\n8. **No Cross-Section Drawings** - No vertical clearance drawings are provided for overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas above/adjacent to transformers.\n\n9. **No Specific Equipment Type Designation** - No indication of whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type, preventing verification of oil-specific clearance and drainage requirements.\n\n10. **No Transformer Easement Width Documentation** - While the grouping notes that AE Design determines easement width, no easement is shown on the plans.\n\n---\n\nNow let me proceed with systematic evaluation of each checklist item:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bba534d5-0ed6-41d8-bc2c-fb63a7697ee2","uuid":"b754110c-e3cc-4527-a1d6-bad3c9c4517b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246635511,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W15T0NB4XPGYS4KTSHG5B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Px6QMm9HUrkUaM5YW5wXYT","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 in proximity to southern OHE line; all buildings in proximity to western OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are shown in plan view relative to overhead electric lines on Sheet 9, but no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided to verify the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows Buildings 1-8 in plan view near OHE lines, particularly Buildings 7-8 near the southern OHE and all buildings near the western OHE. No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor locations are visible in the site plan set.","reasoning":"Per EL-1.1 and UCM § 1.10.3, the clearance requirement requires verification by elevation drawing showing surveyed conductor location and clearance dimension from building face. The absence of such elevation documentation means the requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings; transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three proposed electrical transformer pads are shown on the site plan in proximity to the buildings. However, no clearance dimensions or radial clearance verification are provided demonstrating that the 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors is maintained.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows three transformer pad locations on the proposed electrical site plan. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows the overall site layout with overhead electric lines. No dimension lines or clearance annotations showing 15-foot radial distance from outside conductors to transformer pads are present on any sheet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires customer facilities (including transformer pads) to maintain 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary/neutral conductors. Without documented clearance verification on the plans, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections; building overhangs, awnings, balconies, roofs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets showing projected building elements (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) relative to overhead conductors are provided to verify clearances. Applicant must provide surveyed building elevations with conductor locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set includes building footprints on Sheet 21 but no architectural elevation drawings are visible showing building projections and their relationships to overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Verification of clearances for building projections requires elevation documentation showing both the projected element and the surveyed overhead conductor location with dimension annotations per UCM § 1.10.3. Such documentation is absent from the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows no gas pump canopy structures labeled or indicated anywhere on the property.","reasoning":"This item is not applicable because the site contains only residential townhome development with no gasoline dispensing facilities proposed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Stairs, elevated walkways, elevated platforms if any"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 9 shows the overall site layout with various walkways and potential elevated structures, but no elevation or section drawings are provided to verify that stairs, elevated walkways, or platforms maintain the required 15-foot radial clearance from overhead electric distribution facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows sidewalks and pedestrian pathways on Sheet 9 in areas that may be elevated relative to finished grade, particularly near the detention pond area. However, no cross-section details or elevation drawings are provided showing vertical relationships to overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Without section views showing the vertical position of any elevated structures and the surveyed location of overhead conductors, compliance with the 15-foot radial clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings; western and southern property lines where overhead electric lines exist in right-of-way and on adjacent property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist along the western property line (Valley View Road) and southern property line, with poles and conductors visible on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4). Buildings 7 and 8 are located adjacent to the southern OHE line boundary, and the western driveway crosses underneath the western OHE line. No surveyed elevations and clearance dimensions are provided to demonstrate that buildings maintain the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from the outside conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) clearly depicts overhead utility lines and poles along the western boundary (Valley View Road) and across the property boundaries. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows Buildings 7-8 immediately adjacent to the southern boundary where the OHE line is located. Buildings are shown in plan view only, with no elevation or profile documentation of conductor locations.","reasoning":"The existence of overhead electric facilities along the property boundaries adjacent to buildings is confirmed. However, UCM § 1.10.3 requires permanent clearances to be verified with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions. Buildings within potential clearance distance must be verified with elevation documentation. The plans show no such documentation, constituting a failure to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan set showing surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors. Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor data and clearance dimension annotations are required per UCM § 1.10.3 to demonstrate that required clearances are met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set includes architectural and utility plans, but no dedicated building elevation sheets showing surveyed overhead conductor locations and elevations appear in the available documentation.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.3, building elevation sheets must be provided showing surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions. The absence of such documentation means compliance cannot be verified from the available evidence.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings; western driveway entrance; southern boundary retaining walls"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings, building projections, retaining walls, or other site features. Clearance verification requires dimension lines extending from the outside conductor to all structures and site improvements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows buildings and retaining walls in plan view relative to OHE lines but without clearance dimension annotations. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows finished grades and wall elevations but no dimensions relating to overhead conductors. Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) shows no overhead utilities at all. No section views display dimension lines from conductors to site features.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires dimension lines showing clearances from the outside conductor to building edges and other structures. The complete absence of such dimensions across all relevant sheets constitutes a failure to document required clearances.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences along property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9 and Sheet 31) along the southern and eastern property boundaries in proximity to existing overhead electric lines. However, no clearance dimensions are provided demonstrating that fences maintain the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 and Sheet 31 show wooden privacy fencing (marked with 'H.6' pattern) along the southern property line where the OHE line exists. No dimension annotations show the clearance distance from the fence to the outside conductor.","reasoning":"While fences are proposed in the vicinity of overhead conductors, the clearance dimensions required by UCM § 1.10.3 are not provided. Without explicit clearance documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence locations along property boundaries with electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are proposed along the southern property boundary where existing utility poles are located (per the existing conditions survey). Clearance dimensions showing minimum 10-foot horizontal distance from fence posts to the electric poles are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) shows utility poles at the southern boundary. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows fences proposed along the southern boundary in proximity to these poles. No dimension annotations show distances from fence posts to pole centers.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, fence posts must maintain 10-foot clearance from electric poles. Without clearance dimensions on the plans, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation fences are present adjacent to the property on the site plan. This item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all available site plans shows no substation property boundaries or substation fences indicated on the property or immediately adjacent to it.","reasoning":"This item is not applicable as no substation fences exist on or adjacent to the site.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) are present on the site plan. Only overhead distribution lines are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows overhead utility lines without voltage labeling beyond the 'OHE' designation. Based on the survey legend and the presence of poles with down guys (characteristic of distribution facilities, not transmission towers), these are distribution-level facilities, not transmission-level (≥60kV).","reasoning":"This item is not applicable as the overhead facilities on site appear to be distribution-level (< 60kV), not transmission-level facilities requiring specialized grounding and material specifications.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle barrier fencing or posts if proposed beneath overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier posts or fencing are explicitly labeled as such on the site plan. However, if any fencing in proximity to the OHE lines is intended to function as vehicle barriers, no clearance verification exhibits are provided showing the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from the outermost electric line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows fencing along property boundaries but does not explicitly identify any fence as a vehicle barrier. Standard property perimeter fencing is shown without clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"If vehicle barrier fencing is proposed beneath overhead lines, clearance dimensions would be required per UCM § 1.10.3. The plans do not clearly specify which (if any) fences are vehicle barriers, and no clearance dimensions are provided for any fencing beneath OHE lines.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls along southern property boundary parallel to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Concrete retaining walls are proposed along the southern boundary of the property parallel to and in proximity to the existing overhead electric line (OHE). Sheet 11 shows the retaining wall with top-of-wall elevations (TW ranging from 682.23 to 683.84 feet), but no vertical clearance dimensions from the outermost electric line conductor to the wall are provided. Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) shows no overhead utilities at all.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows retaining walls along the southern boundary near the OHE line. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) provides TW elevations for the wall but no reference to conductor elevation or clearance. Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) completely omits any representation of overhead utilities.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.3, retaining walls must maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outermost electric line. The vertical clearance requirement means the conductor elevation must be known and compared to wall height. Without conductor elevation data and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified and the requirement is not met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation walls are present adjacent to the property. This item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plans shows no substation property boundary indicated on the property or immediately adjacent to it.","reasoning":"This item is not applicable as no Austin Energy substation is present on or adjacent to the property.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) if proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access bridges or elevated platforms are explicitly identified on the site plan. If such structures exist as part of the site design, section views showing the required clearances from overhead conductors are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of the site plan shows pedestrian walkways and potential elevated structures near the detention pond area, but no structures are explicitly labeled as emergency access bridges or platforms.","reasoning":"If emergency access structures exist, they would require both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances per UCM § 1.10.3, verified by section views. Without such documentation, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall section exhibits (Sheet 38) do not show clearance dimension annotations from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of the walls. The Wall Plan section shows the wall details but completely omits representation of overhead electric lines, preventing clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) contains detailed cross-section views of the 14-foot maximum retaining wall design with rebar, backfill, and elevation data, but no overhead electric lines or clearance dimension lines are shown.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.3, section views for retaining walls near overhead lines must include dimension lines showing clearance from the outside conductor to the wall face. The complete absence of conductor representation and clearance dimensions constitutes a failure to provide required documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway entrances on western boundary where OHE line crosses"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are proposed with entrances on the western property boundary that cross directly beneath the existing overhead electric line (OHE). Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows finished grade spot elevations ranging from 679.75 to 688.40 feet at the driveway locations, but provides no vertical clearance dimensions verifying the required minimum 16-foot clearance (for parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot clearance (for areas with truck traffic). Mid-span clearance survey data is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows driveway alignment crossing the OHE line on the western property frontage. Sheet 11 provides spot elevations at driveway locations (679.75-688.40 feet) but no conductor elevation or clearance dimensions are shown. The presence of truck traffic appears likely given the commercial-scale development.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.6.2, driveways require minimum 16-18 foot vertical clearance depending on truck traffic. The plans provide finished grade elevations but no overhead conductor elevation or clearance verification. Without documented mid-span clearance measurements showing the required vertical distance, compliance cannot be confirmed and the requirement is not met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vehicle parking areas are shown on the site plan (both surface and garage parking), but the site plan does not explicitly identify any vehicle display pads or indicate which parking areas (if any) are positioned beneath overhead electric lines. Vertical clearance dimensions are not provided for any parking areas in proximity to OHE.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows multiple parking areas, both surface parking and garage parking within buildings. No parking pads are explicitly labeled as vehicle display areas, and no vertical clearance dimensions from overhead lines to parking surfaces are provided.","reasoning":"If vehicle parking or display is located beneath overhead lines, clearance dimensions would be required per UCM § 1.10.6.2. The plans do not clearly indicate which (if any) parking areas fall beneath overhead lines, and no clearance dimensions are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines (≥60kV) are present on site. Only distribution lines are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead facilities shown on Sheet 4 are identified as distribution-level 'OHE' without transmission-level voltage labeling or transmission tower structures characteristic of 69kV, 138kV, or 345kV facilities.","reasoning":"This item applies only to transmission lines. The facilities on site appear to be distribution-level, not transmission-level infrastructure.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway grades with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site contains only local residential development with no highway or freeway infrastructure.","reasoning":"This item is not applicable as the project does not involve highway/freeway design with transmission structure underbuilds.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Electric poles at western driveway entrance"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) at and near the proposed western driveway entrance. The site plan (Sheet 9) does not provide explicit relocation notes, revised pole locations, or a minimum 30-foot setback dimension from the driveway edge to existing poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) shows utility poles near the western property boundary at the driveway location. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows the driveway but does not indicate whether existing poles will be relocated or maintained, and no 30-foot setback dimension is shown.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, poles in conflict with driveways must be relocated with 30-foot minimum clearance or relocation notes must be provided. Without explicit relocation details or clearance documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All overhead electric facilities and site features"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan provides no clearance dimensions at all from any overhead electric facilities to site features. Where dimensions are absent, it is impossible to verify that they are measured from the outside conductor rather than from pole centerline. Per UCM § 1.10.3, the critical measurement point is the outside conductor, not the pole centerline. The plan's complete absence of clearance dimensions means this requirement cannot be evaluated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheets 9, 21, and 11 reveals no dimension lines originating from overhead conductors or poles and extending to any site features. No clearance dimensions are provided anywhere on the plans.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires clearances measured from the outside conductor. Without any clearance dimensions on the plans, the applicant cannot demonstrate correct measurement methodology, and the failure to provide dimensions constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Streetlight pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows site lighting but does not clearly identify which lighting elements are proposed streetlight poles. If new streetlight poles are proposed, their locations relative to overhead electric lines are not documented with clearance dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows general lighting elements but does not clearly differentiate between decorative landscape lighting and streetlight poles, nor does it provide clearance dimensions from any proposed poles to overhead lines.","reasoning":"Without clear identification of streetlight pole locations and clearance dimensions from overhead lines, compliance with Reviewer Convention standards cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks at property ends along Valley View Road right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing power poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) along Valley View Road at the western property boundary. Sheet 9 shows sidewalks along the property frontage, but no clarification is provided regarding whether sidewalks at the property corners/ends are cleared from the existing poles or if poles require relocation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows utility poles at the western property line along Valley View Road. Sheet 9 shows sidewalk alignment but does not indicate clearance or pole relocation status at property ends.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, sidewalks must be cleared from power poles at property line ends. Without explicit documentation showing either pole relocation or sidewalk clearance from poles, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosures and receptacle locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash collection areas are referenced in the site plan notes (Sheet 9) but specific trash enclosure and receptacle locations are not clearly identified in plan view. If trash facilities are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, clearance verification considering the raised height during bin service is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 references trash collection requirements in notes but does not clearly indicate the specific locations of trash enclosures or receptacles in the plan view, nor does it show any overhead line clearances for such features.","reasoning":"Without clear identification of trash facility locations relative to overhead lines and clearance dimensions accounting for raised bin height, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Sites within electric easements; areas beneath overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows 5-foot electric easements along property boundaries and overhead electric lines running through/adjacent to the property. The proposed site features (buildings, driveways, retaining walls) shown on Sheet 9 are located in proximity to these easements and overhead lines. However, no dimension exhibits verify that items within the electric easements or beneath overhead distribution lines maintain the minimum 7.5-foot clearance from the outside conductor. The absolute prohibition against installing customer facilities under or over distribution lines cannot be verified as being met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows electric easements (5-foot easements recorded along boundaries) and overhead lines. Sheet 9 shows proposed improvements in proximity to these infrastructure elements. No clearance dimensions verify 7.5-foot clearance from conductor, nor do the plans explicitly confirm that no structures are being placed directly under overhead distribution lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 contains both a clearance requirement (7.5 feet) and an absolute prohibition on installing facilities under/over distribution lines. The plans provide no documentation verifying either requirement is met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations are not clearly identified on the site plan or utility plan. If water meters are proposed to be installed near existing overhead electric service drops, no clearance dimensions verify the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows proposed electrical infrastructure but does not clearly identify water meter locations relative to overhead service drops or existing infrastructure.","reasoning":"Without clear identification of water meter locations relative to overhead electric service lines and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing is shown on utility sheets (Sheet 19, Sheet 21) but clearance dimensions from water lines to existing overhead distribution poles and conductors are not provided on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plans show water line routing but do not provide clearance dimensions between water lines and overhead electric infrastructure.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, water lines near overhead utilities require clearance documentation. Without such dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Permanent structure foundations within 5 feet of property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While buildings are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9), no building foundation detail drawings are provided, and no explicit documentation shows whether foundations are located within 5 feet of the property line where electric facilities in the right-of-way or adjacent property require clearance space.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows building outlines but does not provide detailed foundation plans showing specific setbacks from property line or relationships to adjacent ROW utilities.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, if foundations are within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW, clearance space must be documented. Without foundation detail plans, this requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and all site features in proximity to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway proposed grades (Sheet 11: 679.75-688.40 feet) are shown in proximity to overhead electric facilities. The vertical clearance from these grades to the overhead conductors is not documented. A registered surveyor's mid-span clearance survey is required to verify that minimum clearance requirements (16-18 feet for driveways per UCM § 1.10.6.2) are satisfied, but no such survey data is provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 shows finished driveway grades ranging 679.75-688.40 feet. Sheet 9 shows driveways crossing the OHE line. No conductor elevation or vertical clearance dimensions are provided, and no surveyor's mid-span clearance report is included in the documentation.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.3, when vertical clearance may be marginal or insufficient, a registered surveyor must provide mid-span clearance data. The absence of this documentation is a failure to provide required verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossings of roadways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing overhead electric lines cross proposed driveways on the western property boundary (Sheet 9), but no notation indicates whether these crossings are oriented at the required 90-degree angle to the driveway centerline.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows the OHE line crossing driveways but does not provide angle dimension annotations relative to driveway alignment.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, overhead line roadway crossings should be at 90 degrees. Without angle documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric infrastructure only. Existing overhead lines (Sheet 9) do not indicate voltage levels or wire types. Without section views or detailed crossing information, it cannot be determined whether secondary overhead lines (if present) cross over primary lines in violation of Reviewer Convention standards.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 and Sheet 21 show existing and proposed electrical infrastructure, but no explicit cross-section details are provided showing the relative vertical positioning of multiple overhead conductor types.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, secondary lines must not cross over primary lines. Without section view documentation, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are shown or proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all site plan sheets shows no marquee sign structures proposed.","reasoning":"This item is not applicable as marquee signs are not part of the proposed development.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed power poles for underground service conversion"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric infrastructure but does not clearly indicate whether new power poles are proposed for the underground service conversion. If new poles are proposed, their horizontal spacing relative to existing poles is not documented with the required 20-foot minimum dimension.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and underground infrastructure but does not explicitly identify whether new power poles will be installed or provide distance dimensions between new and existing poles.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, if new poles are proposed for underground service conversion, 20-foot spacing from existing poles must be documented. Without clear pole identification and spacing dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixtures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape and site plans show general lighting elements, but decorative lighting fixture locations and their clearance from overhead electric lines are not clearly documented. If decorative lighting is positioned beneath overhead lines, clearance verification exhibits with required dimensions (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and Sheet 9 (Site Plan) show general site features including lighting symbols but do not clearly identify decorative lighting fixture locations and distances from overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.3, decorative lighting beneath overhead lines requires clearance verification. Without clear identification of fixture locations and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed at southern property boundary; trees in proximity to overhead electric distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows three tree symbols in the bottom-right corner with canopy circle outlines that graphically overlap the overhead electric line (OHE) line running along the southern boundary. Two trees are labeled 'M' (mitigation trees) and one is labeled 'P' (parking buffer point tree). No tree species are identified on Sheet 31. No documentation shows that these trees are utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F (utility-compatible trees marked 'UC' with mature height ≤20 feet). No clearance distances are documented showing the 10 lateral feet minimum from distribution conductors or 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors required by UCM § 1.10.10.4.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) vision analysis directly observed: 'The drawn circular outlines representing the canopies of these three specific trees graphically overlap the line labeled \"-OHE-\".' Sheet 31 provides no tree species names or utility compatibility information. No clearance dimensions are provided.","reasoning":"Per ECM § 2.4.1.D, § 2.4.2.C, and UCM § 1.10.10.4, trees within clearance distances of overhead conductors must be utility-compatible species. The plans show trees whose canopy circles overlap the OHE line, indicating either placement within required clearance distances or violation of clearance requirements. Without species identification and clearance documentation, the requirement cannot be met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical meters are shown on Sheet 21 as being mounted to building exterior walls, but enlarged meter area detail plans are not provided. No site plan detail shows meter installation locations with 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances per UCM § 1.10.9, nor are potential obstructions (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, building projections) identified relative to meter access requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electrical meter locations but does not provide enlarged detail plans showing the required working clearance zones and checking for obstructions per UCM § 1.10.9.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.9.3.1, proposed meter locations must not be obstructed by site features. Without enlarged detail plans showing working clearance zones, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed buildings adjacent to existing streetlights"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing streetlight or utility light poles may be present along the property frontage (Sheet 4). Sheet 9 shows building locations but does not provide clearance dimensions from buildings to existing streetlight poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows utility poles at the property line. Sheet 9 shows buildings in plan view but does not indicate clearance distances from buildings to any light poles.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, buildings must maintain clearances from existing streetlights. Without documented clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy wires from electric poles at western property boundary; accessible paths and driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) identifies a down guy wire from a utility pole at the northwestern area of the property. The site plan (Sheet 9) shows the main driveway entrance crossing directly beneath the pole location where the down guy is located. The down guy anchor point and the extent of the down guy cable are not clearly depicted on the site plan relative to the proposed driveway and pedestrian pathways. No note indicates whether the down guy will conflict with accessible routes or if the pole will be converted to self-supporting configuration.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 clearly shows a down guy ('DOWN GUY' label) at a utility pole on the western boundary. Sheet 9 shows the main driveway entrance routing at this same location. The site plans do not indicate down guy relocation, pole conversion, or documentation that down guy conflicts are resolved.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.17.0 and Reviewer Convention, down guy wires conflicting with accessible paths or driveways must be resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles. The absence of conflict resolution documentation constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No angled guy anchors from transmission structures are shown on the site plan. This item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The existing overhead infrastructure shown on Sheet 4 consists of distribution-level poles with down guys, not transmission towers with angled guy anchors.","reasoning":"This item applies only to angled transmission guy easements, which do not appear to exist on this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor points if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) identifies down guy locations but does not clearly show the specific anchor point locations or provide easement boundaries. No easement exhibit showing 10-foot width extending 5 feet past the anchor ground entry point is provided on the submitted site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 labels a down guy but does not clearly depict the anchor point location or provide an easement boundary demonstrating the 10-foot-wide, 5-foot-extension requirement.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, down guy anchor easements require specific boundaries. Without easement exhibits showing the required dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) are shown positioned with overhead electric lines above them. Proposed transformers are pad-mounted and shown as part of the underground electrical system.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows pad-mounted transformer locations as part of the underground electrical infrastructure, not positioned beneath overhead lines.","reasoning":"The proposed transformers are not positioned beneath overhead lines, so this clearance item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations are shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The proposed electrical infrastructure consists of pad-mounted transformers in landscape areas, not niche service configurations.","reasoning":"This item does not apply as no niche service configurations are proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas; equipment operation zones; work platforms"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones may be depicted on erosion control or construction phasing sheets, but no plan view clearly identifies staging area boundaries with documented 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines. OSHA requires 20-foot clearance during construction, distinct from permanent clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set includes erosion control and construction phasing information, but staging area boundaries and construction equipment zones are not clearly related to overhead electric lines with minimum clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.2 and OSHA regulations, construction staging must maintain 10-foot radial clearance (or 20 feet during equipment operation). Without documented clearance dimensions for staging areas, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Entire project site; construction activities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The cover sheet (Sheet 1) does not include a note requiring that the owner/contractor notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. While Sheet 3 (General Notes) contains comprehensive electric transmission notes, the specific 48-hour notification requirement is not explicitly stated on either the cover sheet or general notes sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 1 (Cover Sheet) found: 'There are **no notes** present on this cover sheet regarding a 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.' Sheet 3 contains electric transmission and electric notes but the specific 48-hour notification requirement is not included in blocks 13, 17, or 19.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code, all plans with overhead electric lines must include explicit notice of the 48-hour notification requirement. The absence of this required note constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Service-mast through-roof installations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are provided showing service-mast through-roof installation details or clearance dimensions from the roof line. Without elevation documentation, the required 3-foot clearance above roof or 18-inch clearance for masts within 4 feet of roof edge cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows building electrical service information but no detailed roof elevation plans are provided showing service-mast vertical clearances.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.6.2, service-mast clearance requirements require elevation documentation. Without such plans, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e942253-7258-4c80-b1f5-d3905a77aa10","uuid":"970b4080-3d41-4132-9f45-b69fb00524b9"}
