{"level":30,"time":1778246741847,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W7EAT9JKA77ZPX3NQKF22","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for the **EL-13 Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements** grouping.\n\n## Summary\n\nI evaluated all 39 checklist items for this transformer pad clearance review. The analysis identified critical documentation gaps and specific compliance failures:\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**FAIL (6 items):**\n- **EL-13.23**: Storm drain line runs directly adjacent to Transformer Pad 3 (east-central location), violating the 5-foot minimum clearance\n- **EL-13.31**: No cross-section drawings provided showing vertical clearances\n- **EL-13.34**: Transformer Pad 3 location raises concerns about easement conflicts (no AE Design written approval documented)\n- **EL-13.35**: No transformer easements shown around any of the four pads\n- **EL-13.37**: No transformer pad dimensions specified on plans; no reference to AE Design-approved detail sheets\n- **EL-13.38**: Transformer Pad 1 (northwest at main entrance) located within 4 feet of vehicle driveway but lacks required bollard protection\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (17 items):**\nMost clearance-related items cannot be verified because no horizontal clearance dimensions are labeled on the plans. Critical missing information includes:\n- Building clearances (EL-13.1, 6)\n- Fence clearances (EL-13.3, 4)\n- Sidewalk clearances (EL-13.7)\n- Hot-stick use area clearances (EL-13.10, 11)\n- Fire hydrant clearances (EL-13.12)\n- Tree/vegetation clearances (EL-13.13, 14, 15)\n- Utility clearances (EL-13.21, 22, 25, 26)\n- Drainage direction for oil-filled equipment (EL-13.32 - transformer type not specified)\n- Electrical routing on private property (EL-13.36)\n\n**NOT APPLICABLE (12 items):**\nSeveral items don't apply to this project (no retaining walls near pads, no balconies, no fire escapes, no stairwells, no bike racks, no light poles, no gas service, no overhead lines)\n\n**PASS (1 item):**\n- **EL-13.33**: All transformer pads located on private property, not in public right-of-way\n\nThe structured findings have been returned in the required format, including all agent traces showing the evidence basis for each determination."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bba534d5-0ed6-41d8-bc2c-fb63a7697ee2","uuid":"546986bd-4a7b-460a-8b65-e264f11509f8"}
