bility of this exception cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies or overhangs are shown on the site plan or building plans above or immediately adjacent to transformer pad locations. This item does not apply to this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 and Sheet 21 show building footprints and transformer pad locations. The building footprints do not indicate balconies or overhangs directly above any transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement is only applicable when balconies or overhangs are present above or adjacent to transformers. Since none are shown, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No window, door, or ventilating duct locations are dimensioned relative to transformer pads. The requirement applies to oil-filled equipment when windows/doors/ducts are less than 12 feet from grade or lack 5-foot lateral separation; however, transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 21 do not indicate specific window, door, or ventilating duct locations relative to transformer pads, nor do they specify transformer type (oil-filled or dry-type).","reasoning":"This requirement applies specifically to oil-filled equipment. Without transformer type specifications and without dimensioned locations of windows/doors/ducts relative to pads, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads adjacent to sidewalks"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown on Sheets 9 and 21, and several transformer pads are adjacent to sidewalk areas (particularly TP1 and TP2 on the western side). However, no specific clearance dimensions from the back of sidewalk to pad edges are labeled.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads adjacent to labeled concrete sidewalks (e.g., '5' Concrete Sidewalk'). Sheet 9 confirms sidewalk locations throughout the site. No dimension lines show distance from sidewalk back edge to transformer pad edge.","reasoning":"While sidewalks are adjacent to some pads, the 2-foot minimum clearance from back of sidewalk cannot be verified without dimensioned measurements on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as emergency exits are shown on the building plans adjacent to transformer pads. This item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows building footprints and indicates internal unit divisions and 'Patio (typ.)' areas, but does not depict external stairwells or emergency exit stairs adjacent to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when stairwells are present adjacent to transformers. Since none are shown, the item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or external stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the building plans. This item applies only to oil-filled equipment with fire escapes present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 shows the Fire Protection Plan with building footprints and fire lane routing. No external fire escapes or dedicated external emergency exit stairs are labeled or depicted on the building footprints.","reasoning":"Since no fire escapes are shown on the plans, this requirement is not applicable. The requirement also applies only to oil-filled transformers, which are not specified on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The hot-stick use area (access door side) must maintain minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure. However, no access door orientation is indicated on any transformer pad, and no clearance dimensions are labeled from pads to adjacent features.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads as simple rectangle symbols with no indication of door orientation. No dashed lines or symbols indicate the access door location or the hot-stick use area.","reasoning":"Without access door orientation documented on the plans, the specific directional clearance requirement (10 feet from the access door side) cannot be verified. Actual measured clearances must be shown on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations (if applicable)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing whether any transformer locations are in confined spaces (niche, vault, or enclosed area on 3+ sides). Without access door orientation and vertical clearance documentation, the 15-foot confined space clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No cross-section drawings are provided on the plan set showing vertical dimensions or confined space configurations above or adjacent to transformer pads. Sheet 21 shows pad locations in plan view only, without sectional details.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when a transformer faces a confined space (3+ sides enclosed). Without cross-sections or explicit documentation of pad location relative to building configuration, it cannot be determined whether this condition is met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrants are shown on Sheet 10 (two 'Proposed Fire Hydrant' locations marked), but no clearance dimensions are labeled from these hydrants to the four transformer pads on Sheet 21.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 shows fire hydrant locations (one in SW corner, one in south-central area). Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. No dimension lines show distances between hydrants and transformer pads.","reasoning":"While fire hydrants are present on the site, specific distances from hydrants to transformer pads are not dimensioned on the plans. The 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified without explicit measurements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Perimeter landscape areas near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) along property perimeters, and a tree list is provided (Sheet 32), but specific tree species identification and utility-compatibility verification per ECM Appendix F are not documented. Additionally, transformer pads are not depicted on the landscape plan, so exact distances from trees to pads cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows tree locations with only type abbreviations (SY, PL, M, P). Sheet 32 provides tree details but does not indicate which trees are utility-compatible (ECM Appendix F 'UC' designation). Transformer pad locations are not shown on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"Without specific tree species names and ECM Appendix F utility-compatibility verification, and without transformer pad depiction on the landscape plan, the 10-foot lateral clearance requirement cannot be verified for trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows broad landscape zones (H.1 through H.7 hatch areas) but does not provide detailed shrub or low-lying vegetation planting locations. Transformer pads are not depicted on the landscape plan. Without access door orientation on the electrical plan and without detailed shrub locations on landscape plan, the 10-foot clearance (access door side) and 5-foot clearance (other sides) requirements cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 uses hatch patterns to denote landscape zones (paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open space, sod) but does not detail individual shrub plantings. Transformer pads are not shown on this sheet.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies different clearances for the access door side (10 feet) vs. other sides (5 feet). Without transformer access door orientation and detailed shrub locations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Property areas with trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31), and tree protection/planting details are provided (Sheet 37), but specific identification of trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads is not documented. Transformer pads are not depicted on the landscape plan. No root barrier details are shown near transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows tree locations but does not indicate which are within 20 feet of underground electric equipment (transformers). Sheet 37 shows general tree protection standards but not specific root barriers for trees near the four transformer pads.","reasoning":"Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment require root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment). Without transformer pad locations on the landscape plan and without root barrier specifications tied to specific transformer locations, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpster or trash enclosure locations are shown on the site plan adjacent to transformer pads. Without explicit depiction of dumpster locations relative to transformer pads, the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 includes a 'Trash Collection Notes' block referencing curbside unattended container restrictions and enforcement signage, but does not show specific dumpster locations. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but no dumpster labels or symbols.","reasoning":"While trash collection is addressed in general notes, specific dumpster locations relative to transformer pads are not identified on the plans. The clearance requirement cannot be verified without showing dumpster locations.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No bike racks are shown on the site plan. Sheet 9 indicates 41 bicycle parking spaces provided (39 long-term, 2 short-term), but no bike rack locations are depicted relative to transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 includes a 'Parking Data' block showing 41 bicycle parking spaces, but the site plan does not visually locate bike racks adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"While bicycle parking is required and provided, specific bike rack locations are not shown relative to transformer pads. This item is not verifiable as 'applicable' without seeing bike racks near transformers.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light poles are not specifically located near transformer pads on the site plan. The photometric plan is not included in the submitted documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 does not show light pole locations in proximity to the transformer pad locations shown on Sheet 21. No photometric plan is provided.","reasoning":"Without light pole locations shown near transformer pads, this requirement is not applicable. If light poles are shown in later submittals near transformers, this item would require evaluation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Areas adjacent to fire lanes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire lanes are shown on Sheet 10 (looping through the site). Transformer Pad 1 (northwest) is located adjacent to the main entrance driveway which serves as a fire lane. Visual analysis suggests the pad is approximately 2-5 feet from the fire lane edge, which would violate the 15-foot minimum clearance if the standard applies. However, no explicit 15-foot dimension is labeled on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 labels fire lanes throughout the site. Sheet 21 shows TP1 positioned immediately adjacent to the curved entrance driveway that is part of the fire lane system. Visual measurement using the 1\"=20' scale suggests clearance of 2-5 feet.","reasoning":"The 15-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from the plans because no specific clearance dimension is labeled. However, the visual positioning of TP1 near the fire lane entrance appears potentially problematic if the 15-foot requirement applies to all fire lane locations.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Four transformer pads are proposed. No specific distances between individual pads are dimensioned on the plans, but the pads are located in geographically separated areas of the site (northwest, west-central, east-central, south-central), with no two pads appearing to be in close proximity (all appear > 5 feet apart based on visual analysis).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads in different geographic locations across the site. None appear to be within 5 feet of each other.","reasoning":"While clearance dimensions are not labeled, the spatial separation shown on the plan suggests this requirement is likely met. The pads are distributed across the site with adequate spacing between them.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines (W) are shown on Sheet 21 near all transformer pads, and on Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan). However, no specific horizontal clearance dimensions are labeled between pad edges and water line locations. Measurement tool would be appropriate for verification if visual dimensions are insufficient.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows water lines (dashed lines labeled 'W') running through the site in proximity to transformer pads. For example, TP3 has a water line running approximately 5-10 feet away. No dimension lines quantify these distances.","reasoning":"The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified from the plans without dimensioned measurements or engineer's certification of clearances. The visual proximity of water lines to some pads (particularly TP3) is concerning but cannot be confirmed without precise measurements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines (WW) are shown on Sheet 21 near transformer pad locations, particularly TP3 which has a WW line running approximately 5-10 feet away on the west side. However, no specific horizontal clearance dimensions are labeled.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows wastewater lines (solid lines labeled 'WW') in proximity to transformer pads. TP3 shows WW line running very close (approximately 5-10 feet east).","reasoning":"The minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be verified without dimensioned measurements. The apparent close proximity of wastewater lines to some pads, particularly TP3, raises concerns about compliance, but cannot be confirmed without precise measurements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 3 (east-central location between Buildings 4 and 5)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows a storm drain line (SD) running directly through the corridor between Buildings 4 and 5 where Transformer Pad 3 is located. Vision analysis indicates the storm drain line passes extremely close to, or potentially directly underneath, the transformer pad symbol (clearance visually estimated at < 5 feet). No separation dimensions are shown. No profile view is provided demonstrating clearance. This represents a clear violation of the minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 clearly shows a solid line labeled 'SD' (storm drain) running north-south directly through the space between Buildings 4 and 5. The transformer pad symbol is positioned in this same corridor, with the storm drain line passing within less than 5 feet of the pad based on visual scale analysis.","reasoning":"The UCM § 2.9.1.B.2 minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines is not met based on the shown proximity. The storm drain line appears to run dangerously close to or directly adjacent to TP3, violating the clearance requirement. No documentation of approved alternative clearance is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service infrastructure is shown on the utility plans. Gas lines are not depicted on Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) or Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan). No gas service is proposed for this site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 Utility Tap Plan legend includes symbols for water (W), wastewater (WW), storm drain (SD), and reclaimed water (RW), but does not include gas. No gas lines are shown on either Sheet 19 or Sheet 21.","reasoning":"Gas service is not present on the site, so this requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple underground utilities are shown near transformer pads (electric lines, water lines, wastewater lines, storm drain lines), but no specific separation dimensions (horizontal or vertical) are labeled on any plan or profile sheet. The minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from other underground utilities cannot be verified without profile views or dimensioned separation callouts.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows multiple utility lines running throughout the site in proximity to transformer pads (blue lines for electric, dashed lines for water, solid lines for wastewater and storm drain). No profiles or dimension lines show vertical separation between utilities.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies both horizontal and vertical clearances of 12 inches. Without profile views showing vertical separation and without horizontal dimensions labeled on the plan view, compliance cannot be verified. Profile sheets are not provided in the submittal.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plans show utilities routed near transformer pads and buildings located in the immediate vicinity of transformer locations. However, no cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical relationships between transformer pads and utility lines running underneath or above them. The requirement prohibits transformers or AE facilities from being located over/under other utility lines, or customer buildings/structures from being placed over AE underground facilities. Without profile or cross-section views, this cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows plan-view layout of transformers and utilities. Sheet 9 shows building footprints. No profile or cross-section drawings are provided that would show vertical positioning of utilities relative to transformers or buildings.","reasoning":"This requirement addresses three-dimensional conflicts between transformers, utilities, and structures. Without cross-sections or profiles showing vertical relationships, compliance cannot be verified from the plan view alone.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution lines are shown on the site plans. The utility routing shown on Sheets 9, 19, and 21 is entirely underground or internal to buildings. No overhead electrical conductors are depicted.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9, 19, and 21 show underground utility routing. No overhead lines are labeled or depicted on any site plan sheet. The utility system is designed as underground distribution.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when overhead distribution lines are present. Since none are shown on the plans, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are shown on the site plans. All electrical distribution is shown as underground routing. The 15-foot radius clearance requirement applies only when overhead conductors are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows only underground electric lines (blue dashed lines labeled 'E') running from entry point to transformers and meters. No overhead distribution conductors are depicted.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to overhead distribution facilities. Since the site has underground distribution only, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All four transformer pads are located in open external areas or narrow courtyards between buildings—not within niches, vaults, or fully enclosed building footprints. Niche configurations are specialized installations where AE equipment is accessible from outside but located within the customer's building footprint. This project does not propose niche service.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows all four transformer pads in external locations: TP1 in landscape island, TP2 beside sidewalk, TP3 in building courtyard, TP4 in internal courtyard. None are within building footprints or enclosed niches.","reasoning":"Niche service is a specialized configuration with specific vertical clearance requirements (35 feet). Since no niches are proposed, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations are proposed for this project. All transformer pads are located in external areas, not within building footprints.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows all transformers in external locations, not within building structures.","reasoning":"Niche service requirements apply only when equipment is located within the building footprint and accessible from outside. Since no niche installations are proposed, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided on the plan set showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows topographic contours indicating varying grades across the site, which implies potential overhead structures or grade changes that could affect vertical clearances to transformer access areas. Without cross-sections demonstrating vertical clearance compliance, this requirement is not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plan set (Sheets 1-39) does not include vertical cross-section drawings at transformer pad locations showing overhead obstructions, grade changes, or vertical clearances. Sheet 11 shows contour lines with elevation changes across the site.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 and AE Design practice require cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances when overhead structures or significant grade variations exist above or adjacent to transformer locations. The absence of these required drawings constitutes non-compliance with documentation requirements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations (if oil-filled equipment is used)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The requirement applies specifically to oil-filled equipment—liquid flow must be directed away from buildings. Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan. General grading analysis on Sheet 11 suggests drainage slopes direct flow away from buildings in the areas where transformers are located, but specific confirmation of transformer type and pad-level grading is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 does not specify whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type. Sheet 11 shows general site drainage patterns with contours indicating flow generally away from building structures. However, no specific pad-level grading or transformer type designation is provided.","reasoning":"Without transformer type specifications and without pad-level grading details (rather than general site contours), compliance with the oil-filled equipment drainage requirement cannot be verified. This requirement does not apply if transformers are dry-type.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All four transformer pads are located entirely on private property within the site boundary. Sheet 2 (Plat) shows clear property boundaries for Lot 1. Sheets 9 and 21 show transformer pad locations interior to or near the property boundary but not within public right-of-way. No transformer pads straddle property lines or are located in Valley View Road right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 2 shows the plat boundary of Lot 1. Sheets 9 and 21 show transformer pad locations well within the interior or near-boundary areas of the property. The western boundary is marked as Valley View Road right-of-way, and no transformer pads are located beyond this boundary.","reasoning":"Visual analysis confirms all transformer pads are positioned on private property, not in public right-of-way or straddling property lines. This requirement is met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 2 (Plat) depicts multiple easements across the property: 15' P.U.E., 5' P.U.E., 5' Electric Easement, 25' Drainage Easement, and 10' Water/Wastewater Easement. The facts.md document also identifies two critical undepicted easements: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 acres, NE interior, no-build zone) and City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 acres, NE corner). Transformer Pad 3, located between Buildings 4 and 5 in the north-central area of the site, is positioned in an area that may conflict with the City of Austin Drainage Easement or other utility easements. No documentation shows that transformer pads have received Austin Energy Design written approval to be located within or near these easements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 2 shows multiple easements: 15' P.U.E., 5' P.U.E., 5' Electric Easement, 25' Drainage Easement, 10' Water/Wastewater Easement. Facts.md identifies additional undepicted easements. Transformer Pad 3 is located in the north-central area where easements are concentrated. No approval documentation is provided for placement in/near easements.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits transformer placement in drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, or electrical easements under overhead lines without Austin Energy Design written approval. No such approval is documented in the project files. TP3's location relative to the various easements shown on Sheet 2 raises concerns about compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements are depicted on any sheet of the site plan. Sheets 9 and 21 show transformer pad locations but with no rectangular dashed lines or labels indicating dedicated transformer easement areas around the pads. The requirement calls for transformer easements of width determined by Austin Energy Design for accessibility. Without these easements shown on the plans, the requirement is not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 21 show transformer pad locations as simple square symbols with no associated rectangular dashed lines indicating easement boundaries. No easement width dimensions or AE Design specifications are noted.","reasoning":"The UCM § 1.10.3 requirement calls for transformer easements to be shown on the plans with dimensions determined by AE Design. The complete absence of these easements from the submitted plans constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows electrical lines routing from transformer pads to meters on individual buildings. All routing appears to stay within the site boundary on private property based on visual analysis. However, no explicit annotation or certification states that electrical routing from transformers to meters is 100% on private property. Without specific documentation or notation confirming this, compliance cannot be fully verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows blue dashed lines representing underground electric lines connecting transformers to pull boxes and meters. These lines appear to remain within the property interior based on visual positioning relative to property boundary lines shown on Sheets 2 and 9.","reasoning":"While visual analysis suggests electrical routing is on private property, without explicit engineering certification or annotation confirming 100% private property routing, the requirement cannot be verified from the submitted documents alone.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads labeled as 'Electrical Transformer Pad' but provides NO dimensions specifying pad size (length × width × depth). The requirement mandates that transformer pad dimensions match Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets for the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase). No pad dimensions are provided on the plans, and no reference to Austin Energy Design detail sheets or service type specifications is documented. This is a critical omission.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads as unlabeled square/rectangular symbols with no dimension callouts. No reference numbers link to AE Design detail sheets. No service type (single-phase vs. three-phase) is indicated.","reasoning":"The requirement explicitly calls for transformer pad dimensions to be specified on the plans and to match AE Design-approved details for the designated service type. The complete absence of dimensions and AE Design references constitutes non-compliance with this fundamental requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 1 (northwest, at main entrance)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 1 is located in the northwest area of the site, immediately adjacent to the main entrance driveway (which provides access to parking and vehicle circulation). Visual analysis using the 1\"=20' scale indicates the pad is positioned approximately 2-5 feet from the driveway curb edge. The requirement mandates that equipment pads installed within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes must have 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts (bollards) per AE Design equipment pad details. Bollards ARE shown on the site plan at other locations (east side, near Buildings 4-5 and 7), but NO bollards are shown around Transformer Pad 1 despite its proximity to the main vehicle entrance/circulation driveway within the 4-foot threshold.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows TP1 positioned 2-5 feet from the curved main entrance driveway curb. Sheet 9 shows bollards labeled '(Typ.)' at two other locations on the east side of the site, but no bollards are indicated near TP1.","reasoning":"The pad's location within 4 feet of an active vehicle circulation driveway requires bollard protection. The absence of bollards at this location while bollards are provided at other site locations (Sheets 9 and 21) indicates non-compliance with this requirement. Bollards must be shown on the plans per AE Design equipment pad details.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution facilities are shown on the site plans. All electrical distribution is designed as underground. The requirement prohibits customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, billboards, chimneys, antennas, tanks) from being installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Since no overhead distribution is present, this item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9, 19, and 21 show underground electrical distribution only. No overhead lines are depicted. Building locations are interior to the property.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when overhead distribution facilities are present. Since the site has underground distribution only, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"db3364e9-4955-4fce-b840-6e31084f272d"}
