{"level":30,"time":1778247059830,"pid":122,"hostname":"bd047d16-36d","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W7YYK9G292C2WYKQVEG5W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014ugC4gZpmd4KurKwvbAfPd","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"comments":[{"headline":"Missing building elevations and clearance surveys","summary":"No building elevation sheets, section/plan dimension exhibits, or registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey data are provided. Required documentation prevents verification of 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearance compliance for overhead electric facilities throughout the site.","sheets":[9,21],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"No building elevation sheets showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are included in the site plan package. Building elevation sheets are required per UCM § 1.10.3 but are absent.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on or adjacent to site. No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are included in the site plan package. Required building elevation sheets showing conductor heights and clearances to building features are missing."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations are not included in the submitted site plan set."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan set showing surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors. Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor data and clearance dimension annotations are required per UCM § 1.10.3 to demonstrate that required clearances are met."}]},{"text":"Section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from the outermost electric conductor to building edges and projections are not provided. Required clearance verification exhibits are missing from the site plan package.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings and building projections are not provided. Required clearance verification exhibits are missing from the site plan package."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No section or plan view exhibits provided showing dimension lines from outer conductor to building edges."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Plans do not include section and plan view exhibits showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings, building projections, retaining walls, or other site features. Clearance verification requires dimension lines extending from the outside conductor to all structures and site improvements."}]},{"text":"No registered surveyor's mid-span clearance survey data is provided documenting overhead conductor elevations and pole locations. When vertical clearance appears marginal, surveyor data is required but not submitted.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Proposed driveway finished surface elevations are shown on the grading plan. Overhead electric lines exist on site boundaries with spot elevations shown on electrical plan. However, no registered surveyor's mid-span clearance survey data is provided, and no profile sections show vertical clearances from overhead line lowest point to driveway surfaces. When vertical clearance appears marginal or insufficient, surveyor data is required but not submitted."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey provided showing pole locations and conductor elevations for clearance verification."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Driveway proposed grades (Sheet 11: 679.75-688.40 feet) are shown in proximity to overhead electric facilities. The vertical clearance from these grades to the overhead conductors is not documented. A registered surveyor's mid-span clearance survey is required to verify that minimum clearance requirements (16-18 feet for driveways per UCM § 1.10.6.2) are satisfied, but no such survey data is provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Buildings and structures lack overhead line clearance verification","summary":"Proposed buildings and elevated structures are positioned in proximity to overhead electric lines without documented clearance verification. No elevations or dimensions demonstrate compliance with required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from the outside conductor.","sheets":[9,21,11],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Electrical utility coordination may be required if structures must be relocated or overhead electric line repositioned.","attn":"Buildings 6, 7, 8 specifically noted near southern OHE line; all buildings near western OHE line on Valley View Road ROW. Confirm whether pole relocation is proposed or structures must be repositioned.","details":[{"text":"Buildings are shown in plan view relative to overhead electric lines but no surveyed building elevations are provided to verify required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor. Clearance cannot be verified without elevation views dimensioned from the conductor.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on western and southern site boundaries; buildings are set back from these lines on plan view, but no surveyed building elevations provided showing conductor heights or clearance dimensions. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance without elevation views dimensioned from the outside conductor."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Buildings 6, 7, and 8 are shown in proximity to the southern OHE line without any documented clearance dimensions from the outside conductor. No clearance verification provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings are shown in plan view relative to overhead electric lines on Sheet 9, but no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided to verify the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor."}]},{"text":"Buildings maintain apparent setbacks from property lines on plan, but no surveyed elevations or clearance dimensions verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances as permanent requirements. Buildings 7 and 8 adjacent to southern OHE; all buildings near western OHE line.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist in right-of-way adjacent to site (western and southern boundaries); buildings maintain apparent setbacks from property lines, but no surveyed elevations or clearance dimensions verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances as permanent requirements per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings located near OHE lines on south and east boundaries but no clearance dimensions from conductor shown on site plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist along the western property line (Valley View Road) and southern property line, with poles and conductors visible on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4). Buildings 7 and 8 are located adjacent to the southern OHE line boundary, and the western driveway crosses underneath the western OHE line. No surveyed elevations and clearance dimensions are provided to demonstrate that buildings maintain the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from the outside conductors."}]},{"text":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) are not shown in elevation view with dimensions to overhead conductors. Building elevation and section views required to verify clearances are not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) are shown in elevation view with dimensions to overhead electric conductors. Building elevation and section views required to verify clearances are not provided in the site plan package."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed conductor elevations and clearances from building projections (overhangs, balconies, canopies) to overhead conductors."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets showing projected building elements (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) relative to overhead conductors are provided to verify clearances. Applicant must provide surveyed building elevations with conductor locations."}]},{"text":"Elevated walkways and pedestrian platforms are shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions from OHE lines are provided. No elevation or section drawings verify required 15-foot radial clearance.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Elevated walkways and pedestrian platforms are shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions from OHE lines are provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 9 shows the overall site layout with various walkways and potential elevated structures, but no elevation or section drawings are provided to verify that stairs, elevated walkways, or platforms maintain the required 15-foot radial clearance from overhead electric distribution facilities."}]},{"text":"Emergency access structures (elevated platforms or bridges) are not explicitly identified on the site plan. If present, section views showing required clearances from overhead conductors are not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.16","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Emergency access structures not clearly identified on plans. No elevation sections provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No emergency access bridges or elevated platforms are explicitly identified on the site plan. If such structures exist as part of the site design, section views showing the required clearances from overhead conductors are not provided."}]},{"text":"Vehicle parking areas are shown on site plan but site plan does not explicitly identify vehicle display pads or document vertical clearance dimensions for any parking areas in proximity to OHE.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.19","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Parking locations shown but no vertical clearance from OHE lines documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Vehicle parking areas are shown on the site plan (both surface and garage parking), but the site plan does not explicitly identify any vehicle display pads or indicate which parking areas (if any) are positioned beneath overhead electric lines. Vertical clearance dimensions are not provided for any parking areas in proximity to OHE."}]}]},{"headline":"Driveway clearances and crossing specifications missing","summary":"Driveways cross existing overhead electric lines without documented vertical clearance verification, utility pole relocation coordination, or OHE crossing angle specifications. Required 16-18 foot clearance for parking-area driveways and 30-foot clearance for transmission lines are unverified.","sheets":[9,11,4],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Utility coordination required for pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting configuration; Austin Energy input needed for crossing specifications.","attn":"Western driveway entrance crosses beneath OHE line at multiple locations. Confirm whether existing poles will be relocated, converted to self-supporting, or if driveway alignment will be adjusted.","details":[{"text":"Driveways are proposed with finished grade spot elevations 679.75 to 688.40 feet at locations crossing existing OHE, but no vertical clearance dimensions verify required 16-18 foot minimum clearance. Mid-span clearance survey data not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Internal driveways and parking areas shown on site plan have finished floor elevations (FFEs) on grading plan, but no profile sections or cross-sections showing vertical clearance from lowest point of overhead electric lines to driveway/parking surfaces are provided. Mid-span clearance verification by registered surveyor is not included."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Driveway shown crossing southern OHE line with no vertical clearance dimensions or surveyed mid-span conductor elevation data provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Driveways are proposed with entrances on the western property boundary that cross directly beneath the existing overhead electric line (OHE). Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows finished grade spot elevations ranging from 679.75 to 688.40 feet at the driveway locations, but provides no vertical clearance dimensions verifying the required minimum 16-foot clearance (for parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot clearance (for areas with truck traffic). Mid-span clearance survey data is not provided."}]},{"text":"Grading plan does not show 30-foot vertical clearance dimensions from transmission lines to final grade elevations for driveways and roads in transmission easement or beneath transmission lines.","citation":"UCM § 1.14.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.20","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Grading plan does not show 30-foot vertical clearance dimensions from transmission lines to final grade."}]},{"text":"Existing electric poles are shown on existing conditions survey at proposed western driveway entrance, but site plan does not provide explicit relocation notes, revised pole locations, or minimum 30-foot setback dimension from driveway edge to existing poles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveway crosses OHE line but utility pole locations not explicitly shown on site plan. Pole relocation notes not provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) at and near the proposed western driveway entrance. The site plan (Sheet 9) does not provide explicit relocation notes, revised pole locations, or a minimum 30-foot setback dimension from the driveway edge to existing poles."}]},{"text":"Existing overhead electric lines cross proposed driveways on western property boundary, but no notation indicates whether crossings are oriented at required 90-degree angle to driveway centerline.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.32","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"OHE line crossing angle at driveway not specified on plans."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing overhead electric lines cross proposed driveways on the western property boundary (Sheet 9), but no notation indicates whether these crossings are oriented at the required 90-degree angle to the driveway centerline."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan shows underground infrastructure only. Existing overhead lines do not indicate voltage levels or wire types. Section views or detailed crossing information showing whether secondary overhead lines cross over primary lines are not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.33","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No section views or crossing details showing relationship between secondary and primary overhead lines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric infrastructure only. Existing overhead lines (Sheet 9) do not indicate voltage levels or wire types. Without section views or detailed crossing information, it cannot be determined whether secondary overhead lines (if present) cross over primary lines in violation of Reviewer Convention standards."}]}]},{"headline":"Retaining walls and fences lack overhead line clearance documentation","summary":"Retaining walls and fences are proposed along site boundaries in proximity to overhead electric lines without documented clearance dimensions or section views. Required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor and 10-foot minimum pole distance are unverified.","sheets":[9,11,31,38,39],"applicableArea":"Site Perimeter","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"Southern boundary retaining walls run parallel to and in close proximity to OHE line. Confirm wall construction depth and whether walls extend into easement. Southern and eastern property boundaries have proposed fencing.","details":[{"text":"Concrete retaining walls proposed along southern property boundary parallel to and in proximity to existing OHE line. Sheet 11 shows top-of-wall elevations (TW 682.23-683.84 feet) but no vertical clearance dimensions from outside conductor to wall are documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are shown on the grading plan (Sheet 11) and wall detail sheets (Sheets 38-39), and overhead electric lines exist on site boundaries. However, no clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outermost electric line to the wall face are provided. Clearance verification requires dimension lines originating at conductor location."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining walls are shown directly over or parallel to the southern OHE line. No clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the wall face provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Concrete retaining walls are proposed along the southern boundary of the property parallel to and in proximity to the existing overhead electric line (OHE). Sheet 11 shows the retaining wall with top-of-wall elevations (TW ranging from 682.23 to 683.84 feet), but no vertical clearance dimensions from the outermost electric line conductor to the wall are provided. Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) shows no overhead utilities at all."}]},{"text":"Retaining wall section exhibits (Sheet 38) do not show clearance dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost wall edge. Wall Plan section omits overhead electric lines, preventing clearance verification.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.17","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining wall section views are provided on Sheets 38-39, but clearance dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall face are not shown. Section exhibits lack the required clearance verification dimensions."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No section views provided showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to retaining wall faces."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining wall section exhibits (Sheet 38) do not show clearance dimension annotations from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of the walls. The Wall Plan section shows the wall details but completely omits representation of overhead electric lines, preventing clearance verification."}]},{"text":"Fences are shown on site plan and landscape plan (perimeter fencing) along southern and eastern property boundaries in proximity to OHE, but no clearance dimensions demonstrate 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor to fence face.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.9","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan and landscape plan (perimeter fencing with 'X' symbols), but clearance dimensions from the outside conductor of overhead electric facilities to the fence face are not provided. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Wooden privacy fence is shown near OHE line on landscape plan but no clearance dimensions provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9 and Sheet 31) along the southern and eastern property boundaries in proximity to existing overhead electric lines. However, no clearance dimensions are provided demonstrating that fences maintain the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of overhead electric facilities."}]},{"text":"Fence posts are shown on site plan and landscape plan near utility poles on western and southern boundaries, but dimension annotations showing 10-foot minimum horizontal clearance from fence posts to electric poles are not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fence posts are shown on site plan and landscape plan, and utility poles (OHE) exist on western and southern boundaries, but dimension annotations showing 10-foot minimum horizontal clearance from fence posts to electric poles are not provided. Cannot verify requirement from available plan documentation."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fence posts shown in proximity to OHE but utility pole locations not explicitly marked and no 10-foot clearance dimensions provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences are proposed along the southern property boundary where existing utility poles are located (per the existing conditions survey). Clearance dimensions showing minimum 10-foot horizontal distance from fence posts to the electric poles are not provided."}]},{"text":"Transmission line easement referenced on site plan but no proposed fencing beneath transmission lines is shown. Fence material specifications and grounding details required per UCM § 1.14.0 are not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.14.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.12","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transmission line easement referenced on site plan but no proposed fencing beneath transmission lines shown. Fence material specifications and grounding details not provided."}]},{"text":"No vehicle barrier posts or fencing are explicitly labeled as such on site plan. If any fencing in proximity to OHE lines functions as vehicle barriers, no clearance verification exhibits show required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outermost electric line.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.13","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No vehicle barrier posts or fencing are explicitly labeled as such on the site plan. However, if any fencing in proximity to the OHE lines is intended to function as vehicle barriers, no clearance verification exhibits are provided showing the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from the outermost electric line."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformers, meters, and service equipment lack clearance documentation","summary":"Proposed electrical transformers, meters, and service masts lack documented clearance verification from overhead electric lines and conductor type identification. Required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance, 15-foot radial clearance, and meter working space are unverified.","sheets":[21,19,20],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy coordination needed for transformer clearance review and conductor identification.","attn":"Three transformer pads shown on electrical plan. Confirm locations and whether pad-mounted units require relocation due to clearance violations. Meter access requirements must be verified with utility provider.","details":[{"text":"Three proposed electrical transformer pads shown on site plan in proximity to buildings. No clearance dimensions or radial clearance verification documented demonstrating 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors maintained. Conductor type not labeled on plans.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines shown on site boundaries but conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) not labeled on plans. Without conductor type identification and conductor locations, the 15-foot radial clearance requirement for overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad shown on site but no clearance dimensions from OHE lines provided. Conductor voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission) not confirmed on plans."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Three proposed electrical transformer pads are shown on the site plan in proximity to the buildings. However, no clearance dimensions or radial clearance verification are provided demonstrating that the 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors is maintained."}]},{"text":"Electrical meters shown on Sheet 21 mounted to building exterior walls, but enlarged meter area detail plans are not provided. No site plan detail shows meter installation with required 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances, nor are potential obstructions identified.","citation":"UCM § 1.9.3.1","sourceId":"1:EL-1.38","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows proposed meter locations with callout annotations near buildings, but detailed meter clearance area drawings are not provided. Cannot verify from plan view whether meters maintain required working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) and are not obstructed by site features, structures, or landscaping."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Meter locations shown on electrical plan but detailed obstruction analysis and access clearance verification not provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical meters are shown on Sheet 21 as being mounted to building exterior walls, but enlarged meter area detail plans are not provided. No site plan detail shows meter installation locations with 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances per UCM § 1.10.9, nor are potential obstructions (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, building projections) identified relative to meter access requirements."}]},{"text":"Proposed pad-mounted electrical transformers shown on electrical design plan but no section views showing vertical clearance dimensions from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment are provided. 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.43","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformers are shown as proposed on the electrical design plan (pad-mounted units located on ground near buildings), and overhead electric lines exist on site boundaries. However, no section views showing vertical clearance dimensions from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment are provided. Cannot verify 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad shown on electrical plan but no section view showing vertical clearance from overhead lines to top of equipment provided."}]},{"text":"Water meter locations shown on utility plan sheets but clearance dimensions from overhead electric service drop conductors to water meter locations are not provided. 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3; UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.28","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations are shown on utility tap plan sheets (19-20) and electrical plan (21), but clearance dimension annotations from overhead electric service drop conductors to water meter locations are not provided. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance without dimension documentation."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations shown on utility plan but clearance from overhead electric service drops not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations are not clearly identified on the site plan or utility plan. If water meters are proposed to be installed near existing overhead electric service drops, no clearance dimensions verify the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor."}]},{"text":"No building elevation sheets provided showing service-mast through-roof installation details or clearance dimensions. Required 3-foot clearance above roof or 18-inch clearance for masts within 4 feet of roof edge cannot be verified per UCM § 1.10.6.2.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.47","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing service-mast installations and roof clearance dimensions."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets are provided showing service-mast through-roof installation details or clearance dimensions from the roof line. Without elevation documentation, the required 3-foot clearance above roof or 18-inch clearance for masts within 4 feet of roof edge cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Structures in utility easements lack clearance verification","summary":"Buildings, driveways, and retaining walls are positioned within electric utility easements or adjacent property-line areas without documented clearance from outside conductors or utility access space. 5-foot easements along boundaries cannot accommodate customer facilities.","sheets":[2,9,4,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy input required to confirm easement boundaries, permissions, and whether structures can be relocated or easement modified.","attn":"Existing 5-foot electric easements shown along property boundaries. Confirm whether proposed site features (buildings, walls, driveways) actually encroach into easement, or if there is adequate clearance from easement edge.","details":[{"text":"Existing conditions survey shows 5-foot electric easements along property boundaries and overhead distribution facilities through/adjacent to property. Proposed site features on Sheet 9 (buildings, driveways, retaining walls) located in proximity to easements and OHE lines. No dimension exhibits verify minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor nor confirm features do not violate absolute prohibition on customer facilities under/over distribution lines.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 2 (Plat) and Sheet 21 show electric easements on site boundaries and interior. Buildings and site features are located throughout the site, including within and adjacent to easement areas. However, no clearance dimensions verify that customer facilities within electric easements maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductors. Furthermore, the absolute prohibition on installing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy distribution facilities cannot be verified without complete easement delineation on all relevant sheets."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Driveway and retaining walls shown directly over/crossing OHE line, violating absolute prohibition on customer facilities under/over distribution lines. No clearance documentation provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows 5-foot electric easements along property boundaries and overhead electric lines running through/adjacent to the property. The proposed site features (buildings, driveways, retaining walls) shown on Sheet 9 are located in proximity to these easements and overhead lines. However, no dimension exhibits verify that items within the electric easements or beneath overhead distribution lines maintain the minimum 7.5-foot clearance from the outside conductor. The absolute prohibition against installing customer facilities under or over distribution lines cannot be verified as being met."}]},{"text":"Buildings shown on site plan are setback from property lines, but exact distances from permanent structure foundations to property lines are not clearly dimensioned. Without precise setback dimensions and clear delineation of utility facility locations in adjacent ROW, cannot verify adequate clearance space exists for future utility work.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.30","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings shown on site plan are setback from property lines, but exact distances from permanent structure foundations to property lines are not clearly dimensioned. Without precise setback dimensions and without clear delineation of where electric facilities are located in adjacent ROW or neighboring properties, cannot verify that adequate clearance space exists for future utility work."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building setbacks from property line not explicitly dimensioned on site plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"While buildings are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9), no building foundation detail drawings are provided, and no explicit documentation shows whether foundations are located within 5 feet of the property line where electric facilities in the right-of-way or adjacent property require clearance space."}]},{"text":"Down guy anchor locations from distribution poles not explicitly shown or dimensioned on site plan or easement exhibits. No easement exhibit showing 10-foot width extending 5 feet past the anchor ground entry point is provided on submitted site plan.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.42","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy anchors from distribution poles (if they exist on site) are not explicitly shown or dimensioned on the site plan or easement exhibit (Plat, Sheet 2). Cannot verify whether dedicated easements for down guy anchors (10-foot width, 5-foot minimum extension past anchor ground entry) are provided or properly dimensioned."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy anchor locations and associated easement boundaries not shown on site plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) identifies down guy locations but does not clearly show the specific anchor point locations or provide easement boundaries. No easement exhibit showing 10-foot width extending 5 feet past the anchor ground entry point is provided on the submitted site plan."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan shows underground electric infrastructure but does not clearly indicate whether new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion. If poles are proposed, their horizontal spacing relative to existing poles is not documented with required 20-foot minimum dimension.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.35","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric infrastructure but does not clearly indicate whether new power poles are proposed for the underground service conversion. If new poles are proposed, their horizontal spacing relative to existing poles is not documented with the required 20-foot minimum dimension."}]}]},{"headline":"Site improvements and utilities lack overhead line clearance documentation","summary":"Proposed sidewalks, trash enclosures, water lines, streetlight poles, and detected down guy wires lack documented clearance from overhead electric lines and poles. Required clearance dimensions are missing for multiple site improvements.","sheets":[9,4,19,21,31],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Public works coordination may be needed for sidewalk alignment and streetlight placement if relocation is required.","attn":"Down guy wire identified at northwestern utility pole. Confirm whether down guy anchor point and cable extent conflict with proposed driveway and pedestrian pathways. Water line routing shown on Sheets 19-21 but specific clearance from poles not documented.","details":[{"text":"Existing power poles shown on existing conditions survey along Valley View Road at western property boundary. Sheet 9 shows sidewalks along property frontage, but no clarification provided regarding whether sidewalks at property corners/ends are cleared from existing poles or if poles require relocation.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Proposed sidewalks are shown along the Valley View Road frontage on site plan and landscape plan. Existing power poles are indicated on the electrical plan along this boundary. However, dimension annotations showing whether sidewalk improvements clear the power poles at property ends are not provided. Cannot verify clearance from available documentation."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalk improvements shown but existing power pole locations not clearly marked at property line ends."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing power poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) along Valley View Road at the western property boundary. Sheet 9 shows sidewalks along the property frontage, but no clarification is provided regarding whether sidewalks at the property corners/ends are cleared from the existing poles or if poles require relocation."}]},{"text":"Trash collection areas referenced in site plan notes but specific trash enclosure and receptacle locations not clearly identified in plan view. If trash facilities positioned beneath OHE lines, clearance verification considering raised height during bin service is not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.26","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash collection requirements are noted on Sheet 9, specifying that containers shall not be left at curbside unattended, but specific trash enclosure locations and relationship to overhead electric lines are not detailed on the site plan. Cannot verify whether trash enclosures are placed under overhead lines or that clearance requirements are met."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash enclosure locations integrated in buildings but clearance from OHE lines not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash collection areas are referenced in the site plan notes (Sheet 9) but specific trash enclosure and receptacle locations are not clearly identified in plan view. If trash facilities are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, clearance verification considering the raised height during bin service is not provided."}]},{"text":"Water line routing shown on utility sheets but clearance dimensions from water lines to existing overhead distribution poles and conductors are not provided on the plans.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.29","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Water line routing is shown on utility tap plan sheets. Overhead distribution poles and lines are shown on electrical plan. However, clearance dimensions from water line locations to overhead distribution poles and conductors are not annotated on the plans. Clearance verification cannot be completed."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water lines shown near OHE poles but clearance dimensions not provided on utility plans."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Water line routing is shown on utility sheets (Sheet 19, Sheet 21) but clearance dimensions from water lines to existing overhead distribution poles and conductors are not provided on the plans."}]},{"text":"Existing streetlight or utility light poles may be present along property frontage. Sheet 9 shows building locations but does not provide clearance dimensions from buildings to existing streetlight poles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.39","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows existing light poles in the legend and may show some on the drawing, and proposed buildings are shown on Site Plan (Sheet 9). However, specific clearance dimensions from proposed building locations to existing streetlight poles are not dimensioned on the plans. Cannot verify clearances from available documentation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing streetlight or utility light poles may be present along the property frontage (Sheet 4). Sheet 9 shows building locations but does not provide clearance dimensions from buildings to existing streetlight poles."}]},{"text":"Existing conditions survey identifies down guy wire from utility pole at northwestern property area. Site plan shows main driveway entrance crossing directly beneath pole location where down guy is located. Down guy anchor point and cable extent not clearly depicted relative to proposed driveway and pedestrian pathways. No note indicates conflict resolution or pole conversion.","citation":"UCM § 1.17.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.40","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy wires are utility infrastructure that is frequently omitted from site plans. Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole symbols on boundaries but does not explicitly identify guy wire locations. Site plan and electrical design plan show pole symbols but do not detail guy wire or guy anchor locations. Cannot verify whether down guy wires conflict with proposed accessible paths or driveways, or whether conflict resolution (pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles) is documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy wire locations from existing electric poles not shown or documented on site plan. Potential conflicts with accessible routes not identified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) identifies a down guy wire from a utility pole at the northwestern area of the property. The site plan (Sheet 9) shows the main driveway entrance crossing directly beneath the pole location where the down guy is located. The down guy anchor point and the extent of the down guy cable are not clearly depicted on the site plan relative to the proposed driveway and pedestrian pathways. No note indicates whether the down guy will conflict with accessible routes or if the pole will be converted to self-supporting configuration."}]},{"text":"Sheet 9 shows site lighting but does not clearly identify which elements are proposed streetlight poles. If new streetlight poles are proposed, their locations relative to overhead electric lines are not documented with clearance dimensions.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.24","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Streetlight poles not explicitly detailed relative to OHE line locations. No dimension callouts provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows site lighting but does not clearly identify which lighting elements are proposed streetlight poles. If new streetlight poles are proposed, their locations relative to overhead electric lines are not documented with clearance dimensions."}]}]},{"headline":"Trees and decorative lighting lack utility-compatibility documentation","summary":"Three trees proposed at southern property boundary are shown graphically overlapping overhead electric line with no species identification or utility-compatibility verification. Decorative lighting clearance from overhead lines also undocumented.","sheets":[31,9],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"City Arborist coordination may be needed if non-utility-compatible species must be substituted.","attn":"Three trees visible at southern boundary overlapping OHE line shown on Sheet 31. Confirm species and whether trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F (mature height ≤20 feet). Clearance distances must meet 10-foot distribution / 50-foot transmission minimums per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","details":[{"text":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows three tree symbols with canopy circles at southern boundary overlapping OHE line graphically. Trees not identified by species. No documentation verifies trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F (marked 'UC', mature height ≤20 feet). Clearance distances showing 10-foot minimum lateral distance from distribution conductors not documented per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","citation":"ECM § 2.4.1.D; ECM § 2.4.2.C; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and tree list (Sheet 32) are provided, but tree species proposed near overhead electric lines are not identified or verified against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible tree list. Lateral distances from tree locations to overhead conductors are not dimensioned. Cannot verify that trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution lines are utility-compatible species or that proper setbacks are maintained."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Trees shown on landscape plan directly over OHE line. Tree species not verified against ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list. No lateral distance callouts provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows three tree symbols in the bottom-right corner with canopy circle outlines that graphically overlap the overhead electric line (OHE) line running along the southern boundary. Two trees are labeled 'M' (mitigation trees) and one is labeled 'P' (parking buffer point tree). No tree species are identified on Sheet 31. No documentation shows that these trees are utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F (utility-compatible trees marked 'UC' with mature height ≤20 feet). No clearance distances are documented showing the 10 lateral feet minimum from distribution conductors or 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors required by UCM § 1.10.10.4."}]},{"text":"Landscape and site plans show general lighting elements, but decorative lighting fixture locations and their clearance from overhead electric lines are not clearly documented. If decorative lighting positioned beneath OHE lines, clearance verification exhibits showing required 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearances not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.36","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows trees and vegetation but specific decorative lighting fixture locations and their relationship to overhead electric lines are not detailed. Site plan notes exterior lighting compliance requirements (full cut-off, fully shielded per LDC Subchapter E 2.5) but does not specifically detail all decorative light locations relative to OHE lines. Cannot verify clearances from available documentation."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Decorative lighting required to be full cut-off and shielded per lighting notes, but specific fixture locations and OHE clearances not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape and site plans show general lighting elements, but decorative lighting fixture locations and their clearance from overhead electric lines are not clearly documented. If decorative lighting is positioned beneath overhead lines, clearance verification exhibits with required dimensions (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) are not provided."}]}]},{"headline":"No clearance dimension callouts shown on site plans","summary":"The site plan provides no clearance dimensions at all from overhead electric facilities to site features. When dimensions are absent, measurement origin (outside conductor vs. pole centerline) cannot be verified. Per UCM § 1.10.3, critical measurement must originate from outside conductor.","sheets":[9,21,11],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"This is a foundational documentation gap affecting verification of nearly all other clearance items. All clearance dimension callouts must show measurement origin from the outside/outermost conductor, not from pole centerline.","details":[{"text":"Site plan sheets show no clearance dimension callouts originating from overhead electric conductor locations to any site features (buildings, structures, equipment, driveways, walls, fences). Complete absence of dimensions prevents verification that measurements originate from outside conductor per UCM § 1.10.3 requirement.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Clearance dimensions required by code are not shown on site plan sheets. Where clearance dimensions are lacking, no verification can be performed that they extend from the outside conductor (not pole centerline or pole structure). The requirement that dimensions originate from the outer conductor, not pole center, cannot be verified when dimensions are absent."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No clearance dimensions shown on any plan sheets. Measurement methodology (from outside conductor vs. pole center) cannot be verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"The site plan provides no clearance dimensions at all from any overhead electric facilities to site features. Where dimensions are absent, it is impossible to verify that they are measured from the outside conductor rather than from pole centerline. Per UCM § 1.10.3, the critical measurement point is the outside conductor, not the pole centerline. The plan's complete absence of clearance dimensions means this requirement cannot be evaluated."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing construction contractor notification and staging documentation","summary":"Site plan lacks required 48-hour Austin Energy notification note per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752. Construction staging areas with OSHA 10-foot and 20-foot radial clearance requirements also not documented. Pre-construction coordination missing.","sheets":[1,3,5],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy coordination and contractor safety planning required during pre-construction phase.","attn":"Notification requirement is a legal mandate under Texas state law. Contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before any work begins near high-voltage OHE lines. OSHA clearance requirements during construction (20-foot) differ from permanent clearances.","details":[{"text":"Cover sheet (Sheet 1) and general notes (Sheet 3) do not include required note stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. Required notification language per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is missing.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2; Texas Health & Safety Code § 752.003","sourceId":"1:EL-1.46","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on or adjacent to the site. No note is included on the cover sheet or general notes stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. This required notification note is missing from the plan set."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"The cover sheet (Sheet 1) does not include a note requiring that the owner/contractor notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. While Sheet 3 (General Notes) contains comprehensive electric transmission notes, the specific 48-hour notification requirement is not explicitly stated on either the cover sheet or general notes sheets."}]},{"text":"Construction staging areas and equipment operation zones not clearly identified on erosion control or construction phasing sheets. No plan view shows staging area boundaries with documented 10-foot radial clearance from energized OHE lines. OSHA 20-foot construction-phase clearance requirement not detailed separately.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.45","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Erosion and sedimentation control plan (Sheet 5) may show staging areas, and electrical plan shows overhead lines on site boundaries. However, no site logistics plan or construction phasing plan explicitly identifies construction staging areas, crane swing radius, equipment laydown zones, or work platforms with 10-foot radial clearance verification from overhead lines. Cannot verify construction-phase clearance compliance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones not detailed on site plan. OSHA 10-foot radial clearance requirement not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones may be depicted on erosion control or construction phasing sheets, but no plan view clearly identifies staging area boundaries with documented 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines. OSHA requires 20-foot clearance during construction, distinct from permanent clearances."}]}]}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6adf967-2df8-46b4-89e4-bb1c4cb4236f","uuid":"20d079d8-c1e7-4cc3-969b-191782b6bda4"}
